/* 化学 (Kimia) 内置笔记数据：由 index.html 加载。改了这个文件，记得把 index.html 里 kim.js?v= 的版本号也改一下，浏览器才会重新下载。 */
const PPTS_KIM={"kim|T4-1": [["What Is Chemistry?", "化学是什么？", [["Chemistry is the study of matter: its composition, structure, properties, and the changes it undergoes, together with the energy involved.", "化学研究物质的组成、结构、性质、变化及能量变化"], ["Branches: organic, inorganic, physical, analytical, biochemistry, industrial chemistry, environmental chemistry.", "分支：有机、无机、物理、分析、生物化学、工业化学、环境化学"], ["Importance in daily life: medicines and vaccines, fertilisers and pesticides, food preservation, cleaning agents, fuels, plastics, alloys, glass and ceramics, cosmetics.", "应用：药物、肥料、食物保存、清洁剂、燃料、塑料、合金等"], ["Careers: chemist, pharmacist, chemical engineer, food technologist, forensic scientist, materials scientist, environmental officer.", "职业：化学家、药剂师、化工工程师、食品技师等"], ["Development of chemistry: alchemy (turning metals into gold, searching for the elixir) → experimental science (Boyle, Lavoisier) → modern chemistry (atomic theory, periodic table, nanotechnology, green technology).", "发展：炼金术 → 实验科学 → 现代化学"]], "", "Tip: link a chemical to its use and an example whenever the question asks for the 'importance of chemistry'."], ["SPM Chemistry (4541): Paper Format", "SPM化学(4541)：试卷格式", [["Paper 1 (4541/1): 40 objective questions = 40 marks, 1 hour 15 minutes; answer all.", "试卷1：40道选择题＝40分，1小时15分钟，全答"], ["Paper 2 (4541/2) = 100 marks, 2 hours 30 minutes: Section A — 8 structured questions, 60 marks, answer all; Section B — 2 questions, 20 marks, answer ONE; Section C — 1 question, 20 marks.", "试卷2共100分：A部分8题结构题60分（全答）；B部分2题20分（选1）；C部分1题20分"], ["Paper 3 (4541/3) = 15 marks, practical: about 5 minutes planning session + 40 minutes to answer.", "试卷3：15分，实验：约5分钟准备＋40分钟作答"], ["Content: the KSSM Form 4 and Form 5 syllabus. Questions test remembering, understanding, applying and analysing (Paper 2 also evaluating and creating).", "范围：KSSM中四、中五；考记忆、理解、应用、分析（试卷2也考评价与创造）"]], "", "Tip: this format is used from SPM 2021; confirm with your teacher."], ["How SPM Chemistry Marks Are Given", "SPM化学如何给分", [["Marks follow key points: one correct keyword = 1 mark, one explanation = 1 mark. A 6-mark question needs about 3 keywords + 3 explanations.", "按得分点给分：一个关键词1分，一个解释1分；6分题约需3个关键词＋3个解释"], ["A correct, balanced chemical equation is usually 1 mark: correct formulae AND balanced.", "正确且配平的化学方程式通常1分：化学式正确且配平"], ["Calculations: write the formula, substitute with units, then give the answer with the correct unit; the unit is often a separate mark.", "计算：写公式、代入（带单位）、答案带正确单位；单位常单独占分"], ["In mark schemes, // means another answer of the same meaning is also accepted.", "评分表中 // 表示意思相同的其他答案也接受"], ["Use correct scientific terms (atom, ion, molecule) and label every diagram.", "使用准确术语（原子、离子、分子），图要标注"]], "", "Tip: write more key points than the marks; the examiner picks the correct ones."], ["Common Apparatus and Their Uses", "常用仪器及用途", [["Measuring volume: measuring cylinder (approximate, e.g. ±0.5 cm³); burette (0.05 cm³ accuracy, delivers variable volumes in titration); pipette (fixed volume, e.g. 25.0 cm³, accurate); volumetric flask (prepares a standard solution of exact volume).", "量体积：量筒（粗略）、滴定管（精确可变）、移液管（固定体积）、容量瓶（配标准溶液）"], ["Heating: Bunsen burner, tripod stand, wire gauze, crucible and lid (heating metals/solids strongly), evaporating dish (evaporating solutions), boiling tube, test tube, water bath.", "加热：本生灯、三脚架、石棉网、坩埚、蒸发皿、试管、水浴"], ["Containers and others: beaker, conical flask, round-bottom flask, filter funnel, thistle funnel, delivery tube, gas jar, dropper, glass rod, spatula, test-tube rack, retort stand with clamp.", "容器与其他：烧杯、锥形瓶、圆底烧瓶、漏斗、长颈漏斗、导管、集气瓶、滴管等"], ["Weighing: electronic balance (to 0.01 g). Temperature: thermometer. Time: stopwatch. Gas volume: gas syringe, burette inverted in water.", "称量、测温、计时、量气体的仪器"], ["Choose apparatus by purpose and precision: titration needs a burette and a pipette, not a measuring cylinder.", "按用途和精确度选仪器：滴定要用滴定管和移液管"]], "", "Tip: in 'name the apparatus' questions describe the use together with the name."], ["Heating, Handling and Disposal of Chemicals", "加热与化学品的处理", [["Heating a test tube: slant at about 45°, point the mouth away from people, shake gently, heat the sides first, use a test-tube holder.", "加热试管：约 45° 倾斜，管口避开人，轻摇，用试管夹"], ["Bunsen flame: blue flame (air hole open, complete combustion, hot); yellow flame (air hole closed, incomplete combustion, sooty, luminous). Use the blue flame for heating.", "蓝色火焰（空气孔开，完全燃烧，较热）；黄色火焰（不完全燃烧，有烟灰）"], ["Hazard symbols: toxic, corrosive, flammable, explosive, oxidising, radioactive, harmful/irritant, dangerous to the environment. Read the label and wear goggles, gloves and a lab coat.", "危险标志：有毒、腐蚀、易燃、爆炸、氧化、放射、有害、环境危害"], ["Storage: keep volatile flammable liquids away from heat; store reactive metals (Na, K) in oil; store acids and alkalis in separate labelled bottles.", "储存：易燃液体远离热源；钠钾浸在油中；酸碱分开存放"], ["Disposal: pour dilute acids/alkalis down the sink with lots of water after neutralising; do not pour organic solvents, heavy metals (Pb, Hg) or large amounts of chemicals into the sink; put them into labelled waste containers.", "处理：稀酸碱中和后用大量水冲；有机溶剂、重金属放入专用废物容器"], ["Spillage: acid on skin — rinse with plenty of water; spill on bench — neutralise (sodium hydrogencarbonate for acid), then wipe up; inform the teacher.", "酸溅到皮肤用大量水冲洗；桌上酸溢出用碳酸氢钠中和"]], "", "Tip: when asked 'why use the blue flame', answer: it is hotter because of complete combustion and gives no soot."], ["1.1 Measuring Apparatus: Accuracy and Choosing", "1.1 量具：准确度与选择", [["Measuring cylinder: approximate volumes (about 1 cm³ per division); beaker is not accurate.", "量筒：近似体积；烧杯不准确"], ["Pipette: measures a fixed volume (usually 25.0 cm³) accurately; use a pipette filler, never mouth.", "移液管：准确量取固定体积（常用25.0 cm³），用吸球，不可用口"], ["Burette: measures variable volume, reading to two decimal places (precision 0.05 cm³), e.g. 23.45 cm³; read at eye level, at the bottom of the meniscus.", "滴定管：读数到小数点后两位（精度0.05 cm³），视线与弯月面最低处平齐"], ["Volumetric flask: prepares 250 cm³ standard solution; electronic balance: reads mass to 0.01 g; thermometer: temperature; stopwatch: time.", "容量瓶：配250 cm³标准溶液；电子天平：读到0.01 g"], ["Choose by purpose: accurate fixed volume → pipette; accurate variable volume → burette; approximate volume → measuring cylinder.", "按用途选：准确固定体积→移液管；准确可变体积→滴定管；近似→量筒"]], "", "Tip: justify the apparatus you choose (accuracy)."], ["1.1 Laboratory Safety and First Aid (F + H)", "1.1 实验室安全与急救", [["F1 Wear goggles, gloves and a lab coat. H: protects eyes and skin from splashes.", "F1 护目镜、手套、实验服；保护眼睛和皮肤"], ["F2 Use a fume cupboard for toxic gases. H: poisonous gases such as chlorine and sulphur dioxide are removed.", "F2 有毒气体用通风橱"], ["F3 Keep flammable liquids away from flame. H: prevents fire.", "F3 易燃液体远离火焰"], ["F4 Know where the fire extinguisher, sand bucket and eyewash are. H: act quickly in an accident.", "F4 熟悉灭火器、沙桶、洗眼器位置"], ["F5 Burns or chemicals on skin: rinse with plenty of running water, then report to the teacher. H: removes the chemical and cools the skin.", "F5 皮肤沾到化学品或烫伤：大量流水冲洗并报告老师"], ["F6 Do not taste, eat or drink in the lab; wash hands after the experiment.", "F6 不尝、不吃喝，实验后洗手"]], "", "Tip: for 4-6 marks give F + H pairs."], ["1.2 Development of Chemistry", "1.2 化学的发展", [["Alchemy (early): tried to turn metals into gold and find an elixir of life; it used experiments but no scientific method.", "炼金术：想把金属变成金，找长生不老药"], ["Robert Boyle (1627–1691) treated chemistry as a science based on experiments and measurement.", "波义耳：以实验与测量作为科学方法"], ["Antoine Lavoisier showed the role of oxygen in burning and stated conservation of mass; John Dalton proposed the atomic theory (1803).", "拉瓦锡：氧在燃烧中的作用、质量守恒；道尔顿：原子论(1803)"], ["Dmitri Mendeleev arranged elements in a periodic table (1869); Marie Curie discovered polonium and radium.", "门捷列夫：元素周期表(1869)；居里夫人：钋与镭"], ["Chemistry now uses scientific investigation and modern technology.", "现代化学依靠科学探究与科技"]], "", "Tip: the names and years here are examples; check which ones your textbook uses."], ["1.2 Branches of Chemistry and Careers", "1.2 化学的分支与职业", [["Analytical chemistry: identify and measure substances (water and food quality).", "分析化学：鉴定与测量物质"], ["Organic chemistry: carbon compounds; inorganic chemistry: elements and compounds other than most carbon compounds.", "有机化学：碳化合物；无机化学：其余元素与化合物"], ["Physical chemistry: energy and rates of reactions; biochemistry: chemistry of living things; industrial and environmental chemistry.", "物理化学、生物化学、工业与环境化学"], ["Careers: chemist, pharmacist, forensic scientist, chemical engineer, food technologist, biochemist, environmental consultant.", "职业：化学家、药剂师、鉴证科学家、化工师、食品技术员、生化学家、环境顾问"]], "", "Tip: link each career with a branch."], ["1.2 Importance of Chemistry in Daily Life (F + H)", "1.2 化学对生活的重要性", [["F1 Medicine. H: medicines and vaccines treat and prevent diseases.", "F1 医药；药物与疫苗防治疾病"], ["F2 Agriculture. H: fertilisers increase crop yield; pesticides protect crops.", "F2 农业；肥料增产，农药保护"], ["F3 Food. H: preservatives and flavourings keep food fresh and tasty.", "F3 食品；防腐与调味"], ["F4 Industry. H: alloys, plastics, glass and fuels are made by chemical processes.", "F4 工业；合金、塑料、玻璃、燃料"], ["F5 Environment. H: water treatment and green technology reduce pollution.", "F5 环境；水处理与绿色科技"]], "", "Tip: always give the field + a product."], ["Scientific Investigation in Chemistry", "化学中的科学探究", [["Steps: identify a problem → make a hypothesis → plan the experiment (variables, apparatus, procedure) → collect data → analyse → conclude → write the report.", "步骤：提出问题→假设→设计→收集数据→分析→结论→报告"], ["Problem statement is a question: 'How does the concentration of sodium thiosulphate affect the rate of reaction?'", "问题陈述写成疑问句"], ["Hypothesis: 'The higher the concentration of sodium thiosulphate, the shorter the time for the cross to disappear.'", "假设：浓度越高，时间越短"], ["Variables: manipulated (concentration), responding (time/rate), fixed (volume, temperature, mass/size of other reactants).", "变量：操纵（浓度）、响应（时间）、固定（体积、温度等）"], ["Results table with units, graph (manipulated on x-axis), conclusion that accepts or rejects the hypothesis.", "结果表要有单位；图 x 轴为操纵变量；结论接受或否定假设"]], "", "Tip: the conclusion must be the hypothesis stated as a result, e.g. 'The hypothesis is accepted.'"], ["Planning an Experiment: Example", "设计实验示例", [["Aim: to investigate the effect of temperature on the rate of reaction between sodium thiosulphate and sulphuric acid.", "目的：温度对反应速率的影响"], ["Materials: 0.2 mol dm⁻³ \\(\\ce{Na2S2O3}\\), 1.0 mol dm⁻³ \\(\\ce{H2SO4}\\), conical flask, white paper with a cross, measuring cylinders, thermometer, stopwatch, water bath.", "材料与仪器"], ["Procedure: 50 cm³ \\(\\ce{Na2S2O3}\\) is warmed to 30 °C in the flask; place it on the cross; add 5 cm³ acid, start the stopwatch; stop when the cross disappears; record the time; repeat at 35, 40, 45, 50 °C.", "步骤：设定温度，加酸，计时到十字消失；重复"], ["Table: temperature / °C, time / s, 1/time / s⁻¹ (rate ∝ 1/time).", "表格：温度、时间、1/时间"], ["Precautions: swirl the flask the same way each time, the same observer, the same volumes, ventilate (SO₂ gas is produced).", "注意：同样摇晃、同一观察者、相同体积、通风"]], "", "Tip: always state HOW you will measure the responding variable (e.g. time for the cross to disappear)."], ["1.3 Writing Variables, Problem Statement and Hypothesis", "1.3 写变量、问题陈述与假设", [["Manipulated variable: the one you change. Responding variable: the one you measure. Fixed variable: kept the same to make a fair test.", "操纵变量：改变；响应变量：测量；固定变量：保持不变"], ["Problem statement: 'How does ___ affect ___?' or 'Does ___ affect ___?'", "问题陈述：“___如何影响___？”"], ["Hypothesis: 'The higher/lower the ___, the higher/lower the ___.'", "假设：“___越高/低，___越高/低”"], ["Example: effect of the type of metal on the voltage of a simple cell. Manipulated: type of metal; responding: voltage; fixed: electrolyte, concentration, distance between electrodes.", "例：金属种类对简单电池电压的影响"], ["Aim: 'To investigate the effect of ___ on ___.'", "目的：“探究___对___的影响”"]], "", "Tip: use the same words as in the question."], ["1.3 Presenting Data and Drawing Conclusions", "1.3 数据呈现与结论", [["Table: manipulated variable in the first column; headings with units; repeat readings and average if needed.", "表格：操纵变量放第一列；标题带单位"], ["Graph: title, axes labelled with units, suitable scale, plot points, smooth line or line of best fit.", "图：标题、坐标轴与单位、合适刻度、描点、平滑线"], ["Conclusion: state the relationship and whether the hypothesis is accepted or rejected.", "结论：写出关系并说明假设成立与否"], ["Compare results with the hypothesis and suggest improvements (repeat, more readings).", "对照假设并提出改进"]], "", "Tip: one line for the relationship, one for accepted/rejected."], ["1.3 Scientific Skills and Attitudes (F + H)", "1.3 科学技能与态度", [["F1 Observing. H: record colour change, gas, precipitate.", "F1 观察"], ["F2 Inferring. H: explain what an observation means.", "F2 推断"], ["F3 Predicting. H: use a pattern to say what will happen.", "F3 预测"], ["F4 Communicating. H: tables, graphs and a report.", "F4 沟通"], ["F5 Attitudes: honest, systematic, objective, careful and cooperative.", "F5 态度：诚实、有系统、客观、细心、合作"]], "", "Tip: skills = what you do; attitudes = how you do it."], ["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Apparatus and Safety", "示例题：试卷2 A部分", [["Q (a) [1 mark] Name apparatus P used to measure exactly 25.0 cm³ of alkali. Scheme: pipette.", "(a)准确量25.0 cm³用什么？移液管"], ["Q (b) [2 marks] State two safety precautions when heating a test tube. Scheme: slant at 45°; mouth away from people; use a holder (any 2 × 1m).", "(b)加热试管的两项安全措施：任意2点"], ["Q (c) [3 marks] Why is a burette more suitable than a measuring cylinder in titration? Scheme: reads to two decimal places // more accurate; volume is added drop by drop; end point is found accurately (any 3 × 1m).", "(c)为何滴定用滴定管：更准确、逐滴加入、终点准确"], ["Q (d) [2 marks] Name two branches of chemistry. Scheme: organic; inorganic; physical; analytical; biochemistry (any 2 × 1m).", "(d)两个分支"]], "", "Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style."], ["Sample Paper 3 (Practical): Answer Scheme", "示例题：试卷3（实验）评分", [["Problem statement (1m): How does the concentration of sodium thiosulphate solution affect the rate of reaction with sulphuric acid?", "问题陈述(1分)"], ["Variables (3m): manipulated — concentration of sodium thiosulphate; responding — time for the cross to disappear; fixed — volume and concentration of acid, temperature.", "变量(3分)"], ["Hypothesis (1m): The higher the concentration of sodium thiosulphate, the shorter the time for the cross to disappear.", "假设(1分)"], ["Materials and apparatus (2m); procedure (4m); table with headings and units (2m) — see the planning example slide.", "材料与仪器(2分)、步骤(4分)、表格(2分)"]], "", "Tip: self-made scheme; marks are only an example, ask your teacher for the real breakdown."], ["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips", "常见错误与考试提示", [["Writing the hypothesis as a question or without a relationship between the variables.", "假设写成问句，或没写变量关系"], ["Forgetting the fixed variables or giving a fixed variable as manipulated.", "漏写固定变量"], ["Using a measuring cylinder where high precision is required (use pipette/burette).", "需要精确时误用量筒"], ["Not stating the unit in the table headings.", "表头漏写单位"], ["Confusing the roles of a burette (variable volume) and a pipette (fixed volume).", "混淆滴定管和移液管"]], "", "Tip: for procedure questions number the steps and mention repetition."], ["Uji Diri", "自测", [["S: Which apparatus is used to prepare 250 cm³ of a standard solution? J: A volumetric flask.", "问：配 250 cm³ 标准溶液用什么？答：容量瓶"], ["S: Why is a blue Bunsen flame used for heating? J: It is hotter and gives no soot because of complete combustion.", "问：为何用蓝色火焰？答：完全燃烧，更热且无烟灰"], ["S: State the manipulated, responding and fixed variables: effect of acid concentration on the rate of reaction with magnesium. J: Manipulated: acid concentration; responding: rate (volume of gas per time); fixed: mass of magnesium, volume and temperature of acid.", "问：变量？答：操纵：酸浓度；响应：速率；固定：镁质量、酸体积、温度"], ["S: How should a sodium metal be stored? J: Under oil (paraffin).", "问：钠如何储存？答：浸在油中"]], "", ""]], "kim|T4-2": [["Matter and the Kinetic Theory", "物质与动力学理论", [["Matter is anything that has mass and occupies space. It is made of tiny particles: atoms, molecules or ions.", "物质：有质量、占空间；由原子、分子或离子组成"], ["Atom: smallest neutral particle of an element (Mg, Fe). Molecule: two or more atoms joined by covalent bonds (\\(\\ce{O2}\\), \\(\\ce{H2O}\\)). Ion: charged particle (\\(\\ce{Na+}\\), \\(\\ce{Cl-}\\)).", "原子、分子、离子的定义"], ["Kinetic theory: particles are small, discrete, in constant random motion, with attractive forces and spaces between them; the higher the temperature the faster they move.", "动力学理论：粒子小、不连续、持续无规则运动，有引力和空隙；温度越高运动越快"], ["Solid: closely packed, orderly, vibrate in fixed positions, strong forces. Liquid: closely packed, disorderly, move past each other. Gas: far apart, move freely, weak forces.", "固液气：排列、运动、作用力各不同"], ["Evidence: diffusion of purple potassium manganate(VII) in water; diffusion of bromine gas — particles move and have spaces between them.", "证据：高锰酸钾在水中扩散、溴蒸气扩散"]], "", "Tip: in 'explain' questions mention the arrangement, movement and forces of the particles."], ["2.1 Particles in Solid, Liquid and Gas", "2.1 固体、液体、气体中的粒子", [["Solid: particles very close together in a regular arrangement; strong forces of attraction; vibrate about fixed positions; fixed shape and volume; cannot be compressed.", "固体：粒子紧密规则排列；引力强；在固定位置振动；形状体积固定；不可压缩"], ["Liquid: particles close but in a random arrangement; weaker forces; move slowly past one another; fixed volume but no fixed shape; cannot be compressed easily.", "液体：粒子靠近但无规则；引力较弱；缓慢移动；体积固定、形状不固定"], ["Gas: particles far apart in a random arrangement; very weak forces; move rapidly in all directions; no fixed shape or volume; easily compressed.", "气体：粒子相距远；引力极弱；高速运动；无固定形状与体积；易压缩"], ["Kinetic energy of the particles: gas > liquid > solid.", "粒子动能：气体＞液体＞固体"]], "", "Tip: for comparison questions give arrangement, force, movement and energy."], ["2.1 Diffusion as Evidence for the Kinetic Theory", "2.1 扩散：粒子运动的证据", [["Diffusion: the random movement of particles from a region of higher concentration to a region of lower concentration until evenly mixed.", "扩散：粒子由高浓度向低浓度随机移动，直到均匀"], ["Evidence: a crystal of potassium manganate(VII) dissolves and the purple colour spreads through the water without stirring; bromine vapour spreads through a gas jar.", "证据：高锰酸钾晶体在水中扩散；溴蒸气充满集气瓶"], ["This shows that matter is made of tiny discrete particles which are in constant random motion and have spaces between them.", "说明物质由微小粒子构成、不断随机运动、粒子之间有空隙"], ["Diffusion is fastest in gases (particles move fastest and are far apart) and slowest in solids; it is faster at higher temperature.", "气体中扩散最快，固体最慢；温度越高越快"]], "", "Tip: write the observation AND the conclusion about particles."], ["Changes of State and Heating Curves", "状态变化与加热曲线", [["Melting (solid → liquid) and boiling (liquid → gas) absorb heat (endothermic); freezing and condensation release heat. Sublimation: solid → gas directly (iodine, dry ice).", "熔化、沸腾吸热；凝固、凝结放热；升华"], ["Heating curve: temperature rises, flat at the melting point, rises, flat at the boiling point.", "加热曲线：升温—熔点平台—升温—沸点平台"], ["At the flat parts the heat energy absorbed is used to overcome the forces of attraction between particles, not to increase the kinetic energy, so the temperature does not change.", "平台处热能用于克服粒子间引力，不增加动能，所以温度不变"], ["Cooling curve: the reverse; heat released as particles attract each other more strongly (condensation/freezing).", "冷却曲线：反过来"], ["A pure substance has a sharp, fixed melting/boiling point; an impure substance melts over a range and at a lower melting point.", "纯物质熔沸点固定；杂质使熔点降低、范围变宽"]], "", "Tip: 'The heat energy absorbed is used to overcome the forces of attraction between particles.'"], ["2.1 Reading a Heating Curve (F + H)", "2.1 解读加热曲线", [["F1 AB: the solid is heated; temperature rises. H: the particles gain kinetic energy and vibrate faster.", "F1 AB段：固体升温；粒子动能增加、振动加快"], ["F2 BC: melting at the melting point; temperature stays constant. H: heat is absorbed to overcome the forces of attraction between particles, not to raise the kinetic energy.", "F2 BC段：熔化，温度不变；热量用来克服粒子间引力"], ["F3 CD: the liquid is heated; temperature rises. H: kinetic energy increases.", "F3 CD段：液体升温"], ["F4 DE: boiling at the boiling point; temperature stays constant. H: heat overcomes the forces so the particles move far apart.", "F4 DE段：沸腾，温度不变"], ["F5 A pure substance has a sharp melting point; an impure substance melts over a range at a lower temperature.", "F5 纯物质熔点固定；不纯物熔点较低且范围宽"]], "", "Tip: constant temperature + heat used to overcome forces = 2 marks."], ["2.1 Cooling Curve and Experiment Notes", "2.1 冷却曲线与实验说明", [["Cooling curve: temperature falls, then stays constant at the freezing point, then falls again.", "冷却曲线：降温→凝固点保持不变→再降温"], ["At the freezing point heat is released as particles attract each other and form a regular arrangement; this heat equals the heat lost to the surroundings, so the temperature stays constant.", "凝固时粒子间形成引力并释放热量，抵消散失的热量，温度不变"], ["Experiment: naphthalene in a boiling tube heated in a water bath (indirect heating) because naphthalene is flammable; stir and record the temperature every 30 seconds.", "实验：萘放在试管中用水浴间接加热（萘易燃）；搅拌，每30秒记录"], ["Remove the boiling tube from the water bath and let it cool while stirring for the cooling curve; the thermometer must not touch the tube.", "冷却曲线：取出试管边搅拌边冷却；温度计不碰管壁"]], "", "Tip: say 'indirect heating' and give the reason."], ["Development of Atomic Models", "原子模型的发展", [["Dalton (1808): atoms are tiny solid indivisible spheres; atoms of an element are identical.", "道尔顿：不可分割的实心球"], ["Thomson (1897): discovered the electron; 'plum pudding' model — electrons embedded in a positive sphere.", "汤姆逊：发现电子；葡萄干布丁模型"], ["Rutherford (1911): gold foil experiment — most α-particles passed through, a few were deflected, very few bounced back → small, dense, positive nucleus; electrons orbit it.", "卢瑟福：金箔实验；原子有小而致密的带正电核"], ["Bohr (1913): electrons orbit the nucleus in fixed shells with fixed energies.", "玻尔：电子在固定壳层（能级）上运动"], ["Chadwick (1932): discovered the neutron in the nucleus → current model: protons and neutrons in the nucleus, electrons in shells.", "查德威克：发现中子"]], "", "Tip: remember the order D–T–R–B–C and what each contributed."], ["2.2 Contributions of Scientists (F + H)", "2.2 科学家的贡献", [["F1 Dalton (1803): atoms are tiny, solid, indivisible spheres. H: atoms of one element are identical.", "F1 道尔顿：原子是不可分割的实心小球"], ["F2 Thomson (1897): discovered the electron. H: plum-pudding model — electrons embedded in a positively charged sphere.", "F2 汤姆孙：发现电子；葡萄干布丁模型"], ["F3 Rutherford (1911): discovered the nucleus. H: the atom is mostly empty space with a small, dense, positive nucleus; electrons move around it.", "F3 卢瑟福：发现原子核；原子大部分是空的"], ["F4 Bohr (1913): electrons move in fixed orbits (shells) around the nucleus, each with a fixed energy.", "F4 玻尔：电子在固定轨道（壳层）运行"], ["F5 Chadwick (1932): discovered the neutron in the nucleus, giving the modern model.", "F5 查德威克：发现中子"]], "", "Tip: scientist + year + what was discovered."], ["2.2 Rutherford's Alpha-Scattering Experiment", "2.2 卢瑟福的α粒子散射实验", [["Alpha particles (positive) were fired at a very thin gold foil.", "把带正电的α粒子射向极薄的金箔"], ["Observation: most passed straight through; some were deflected through small angles; very few bounced back.", "观察：大多数穿过；少数偏转；极少数反弹"], ["Conclusion: most of the atom is empty space; the nucleus is very small, very dense and positively charged; it repels the alpha particles.", "结论：原子大部分是空的；原子核小而致密且带正电"], ["This replaced Thomson's plum-pudding model.", "取代了汤姆孙模型"]], "", "Tip: observation → conclusion pairs."], ["Structure of the Atom", "原子结构", [["Proton: mass 1 u, charge +1, in nucleus. Neutron: mass 1 u, no charge, in nucleus. Electron: negligible mass, charge −1, in shells.", "质子、中子、电子的质量与电荷"], ["Proton number Z = number of protons = number of electrons in a neutral atom. Nucleon number A = protons + neutrons. Neutrons = A − Z.", "质子数 Z；核子数 A；中子数 = A − Z"], ["Nuclide symbol \\(^{A}_{Z}\\text{X}\\): e.g. \\(^{23}_{11}\\text{Na}\\) has 11 protons, 11 electrons and 12 neutrons.", "核素符号：Na-23：11 质子、11 电子、12 中子"], ["Electron arrangement (first 20 elements): 2.8.8.2 maximum per shell; examples Na 2.8.1; Cl 2.8.7; Ca 2.8.8.2. Valence electrons = electrons in the outermost shell.", "电子排布：2.8.8.2；最外层为价电子"], ["Atomic diagrams: draw the nucleus with the number of protons and neutrons and the shells with electrons.", "画原子结构图：核内质子/中子数、各壳层电子"]], "", "Tip: always check the sum of electrons per shell equals the proton number for a neutral atom."], ["2.3 Worked Example: Particles in Atoms and Ions", "2.3 例题：原子和离子中的粒子", [["Atom with proton number 17 and nucleon number 35: protons = 17; electrons = 17; neutrons = 35 − 17 = 18.", "质子数17、核子数35：质子17、电子17、中子18"], ["Cl⁻ ion: 17 protons, 18 electrons (one extra electron), 18 neutrons; electron arrangement 2.8.8.", "Cl⁻：17质子、18电子、18中子；2.8.8"], ["Na⁺ ion (proton number 11): 11 protons, 10 electrons; electron arrangement 2.8.", "Na⁺：11质子、10电子；2.8"], ["Relative mass: proton 1, neutron 1, electron about 1/1836; relative charge +1, 0, −1.", "相对质量：质子1、中子1、电子约1/1836；电荷+1、0、−1"]], "", "Tip: ion = change in electrons only."], ["2.3 Worked Example: Electron Arrangement and Valence Electrons", "2.3 例题：电子排布与价电子", [["Maximum electrons: first shell 2, second shell 8, third shell 8 (for the first 20 elements), fourth shell 2.", "每层最多：2、8、8（前20号元素）、2"], ["Mg (proton number 12): 2.8.2; three shells → Period 3; two valence electrons → Group 2.", "镁：2.8.2；3个壳层→第3周期；2个价电子→第2族"], ["S (16): 2.8.6; Period 3, Group 16. K (19): 2.8.8.1; Period 4, Group 1.", "硫：2.8.6；钾：2.8.8.1"], ["Atomic diagram: nucleus showing protons and neutrons; electrons drawn on each shell.", "原子图：原子核标质子中子；各壳层画电子"]], "", "Tip: number of shells = period; valence electrons = group (Groups 1 and 2; 10 + valence for 13–18)."], ["Isotopes", "同位素", [["Isotopes are atoms of the same element with the same number of protons but a different number of neutrons (different nucleon numbers).", "同位素：质子数相同、中子数不同"], ["Same chemical properties (same electron arrangement); different physical properties (mass, density, rate of diffusion).", "化学性质相同；物理性质不同"], ["Examples: hydrogen-1, deuterium (hydrogen-2), tritium (hydrogen-3); carbon-12 and carbon-14; chlorine-35 and chlorine-37; uranium-235 and uranium-238.", "例：氢-1、氘、氚；碳-12/碳-14；氯-35/氯-37"], ["Relative atomic mass from abundance: Cl-35 (75%) and Cl-37 (25%): \\(A_r=\\dfrac{35\\times75+37\\times25}{100}=35.5\\).", "由丰度求相对原子质量：35.5"], ["Unstable isotopes are radioactive (radioisotopes), e.g. C-14, I-131, Co-60.", "不稳定同位素有放射性"]], "", "Tip: 'Same number of protons, different number of neutrons.'"], ["2.4 Isotopes: Same and Different Properties (F + H)", "2.4 同位素：相同与不同的性质", [["F1 Isotopes are atoms of the same element with the same proton number but different nucleon numbers. H: they have different numbers of neutrons.", "F1 同位素：质子数相同、核子数不同"], ["F2 Same chemical properties. H: they have the same number of electrons and the same electron arrangement.", "F2 化学性质相同：电子排布相同"], ["F3 Different physical properties. H: different masses, densities and melting points because of different neutrons.", "F3 物理性质不同：质量、密度、熔点"], ["Example: hydrogen has three isotopes, ¹H, ²H and ³H; carbon has ¹²C, ¹³C and ¹⁴C.", "例：氢三种同位素；碳-12、13、14"]], "", "Tip: 'same proton number, different nucleon number' is the 2-mark definition."], ["2.4 Relative Atomic Mass from Isotopes: Worked Example", "2.4 用同位素计算相对原子质量", [["Chlorine has ³⁵Cl (75%) and ³⁷Cl (25%).", "氯：³⁵Cl 75%，³⁷Cl 25%"], ["RAM = (35 × 75 + 37 × 25) ÷ 100 = (2625 + 925) ÷ 100 = 35.5.", "相对原子质量 = (35×75 + 37×25)÷100 = 35.5"], ["Copper has ⁶³Cu (69%) and ⁶⁵Cu (31%): RAM = (63 × 69 + 65 × 31) ÷ 100 = 63.62.", "铜：63.62"], ["Show the formula, the substitution and the final answer; RAM has no unit.", "写公式、代入、答案；相对原子质量无单位"]], "", "Tip: check that the answer lies between the two nucleon numbers."], ["Uses of Isotopes", "同位素的应用", [["Archaeology: carbon-14 dating of fossils and artefacts (half-life 5730 years).", "考古：碳-14 测年"], ["Medicine: iodine-131 treats thyroid disorders and traces the thyroid; cobalt-60 gamma rays for cancer radiotherapy and for sterilising equipment.", "医疗：碘-131、钴-60"], ["Agriculture: phosphorus-32 as a tracer to study the uptake of fertiliser by plants; irradiating food to kill bacteria.", "农业：磷-32 示踪"], ["Industry: checking leaks in pipes (tracers); measuring thickness of paper/metal sheets.", "工业：检漏、测厚"], ["Nuclear energy: uranium-235 as fuel in reactors; deuterium in heavy water (moderator).", "核能：铀-235、氘"]], "", "Tip: link each isotope to the radiation and the exact purpose."], ["2.4 Radioisotope Uses (F + H)", "2.4 放射性同位素的用途", [["F1 Archaeology: carbon-14. H: radiocarbon dating to find the age of fossils and ancient objects.", "F1 考古：碳-14定年"], ["F2 Medicine: cobalt-60 and iodine-131. H: cobalt-60 gamma rays treat cancer and sterilise instruments; iodine-131 treats and diagnoses thyroid disease.", "F2 医学：钴-60治癌、消毒；碘-131甲状腺"], ["F3 Agriculture: phosphorus-32. H: traces how plants absorb fertiliser; radiation preserves food.", "F3 农业：磷-32追踪肥料吸收"], ["F4 Industry: sodium-24. H: detects leaks in underground pipes.", "F4 工业：钠-24检测漏水"], ["F5 Energy: uranium-235 is the fuel in nuclear power stations.", "F5 能源：铀-235为核电燃料"]], "", "Tip: isotope + field + use."], ["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Atomic Structure", "示例题：试卷2 A部分", [["Table: atom X has 6 protons and 6 neutrons; atom Y has 6 protons and 8 neutrons; atom Z has 7 protons and 7 neutrons.", "表：X 6质子6中子；Y 6质子8中子；Z 7质子7中子"], ["(a) [1] Which two atoms are isotopes? Scheme: X and Y.", "(a)哪两个是同位素？X和Y"], ["(b) [2] Why do X and Y have the same chemical properties? Scheme: same number of electrons; same electron arrangement / valence electrons (2 × 1m).", "(b)化学性质为何相同"], ["(c) [2] State the electron arrangement of Z. Scheme: 2.5 (1m) — Z is in Group 15 (1m). (d) [1] State one use of Y (C-14). Scheme: radiocarbon dating.", "(c)Z的电子排布2.5；(d)Y的一项用途：碳-14定年"]], "", "Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style."], ["Sample Paper 2 Section B: Atomic Models and Heating Curve", "示例题：试卷2 B部分", [["(a) [10] Describe how the atomic model developed from Dalton to Chadwick. Scheme: Dalton solid sphere; Thomson electrons in positive sphere; Rutherford nucleus and empty space; Bohr shells; Chadwick neutron (each model name 1m + description 1m).", "(a)原子模型的发展：五位科学家各2分"], ["(b) [10] Explain the heating curve of naphthalene. Scheme: AB solid heated, kinetic energy increases; BC melting, constant temperature because heat overcomes forces; CD liquid heated; DE boiling; heat absorbed overcomes forces (any 10 points).", "(b)解释萘的加热曲线"], ["Write complete sentences and name the apparatus and the method (water bath, stirring) when asked about the experiment.", "写完整句子；提到实验方法（水浴、搅拌）"]], "", "Tip: self-made practice question; the real essay marks come from your teacher's scheme."], ["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips", "常见错误与考试提示", [["Confusing proton number with nucleon number.", "混淆质子数与核子数"], ["Saying isotopes have different chemical properties; they differ in physical properties only.", "同位素化学性质相同"], ["Forgetting to include 'neutral' when stating protons = electrons.", "质子=电子只在中性原子"], ["Giving the Thomson model as 'nucleus' — he found electrons only.", "汤姆逊没有发现原子核"], ["Wrong electron arrangement beyond 2.8.8 (calcium is 2.8.8.2, not 2.8.10).", "钙是 2.8.8.2"]], "", "Tip: draw clear diagrams with the correct number of electrons per shell."], ["Uji Diri", "自测", [["S: What is an isotope? J: Atoms of the same element with the same proton number but different neutron numbers.", "问：什么是同位素？答：质子数相同、中子数不同的原子"], ["S: How many neutrons are in \\(^{27}_{13}\\text{Al}\\)? J: 27 − 13 = 14.", "问：Al-27 有几个中子？答：14"], ["S: Why does the temperature stay constant during melting? J: Heat energy is used to overcome the forces between particles, not to increase kinetic energy.", "问：熔化时温度为何不变？答：热能用于克服粒子间引力"], ["S: Which experiment showed the existence of the nucleus? J: Rutherford's gold foil experiment.", "问：谁证明了原子核存在？答：卢瑟福金箔实验"]], "", ""]], "kim|T4-3": [["Relative Atomic Mass and Relative Molecular Mass", "相对原子质量与相对分子质量", [["Relative atomic mass \\(A_r\\) = average mass of one atom of the element ÷ (1/12 × mass of one atom of carbon-12).", "相对原子质量：相对于 C-12 质量的 1/12"], ["Relative molecular mass \\(M_r\\) = sum of the relative atomic masses of all atoms in the molecule: \\(\\ce{H2O}\\): 2(1) + 16 = 18. For ionic compounds use relative formula mass.", "相对分子质量 = 各原子 Ar 之和"], ["Examples: \\(\\ce{CO2}\\) = 12 + 2(16) = 44; \\(\\ce{CuSO4.5H2O}\\) = 64 + 32 + 4(16) + 5(18) = 250; \\(\\ce{(NH4)2SO4}\\) = 2(14 + 4) + 32 + 64 = 132.", "算例：CO₂=44；CuSO₄·5H₂O=250；(NH₄)₂SO₄=132"], ["Relative masses have no units.", "相对质量没有单位"], ["Common A_r: H 1, C 12, N 14, O 16, Na 23, Mg 24, Al 27, S 32, Cl 35.5, K 39, Ca 40, Fe 56, Cu 64, Zn 65.", "常用 Ar 值"]], "", "Tip: brackets in a formula multiply everything inside them."], ["3.1 Worked Examples: Relative Molecular and Formula Mass", "3.1 例题：相对分子质量与式量", [["Use A_r: H 1, C 12, N 14, O 16, Na 23, Mg 24, Al 27, S 32, Cl 35.5, K 39, Ca 40, Fe 56, Cu 64, Zn 65.", "用相对原子质量：H1、C12、N14、O16、Na23、Mg24、Al27、S32、Cl35.5、K39、Ca40、Fe56、Cu64、Zn65"], ["\\(\\ce{H2SO4}\\): 2(1) + 32 + 4(16) = 98.", "H₂SO₄ = 98"], ["\\(\\ce{Ca(OH)2}\\): 40 + 2(16 + 1) = 74.", "Ca(OH)₂ = 74"], ["\\(\\ce{Al2(SO4)3}\\): 2(27) + 3[32 + 4(16)] = 54 + 288 = 342.", "Al₂(SO₄)₃ = 342"], ["\\(\\ce{CuSO4.5H2O}\\): 64 + 32 + 4(16) + 5(18) = 250. Ionic compounds use 'relative formula mass'.", "CuSO₄·5H₂O = 250；离子化合物称式量"]], "", "Tip: write the working; M_r and A_r have no unit."], ["The Mole Concept", "摩尔概念", [["One mole is the amount of substance that contains as many particles as there are atoms in 12 g of carbon-12: \\(N_A=6.02\\times10^{23}\\) mol⁻¹ (Avogadro constant).", "1 摩尔含 6.02×10²³ 个粒子"], ["Number of moles \\(n=\\dfrac{N}{N_A}\\); \\(n=\\dfrac{m}{M}\\) (M molar mass in g mol⁻¹, equal to A_r or M_r in value); \\(n=\\dfrac{V}{24}\\) for gases at room conditions (V in dm³).", "n = N/NA = m/M = V/24（气体，室温常压，24 dm³ mol⁻¹）"], ["Molar volume of any gas: 24 dm³ mol⁻¹ at room temperature and pressure (25 °C, 1 atm); 22.4 dm³ mol⁻¹ at STP (0 °C, 1 atm).", "气体摩尔体积：室温常压 24 dm³/mol；STP 22.4"], ["Molar mass: mass of one mole of a substance (g mol⁻¹); \\(\\ce{H2O}\\) = 18 g mol⁻¹.", "摩尔质量"], ["Number of atoms in a molecule: 1 mol \\(\\ce{CO2}\\) contains 1 mol C atoms and 2 mol O atoms.", "1 mol CO₂ 含 1 mol C、2 mol O"]], "", "Tip: a 'mole map' — mass ⇄ moles ⇄ particles; moles ⇄ volume."], ["3.2 Mole Map: Which Formula to Use?", "3.2 摩尔图：该用哪个公式？", [["Given mass (g) → moles = mass ÷ molar mass.", "已知质量→摩尔 = 质量 ÷ 摩尔质量"], ["Given volume of gas in dm³ → moles = V ÷ 24 (room conditions); if in cm³ → V ÷ 24 000.", "已知气体体积（dm³）→ V÷24；cm³ 则 ÷24000"], ["Given number of particles → moles = N ÷ 6.02 × 10²³; atoms in a molecule: multiply by the number of atoms.", "已知粒子数→ N÷6.02×10²³；分子中的原子数要相乘"], ["After finding moles, convert to what is asked: mass = n × M; volume = n × 24; particles = n × 6.02 × 10²³.", "先求摩尔，再换算成所求量"], ["Always state the unit: g, dm³, mol, molecules/atoms.", "答案必须带单位"]], "", "Tip: moles first, always."], ["Worked Examples: Mole Calculations", "例题：摩尔计算", [["Q1: Number of molecules in 3.6 g of water: n = 3.6/18 = 0.20 mol; N = 0.20 × 6.02 × 10²³ = 1.2 × 10²³ molecules.", "题1：3.6 g 水：1.2×10²³ 个分子"], ["Q2: Mass of 0.25 mol \\(\\ce{CaCO3}\\) (M = 100): m = 0.25 × 100 = 25 g.", "题2：25 g"], ["Q3: Volume of 4.4 g \\(\\ce{CO2}\\) at room conditions: n = 4.4/44 = 0.1 mol; V = 0.1 × 24 = 2.4 dm³.", "题3：2.4 dm³"], ["Q4: Number of H atoms in 0.5 mol \\(\\ce{NH3}\\): 0.5 × 3 × 6.02 × 10²³ = 9.03 × 10²³.", "题4：9.03×10²³"], ["Q5: Mass of 1.204 × 10²⁴ atoms of Mg: n = 1.204×10²⁴/6.02×10²³ = 2 mol; m = 2 × 24 = 48 g.", "题5：48 g"]], "", "Tip: show every step: mole first, then mass/volume/number."], ["3.2 Worked Examples: Comparing Quantities and Ratio of Atoms", "3.2 例题：比较数量与原子比", [["Which has more atoms: 4 g of He (A_r 4) or 2 g of \\(\\ce{H2}\\) (A_r 1)? He: 4 ÷ 4 = 1 mol atoms; \\(\\ce{H2}\\): 2 ÷ 2 = 1 mol molecules = 2 mol atoms. \\(\\ce{H2}\\) has more atoms.", "4 g 氦与 2 g 氢气谁的原子多？氢气（2 mol 原子）"], ["1 mol of \\(\\ce{CO2}\\) contains 1 mol C atoms and 2 mol O atoms; total 3 mol atoms = 3 × 6.02 × 10²³.", "1 mol CO₂ 含 3 mol 原子"], ["6.4 g Cu and 1.6 g O: Cu = 6.4 ÷ 64 = 0.1 mol; O = 1.6 ÷ 16 = 0.1 mol; ratio 1 : 1.", "6.4 g 铜与 1.6 g 氧：1:1"], ["Equal moles of different gases have the same volume at the same temperature and pressure (24 dm³ at room conditions).", "相同温度压力下，等摩尔气体体积相同"]], "", "Tip: compare in MOLES, not grams."], ["Chemical Formulae: Empirical and Molecular", "化学式：实验式与分子式", [["Empirical formula: simplest whole-number ratio of atoms of each element in a compound. Molecular formula: actual number of atoms in a molecule; = (empirical formula)n.", "实验式：最简整数比；分子式 = (实验式)ₙ"], ["Ionic formula: balance charges, e.g. \\(\\ce{Al^3+}\\) and \\(\\ce{SO4^2-}\\) → \\(\\ce{Al2(SO4)3}\\). Common ions: \\(\\ce{NH4+}\\), \\(\\ce{NO3-}\\), \\(\\ce{OH-}\\), \\(\\ce{CO3^2-}\\), \\(\\ce{SO4^2-}\\), \\(\\ce{PO4^3-}\\).", "离子化合物的化学式：平衡电荷"], ["Empirical formula of magnesium oxide experiment: heat Mg in a crucible with lid, lifting it briefly to let oxygen in; reheat until constant mass. Mass Mg = 2.4 g, mass MgO = 4.0 g → O = 1.6 g.", "氧化镁实验：加热直到质量恒定"], ["Mg: 2.4/24 = 0.10; O: 1.6/16 = 0.10 → ratio 1 : 1 → MgO.", "Mg 0.10 : O 0.10 = 1:1 → MgO"], ["Copper(II) oxide is reduced by hydrogen/methane in a combustion tube until constant mass — used for metals less reactive than hydrogen.", "氧化铜用氢气还原（用于比氢不活泼的金属）"]], "", "Tip: oxides of reactive metals (Mg) are found by oxidising the metal; oxides of unreactive metals (Cu) by reduction."], ["3.3 Names and Formulae of Common Ions", "3.3 常见离子的名称与化学式", [["Cations: H⁺, Li⁺, Na⁺, K⁺, Ag⁺, NH₄⁺ (1+); Mg²⁺, Ca²⁺, Ba²⁺, Zn²⁺, Cu²⁺, Fe²⁺, Pb²⁺ (2+); Al³⁺, Fe³⁺ (3+).", "阳离子：1+、2+、3+"], ["Anions: Cl⁻, Br⁻, I⁻, OH⁻, NO₃⁻, MnO₄⁻ (1−); O²⁻, SO₄²⁻, CO₃²⁻ (2−); PO₄³⁻ (3−).", "阴离子：1−、2−、3−"], ["Names: NH₄⁺ ammonium, OH⁻ hydroxide, NO₃⁻ nitrate, SO₄²⁻ sulphate, CO₃²⁻ carbonate, PO₄³⁻ phosphate, MnO₄⁻ manganate(VII).", "名称：铵、氢氧根、硝酸根、硫酸根、碳酸根、磷酸根、高锰酸根"], ["Transition metals can have more than one charge, shown by a Roman numeral: iron(II) Fe²⁺, iron(III) Fe³⁺, copper(II) Cu²⁺.", "过渡金属有不同价态，用罗马数字表示"]], "", "Tip: memorise these before Form 5 (salts and redox)."], ["3.3 Writing Formulae of Ionic Compounds", "3.3 离子化合物化学式的写法", [["Step 1: write the ions with their charges. Step 2: swap the numbers (criss-cross) so total positive charge = total negative charge. Step 3: simplify; use brackets for polyatomic ions.", "步骤：写离子与电荷→交叉调换→化简；多原子离子加括号"], ["Mg²⁺ + Cl⁻ → \\(\\ce{MgCl2}\\); Ca²⁺ + OH⁻ → \\(\\ce{Ca(OH)2}\\); Al³⁺ + SO₄²⁻ → \\(\\ce{Al2(SO4)3}\\).", "MgCl₂；Ca(OH)₂；Al₂(SO₄)₃"], ["Fe³⁺ + O²⁻ → \\(\\ce{Fe2O3}\\); Cu²⁺ + NO₃⁻ → \\(\\ce{Cu(NO3)2}\\); NH₄⁺ + SO₄²⁻ → \\(\\ce{(NH4)2SO4}\\).", "Fe₂O₃；Cu(NO₃)₂；(NH₄)₂SO₄"], ["Name the compound: metal first, then the non-metal ending in -ide (chloride, oxide) or the polyatomic ion name (sulphate, nitrate).", "命名：金属在前，非金属 -ide 或原子团名称"]], "", "Tip: 1 mark for the correct formula; wrong charges give a wrong formula."], ["Worked Example: Empirical and Molecular Formula", "例题：实验式与分子式", [["Q: A hydrocarbon contains 80% carbon and 20% hydrogen by mass. Its M_r = 30. Find the molecular formula.", "题：烃含 80% C，20% H，Mr = 30"], ["Step 1: moles per 100 g: C = 80/12 = 6.67; H = 20/1 = 20.", "步骤1：摩尔数：C 6.67；H 20"], ["Step 2: divide by the smallest: C = 1; H = 3 → empirical formula \\(\\ce{CH3}\\) (mass 15).", "步骤2：比值 1:3 → CH₃"], ["Step 3: n = 30/15 = 2 → molecular formula \\(\\ce{C2H6}\\).", "步骤3：n = 2 → C₂H₆"], ["If a ratio comes out as 1.5, multiply all by 2 (e.g. 1 : 1.5 → 2 : 3).", "出现 1.5 要乘以 2"]], "", "Tip: show 'mass → mole → ratio → formula' in a table."], ["3.3 Experiment: Empirical Formula of Magnesium Oxide (F + H)", "3.3 实验：氧化镁的实验式", [["F1 Clean the magnesium ribbon with sandpaper. H: removes the oxide layer so all the magnesium reacts.", "F1 砂纸擦镁带；去除氧化层"], ["F2 Heat the magnesium strongly in a crucible with a lid and lift the lid slightly now and then. H: lets oxygen enter; the lid stops white smoke (MgO) from escaping.", "F2 加盖加热，偶尔稍掀盖；让氧气进入，防止白烟逸出"], ["F3 Heat, cool and weigh until the mass is constant. H: shows that all the magnesium has reacted.", "F3 反复加热、冷却、称量至质量不变；说明反应完全"], ["F4 Calculate: mass of Mg = m₂ − m₁; mass of O = m₃ − m₂; moles of each, divide by the smallest to get the ratio. H: Mg : O = 1 : 1, so the empirical formula is MgO.", "F4 计算：质量→摩尔→最简整数比；实验式 MgO"], ["F5 Use tongs for the hot crucible and do not look at the bright flame.", "F5 用坩埚钳；不直视强光"]], "", "Tip: constant mass = complete reaction."], ["3.3 Experiment: Empirical Formula of Copper(II) Oxide (F + H)", "3.3 实验：氧化铜的实验式", [["F1 Pass hydrogen (or methane) through the combustion tube first. H: drives out the air to avoid an explosion.", "F1 先通氢气赶走空气，避免爆炸"], ["F2 Heat the copper(II) oxide while hydrogen flows. H: black copper(II) oxide is reduced to brown copper: \\(\\ce{CuO + H2 -> Cu + H2O}\\).", "F2 加热，黑色氧化铜被还原成棕色铜"], ["F3 Continue passing hydrogen while the tube cools. H: prevents hot copper from being oxidised again.", "F3 冷却时继续通氢气；防止热铜再氧化"], ["F4 Repeat heating, cooling and weighing until constant mass; calculate the ratio Cu : O. H: Cu : O = 1 : 1, so CuO.", "F4 称至恒重，计算比值"], ["F5 Burn off the excess hydrogen at the jet. Magnesium oxide cannot be reduced by hydrogen because magnesium is more reactive than hydrogen.", "F5 烧掉多余氢气；氧化镁不能被氢还原（镁比氢活泼）"]], "", "Tip: use hydrogen only for oxides of metals less reactive than hydrogen."], ["Chemical Equations", "化学方程式", [["A balanced equation shows reactants and products with the same number of each atom on both sides; use state symbols (s), (l), (g), (aq).", "配平：两边各原子数相等；注明状态符号"], ["Example: \\(\\ce{2Mg + O2 -> 2MgO}\\); \\(\\ce{CaCO3 + 2HCl -> CaCl2 + H2O + CO2}\\); \\(\\ce{2H2 + O2 -> 2H2O}\\).", "例子"], ["Ionic equation: only the ions that change; omit spectator ions. \\(\\ce{Ag+(aq) + Cl-(aq) -> AgCl(s)}\\).", "离子方程式：省略旁观离子"], ["Quantitative meaning: coefficients give the mole ratio: \\(\\ce{2H2 + O2 -> 2H2O}\\) means 2 mol H₂ reacts with 1 mol O₂ to give 2 mol H₂O.", "系数表示摩尔比"], ["Steps to write: word equation → correct formulae → balance coefficients (not subscripts) → state symbols.", "步骤：文字→化学式→配平→状态"]], "", "Tip: never change subscripts in a formula to balance an equation."], ["3.4 Balancing Chemical Equations: Steps and Common Errors", "3.4 配平化学方程式：步骤与常见错误", [["Step 1 write the correct formulae. Step 2 count the atoms of each element on both sides. Step 3 change only the coefficients (big numbers in front), never the subscripts.", "步骤：写对化学式→数原子→只改系数"], ["\\(\\ce{2Mg + O2 -> 2MgO}\\); \\(\\ce{C3H8 + 5O2 -> 3CO2 + 4H2O}\\); \\(\\ce{2Al + 3Cl2 -> 2AlCl3}\\).", "2Mg + O₂ → 2MgO 等"], ["State symbols: (s) solid, (l) liquid, (g) gas, (aq) aqueous; add them when the question asks.", "状态符号 (s)(l)(g)(aq)：题目要求时加上"], ["Common errors: changing subscripts (\\(\\ce{MgO2}\\)), forgetting to balance oxygen, wrong formula of the compound.", "常见错误：改下标、漏配氧、化学式错误"]], "", "Tip: the equation mark needs correct formulae AND a balanced equation."], ["Calculations Based on Equations", "根据方程式计算", [["Q: 10 g of calcium carbonate decomposes: \\(\\ce{CaCO3 -> CaO + CO2}\\). Find the mass of CaO and the volume of CO₂ at room conditions.", "题：10 g CaCO₃ 受热分解"], ["Step 1: n(CaCO₃) = 10/100 = 0.10 mol.", "n = 0.10 mol"], ["Step 2: ratio 1 : 1 : 1 → 0.10 mol CaO and 0.10 mol CO₂.", "摩尔比 1:1:1"], ["Step 3: m(CaO) = 0.10 × 56 = 5.6 g; V(CO₂) = 0.10 × 24 = 2.4 dm³.", "CaO = 5.6 g；CO₂ = 2.4 dm³"], ["Limiting reactant: when two reactant amounts are given, find the moles of each and divide by their coefficient; the smaller is limiting; percentage yield = actual ÷ theoretical × 100%.", "限量试剂：比较摩尔数/系数；产率 = 实际/理论 ×100%"]], "", "Tip: use the mole ratio from the balanced equation, not the mass ratio."], ["3.4 Worked Examples: Mass and Volume from an Equation", "3.4 例题：由方程式求质量与体积", [["Q1: 5.0 g \\(\\ce{CaCO3}\\) is heated: \\(\\ce{CaCO3 -> CaO + CO2}\\). n(CaCO₃) = 5.0 ÷ 100 = 0.05 mol; n(CO₂) = 0.05 mol; V = 0.05 × 24 = 1.2 dm³; mass of CaO = 0.05 × 56 = 2.8 g.", "题1：5.0 g CaCO₃ 受热：CO₂ 1.2 dm³；CaO 2.8 g"], ["Q2: 2.4 g Mg with excess HCl: \\(\\ce{Mg + 2HCl -> MgCl2 + H2}\\). n(Mg) = 2.4 ÷ 24 = 0.1 mol; n(H₂) = 0.1 mol; V = 0.1 × 24 = 2.4 dm³.", "题2：2.4 g Mg：H₂ 2.4 dm³"], ["Method: balanced equation → moles of the given substance → mole ratio from the coefficients → moles of the required substance → mass or volume.", "方法：配平→已知物摩尔→系数比→所求物摩尔→质量/体积"]], "", "Tip: the coefficients give the mole ratio."], ["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Mole Calculation", "示例题：试卷2 A部分（摩尔计算）", [["6.5 g of zinc reacts with excess hydrochloric acid: \\(\\ce{Zn + 2HCl -> ZnCl2 + H2}\\) (A_r: Zn = 65).", "6.5 g 锌与过量盐酸反应"], ["(a) [1] Moles of zinc. Scheme: 6.5 ÷ 65 = 0.1 mol.", "(a)锌的摩尔 0.1"], ["(b) [1] Moles of hydrogen. Scheme: 0.1 mol (ratio 1 : 1).", "(b)氢气的摩尔 0.1"], ["(c) [2] Volume of hydrogen at room conditions. Scheme: 0.1 × 24 (1m); 2.4 dm³ with unit (1m).", "(c)体积：公式/代入1分；2.4 dm³ 带单位1分"], ["(d) [2] Number of hydrogen molecules. Scheme: 0.1 × 6.02 × 10²³ (1m); 6.02 × 10²² molecules (1m).", "(d)分子数 6.02×10²²"]], "", "Tip: self-made practice question; marks follow the usual method + answer + unit pattern."], ["Sample Paper 2 Section B: Empirical Formula (Essay and Calculation)", "示例题：试卷2 B部分（实验式）", [["(a) [10] Describe an experiment to determine the empirical formula of magnesium oxide. Scheme: clean Mg; weigh crucible + lid + Mg; heat strongly and lift the lid; continue until Mg burns completely; cool and weigh; repeat heating, cooling and weighing until constant mass; record all masses; calculate the ratio (any 10 points).", "(a)描述氧化镁实验式的实验：任意10点"], ["(b) [6] Mass of Mg = 0.48 g and mass of MgO = 0.80 g. Scheme: mass of O = 0.32 g (1m); n(Mg) = 0.48 ÷ 24 = 0.02 mol; n(O) = 0.32 ÷ 16 = 0.02 mol (2m); ratio 1 : 1 (1m); empirical formula MgO (1m); show the working (1m).", "(b)计算：MgO"], ["(c) [4] Why can't hydrogen be used to find the empirical formula of MgO? Scheme: magnesium is more reactive than hydrogen (1m); hydrogen cannot reduce MgO (1m); copper(II) oxide can be used because copper is less reactive than hydrogen (1m); mass of copper and oxygen can be found by reduction (1m).", "(c)为何不能用氢气还原氧化镁"]], "", "Tip: self-made practice question; marks are an example, check with your teacher."], ["Common Mistakes", "常见错误", [["Mistake: forgetting that brackets multiply, e.g. \\(\\ce{Ca(OH)2}\\) has 2 O and 2 H.", "错误：括号内要乘下标"], ["Mistake: using 22.4 dm³ when the question says room conditions (24 dm³).", "错误：室温用 24，不是 22.4"]], "", ""], ["Uji Diri", "自测", [["S: Calculate M_r of \\(\\ce{Al2(SO4)3}\\). J: 2(27) + 3(32 + 64) = 342.", "问：Al₂(SO₄)₃ 的 Mr？答：342"], ["S: How many moles in 11 g \\(\\ce{CO2}\\)? J: 11/44 = 0.25 mol.", "问：11 g CO₂ 多少摩尔？答：0.25 mol"], ["S: Empirical formula of a compound with 2.4 g C and 0.8 g H? J: C 0.2 : H 0.8 = 1 : 4 → \\(\\ce{CH4}\\).", "问：2.4 g C、0.8 g H 的实验式？答：CH₄"]], "", ""]], "kim|T4-4": [["Development of the Periodic Table", "元素周期表的发展", [["Lavoisier (1789): grouped substances into metals and non-metals.", "拉瓦锡：金属与非金属"], ["Döbereiner (1829): triads — groups of three elements with similar properties, the middle one's atomic mass close to the average of the other two (Li, Na, K).", "德贝莱纳：三元素组"], ["Newlands (1864): law of octaves — every eighth element has similar properties when arranged by increasing atomic mass; failed after calcium.", "纽兰兹：八音律"], ["Mendeleev (1869): arranged elements by increasing atomic mass in groups of similar properties; left gaps for undiscovered elements and predicted their properties (e.g. germanium).", "门捷列夫：按原子质量排列，留空位并预测新元素"], ["Moseley (1913): arranged by increasing proton number — the basis of the modern periodic table.", "莫塞莱：按质子数排列 → 现代周期表"]], "", "Tip: remember that the modern table uses proton number, not atomic mass."], ["4.1 Contributions of Scientists to the Periodic Table (F + H)", "4.1 科学家对周期表的贡献", [["F1 Döbereiner (1829): triads — groups of three elements with similar properties where the atomic mass of the middle one is about the average of the other two (Li, Na, K; Cl, Br, I).", "F1 德贝莱纳：三素组；中间元素原子质量约为两端平均值"], ["F2 Newlands (1864): Law of Octaves — elements arranged by increasing atomic mass; every eighth element has similar properties. H: it failed after calcium.", "F2 纽兰兹：八音律；钙以后不适用"], ["F3 Mendeleev (1869): arranged elements by increasing atomic mass in groups with similar properties. H: he left gaps for undiscovered elements and predicted their properties (e.g. gallium, germanium).", "F3 门捷列夫：按原子质量排列；留空位并预测新元素"], ["F4 Moseley (1913): arranged elements by increasing proton number. H: this is the basis of the modern periodic table and solved the problems of Mendeleev's table.", "F4 莫斯莱：按质子数排列；现代周期表的基础"]], "", "Tip: scientist + year + basis of arrangement + problem or success."], ["Arrangement of the Modern Periodic Table", "现代周期表的排列", [["Elements are arranged in order of increasing proton number in 18 groups (vertical columns) and 7 periods (horizontal rows).", "按质子数递增排列：18 族、7 周期"], ["Group number: group 1 and 2 → equal to the number of valence electrons; groups 13–18 → valence electrons = group number − 10. Period number = number of shells occupied by electrons.", "族数 ↔ 价电子数；周期数 ↔ 电子层数"], ["Example: sodium 2.8.1 → group 1, period 3; chlorine 2.8.7 → group 17, period 3; calcium 2.8.8.2 → group 2, period 4.", "例：Na 第 1 族第 3 周期"], ["Blocks: metals on the left and middle, non-metals on the right, metalloids (Si, Ge) along the staircase; transition elements in groups 3–12.", "金属、非金属、类金属、过渡元素的位置"], ["Elements in the same group have similar chemical properties because they have the same number of valence electrons.", "同族化学性质相似，因价电子数相同"]], "", "Tip: from the electron arrangement you can name the group and the period immediately."], ["4.2 Worked Examples: Position of an Element", "4.2 例题：元素在周期表中的位置", [["Period = number of shells occupied by electrons. Group = number of valence electrons for Groups 1 and 2; 10 + valence electrons for Groups 13–18.", "周期＝壳层数；族＝价电子数（1、2族）；13–18族为10＋价电子数"], ["Element X: electron arrangement 2.8.3 → three shells → Period 3; three valence electrons → Group 13.", "X：2.8.3 → 第3周期、第13族"], ["Element Y: 2.8.7 → Period 3, Group 17 (a halogen). Element Z: 2.8.8.1 → Period 4, Group 1 (an alkali metal).", "Y：第3周期第17族；Z：第4周期第1族"], ["Metals are on the left and in the centre, non-metals on the right, and metalloids (B, Si, Ge, As, Sb, Te) along the staircase line.", "金属在左及中间，非金属在右，类金属在阶梯线上"]], "", "Tip: write the electron arrangement first, then period and group."], ["4.2 Trends Down a Group and Across a Period (F + H)", "4.2 同族与同周期的变化趋势", [["F1 Down a group the atomic size increases. H: the number of shells increases.", "F1 向下原子半径增大；壳层数增加"], ["F2 Down a group, metals become more reactive and non-metals less reactive. H: the valence electrons are further from the nucleus.", "F2 金属更活泼，非金属变弱；价电子离核更远"], ["F3 Across a period the atomic size decreases. H: the proton number increases while the number of shells stays the same, so the attraction between the nucleus and the electrons becomes stronger.", "F3 向右原子半径减小；质子数增加，壳层数不变，引力增强"], ["F4 Across a period the elements change from metal to non-metal.", "F4 由金属变为非金属"]], "", "Tip: use 'proton number' and 'attraction between nucleus and electrons' for periods."], ["Group 18: Noble Gases", "第 18 族：稀有气体", [["Helium, neon, argon, krypton, xenon, radon: monatomic gases, colourless, unreactive.", "氦氖氩氪氙氡：单原子气体、无色、不活泼"], ["Stable electron arrangements: duplet (He) or octet (others) → they neither gain, lose nor share electrons.", "稳定的电子排布：二电子/八电子"], ["Down the group: atomic size increases; melting and boiling points increase (stronger van der Waals forces between larger atoms); density increases.", "向下：原子半径、熔沸点、密度增大"], ["Uses: helium — airships and balloons, breathing mixtures for deep-sea divers (low density, non-flammable); neon — advertising lights; argon — filament light bulbs, welding shield gas (inert); krypton — photographic flash, lasers; xenon — car headlamps.", "用途：氦（气球、潜水）；氖（霓虹灯）；氩（灯泡、焊接保护气）等"], ["Why argon is used in bulbs: it is inert, so the tungsten filament does not oxidise.", "灯泡用氩：惰性，防止钨丝氧化"]], "", "Tip: link the use to the property: unreactive → protective atmosphere."], ["4.3 Uses of Group 18 Elements (F + H)", "4.3 第18族元素的用途", [["F1 Helium: filling weather balloons and airships. H: very light and does not burn.", "F1 氦：气球、飞艇；很轻且不燃烧"], ["F2 Neon: advertising lights. H: gives a bright red-orange glow when electricity passes through.", "F2 氖：霓虹灯；通电发红橙光"], ["F3 Argon: filling light bulbs and used in welding. H: inert, so it stops the hot filament or metal from reacting with oxygen.", "F3 氩：灯泡与焊接；惰性防止氧化"], ["F4 Krypton and xenon: photographic flashes and lasers.", "F4 氪、氙：闪光灯、激光"]], "", "Tip: use + reason (inert, light, glows)."], ["4.3 Why Group 18 Is Unreactive and Trends Down the Group", "4.3 为何第18族不活泼以及变化趋势", [["Group 18 atoms have a stable duplet (He) or octet electron arrangement, so they do not donate, accept or share electrons.", "第18族有稳定的二（氦）或八电子排布，不得、不失、不共用电子"], ["They exist as monatomic gases, colourless, with very low melting and boiling points because the forces between atoms are weak.", "以单原子气体存在，无色；熔沸点很低（粒子间作用力弱）"], ["Down the group: atomic size, density, melting point and boiling point increase.", "向下：原子半径、密度、熔沸点增大"], ["Boiling point increases because the larger atoms have stronger forces of attraction, so more heat energy is needed to overcome them.", "沸点升高：原子较大，引力较强，需要更多热量克服"]], "", "Tip: 'stable electron arrangement' = the reason for inertness."], ["Group 1: Alkali Metals", "第 1 族：碱金属", [["Lithium, sodium, potassium (and Rb, Cs, Fr): soft, low density (Li, Na, K float on water), low melting points, shiny when freshly cut, tarnish quickly in air.", "碱金属：软、密度小、熔点低，新切面有光泽，在空气中快速失去光泽"], ["Down the group: atomic size increases; melting point decreases; density generally increases; reactivity increases.", "向下：半径增大；熔点降低；反应性增强"], ["Reaction with water: \\(\\ce{2M + 2H2O -> 2MOH + H2}\\). Li reacts slowly; Na quickly (melts into a ball, moves, fizzes); K very vigorously with a lilac flame. The solution is alkaline (turns red litmus blue).", "与水反应：生成氢氧化物和氢气；溶液呈碱性"], ["With oxygen: \\(\\ce{4Li + O2 -> 2Li2O}\\) (also Na₂O, K₂O); with chlorine: \\(\\ce{2Na + Cl2 -> 2NaCl}\\).", "与氧、氯反应"], ["Why reactivity increases down the group: atomic size increases, the valence electron is further from the nucleus, the attraction is weaker, so it is easier to donate the electron.", "反应性增强原因：半径大，价电子受核引力弱，易失去"]], "", "Tip: store Li, Na and K in paraffin oil to prevent reaction with water and oxygen."], ["4.4 Group 1: Trends Table and Safety", "4.4 第1族：趋势数据与安全", [["Melting point (approx. °C): Li 181, Na 98, K 63, Rb 39, Cs 29 — decreases down the group because the metallic bond becomes weaker as the atoms get bigger.", "熔点（约）：Li 181、Na 98、K 63、Rb 39、Cs 29；向下降低"], ["Density (g cm⁻³, approx.): Li 0.53, Na 0.97, K 0.86, Rb 1.53, Cs 1.88 — generally increases, with potassium as an exception.", "密度（约）：Li 0.53、Na 0.97、K 0.86、Rb 1.53、Cs 1.88；大体增大，钾为例外"], ["Store in paraffin oil; use a small piece, dry the oil with filter paper, handle with tongs and wear goggles.", "存放：石蜡油；用小块，滤纸吸去油，镊子夹取，戴护目镜"], ["Do not touch with fingers and keep a safe distance when reacting with water.", "不要用手摸；反应时保持距离"]], "", "Tip: the values are approximate; follow your textbook's data."], ["4.4 Experiment: Group 1 Metals with Water (Observations)", "4.4 实验：碱金属与水（观察）", [["Method: cut a small piece, dry the oil, place it gently on water in a trough (cover with a funnel for potassium); add a few drops of phenolphthalein or litmus.", "方法：切小块，吸去油，放入水槽的水面；钾需盖漏斗；加指示剂"], ["Lithium: floats, moves slowly, fizzes gently, keeps its shape, dissolves slowly. Sodium: moves quickly, melts into a silvery ball, fizzes, may burn with a yellow flame. Potassium: very vigorous, lilac flame, may explode.", "锂：缓慢、不熔；钠：熔成小球、快速移动、可能黄焰；钾：剧烈、淡紫色火焰、可能爆炸"], ["Solution: litmus turns blue (or phenolphthalein pink) because an alkali is formed. Test the gas with a lighted splint: it burns with a 'pop' sound, so it is hydrogen: \\(\\ce{2M + 2H2O -> 2MOH + H2}\\).", "溶液呈碱性（石蕊变蓝）；气体用燃着木条检验，发出爆鸣声，是氢气"], ["Conclusion: reactivity increases down the group Li < Na < K.", "结论：反应性 Li＜Na＜K"]], "", "Tip: observation (what you see) ≠ inference (what it means)."], ["Group 17: Halogens", "第 17 族：卤素", [["Fluorine (pale yellow gas), chlorine (yellowish-green gas), bromine (reddish-brown liquid), iodine (purplish-black solid). Diatomic molecules \\(\\ce{X2}\\); poor conductors.", "颜色/状态：F₂ 淡黄气、Cl₂ 黄绿气、Br₂ 红棕液、I₂ 紫黑固"], ["Down the group: size increases; melting/boiling points increase; colour gets darker; reactivity decreases.", "向下：熔沸点升高、颜色变深、反应性减弱"], ["With water: \\(\\ce{Cl2 + H2O <=> HCl + HOCl}\\) (bleaching, acidic solution). With sodium hydroxide: \\(\\ce{Cl2 + 2NaOH -> NaCl + NaOCl + H2O}\\). With iron wool: \\(\\ce{2Fe + 3Cl2 -> 2FeCl3}\\) (Cl₂ most vigorous, I₂ slowest).", "与水、NaOH、铁反应"], ["Displacement: \\(\\ce{Cl2 + 2KBr -> 2KCl + Br2}\\) (solution turns brown): a more reactive halogen displaces a less reactive halide.", "置换反应：活泼卤素置换不活泼卤离子"], ["Why reactivity decreases down the group: the atom is bigger, the outermost shell is further from the nucleus, the attraction on an incoming electron is weaker, so it is harder to gain an electron.", "反应性减弱：半径大，对外来电子引力小，难得电子"]], "", "Tip: use the words 'attraction between nucleus and electron' in every explanation of group trends."], ["4.5 Experiment: Halogens with Iron Wool and Displacement (Observations)", "4.5 实验：卤素与铁丝、置换反应（观察）", [["Iron wool heated in chlorine: glows very brightly, brown solid (iron(III) chloride); in bromine: glows less brightly; in iodine: glows dimly or slowly — reactivity decreases down the group.", "铁丝在氯气中最亮；溴次之；碘最暗：反应性向下减弱"], ["Product: iron(III) halide, e.g. \\(\\ce{2Fe + 3Br2 -> 2FeBr3}\\).", "产物：卤化铁(III)"], ["Displacement: chlorine water + potassium bromide → brown solution (bromine formed); chlorine water + potassium iodide → brown/dark solution (iodine); bromine water + potassium iodide → darker brown.", "置换：氯水+KBr 变棕；氯水+KI 变深棕；溴水+KI 变深"], ["Ionic equation: \\(\\ce{Cl2 + 2Br- -> 2Cl- + Br2}\\); chlorine is the strongest oxidising agent of the three.", "离子方程式；氯的氧化性最强"]], "", "Tip: write the colour change in the solution."], ["4.5 Uses and Tests for Halogens", "4.5 卤素的用途与检验", [["Chlorine: kills bacteria in drinking water and swimming pools; makes bleach and PVC.", "氯：杀菌、漂白剂、PVC"], ["Fluoride (from fluorine): added to toothpaste and water to strengthen teeth.", "氟化物：牙膏与水，强化牙齿"], ["Iodine: antiseptic (tincture of iodine); bromine compounds are used in some fire retardants.", "碘：消毒剂；溴化物：阻燃剂"], ["Test for chlorine: damp blue litmus paper turns red, then is bleached (white).", "检验氯气：湿蓝石蕊试纸先变红后褪色"]], "", "Tip: hazard: halogens are toxic; use a fume cupboard."], ["Period 3 Elements", "第 3 周期元素", [["Na, Mg, Al, Si, P, S, Cl, Ar: across the period the proton number increases; the number of shells is constant (3).", "Na → Ar：质子数增加，电子层数不变"], ["Atomic radius decreases (stronger nuclear attraction on the same number of shells); electronegativity increases; metallic → non-metallic character.", "半径减小；电负性增大；金属性减弱"], ["Oxides: \\(\\ce{Na2O}\\), \\(\\ce{MgO}\\) basic; \\(\\ce{Al2O3}\\) amphoteric (reacts with acids and alkalis); \\(\\ce{SiO2}\\), \\(\\ce{P4O10}\\), \\(\\ce{SO2/SO3}\\), \\(\\ce{Cl2O7}\\) acidic.", "氧化物：碱性 → 两性 → 酸性"], ["Test amphoteric oxide: \\(\\ce{Al2O3 + 6HCl -> 2AlCl3 + 3H2O}\\); \\(\\ce{Al2O3 + 2NaOH + 3H2O -> 2NaAl(OH)4}\\).", "两性氧化物的反应"], ["Reactions with oxygen: sodium burns with a yellow flame, magnesium with a bright white flame, sulphur with a blue flame, phosphorus a white flame.", "与氧反应的现象"]], "", "Tip: the decrease in atomic radius across a period is due to the increase in the nuclear charge."], ["4.6 Trends Across Period 3 (F + H)", "4.6 第3周期的变化趋势", [["F1 Atomic size decreases from Na to Cl. H: the proton number increases but the number of shells (3) is the same, so the nucleus attracts the electrons more strongly.", "F1 Na→Cl 原子半径减小；质子数增加，壳层数不变"], ["F2 Electronegativity and non-metallic character increase. H: it is easier to gain electrons.", "F2 非金属性增强"], ["F3 The elements change from metals (Na, Mg, Al) to a metalloid (Si) to non-metals (P, S, Cl) and a noble gas (Ar).", "F3 金属→类金属→非金属→稀有气体"], ["F4 Electrical conductivity decreases from the metals to the non-metals; Ar is an unreactive monatomic gas.", "F4 导电性由金属向非金属降低；Ar 不活泼"]], "", "Tip: 'same shells, more protons' is the key explanation."], ["4.6 Oxides of Period 3: Basic, Amphoteric, Acidic", "4.6 第3周期氧化物：碱性、两性、酸性", [["Na₂O and MgO are basic oxides: they react with acids to form salts; Na₂O dissolves in water to give an alkali.", "Na₂O、MgO 碱性氧化物：与酸反应"], ["Al₂O₃ is amphoteric: it reacts with both acids and alkalis. \\(\\ce{Al2O3 + 6HCl -> 2AlCl3 + 3H2O}\\); \\(\\ce{Al2O3 + 2NaOH -> 2NaAlO2 + H2O}\\).", "Al₂O₃ 两性：与酸和碱都反应"], ["SiO₂, P₄O₁₀, SO₂ and SO₃ are acidic oxides: they react with alkalis; most dissolve in water to give acidic solutions.", "SiO₂、P₄O₁₀、SO₂、SO₃ 酸性氧化物"], ["Rule: metal oxides are basic, non-metal oxides are acidic, and aluminium oxide is amphoteric.", "规律：金属氧化物碱性，非金属氧化物酸性，氧化铝两性"]], "", "Tip: amphoteric = reacts with BOTH acid and alkali."], ["Transition Elements", "过渡元素", [["Transition elements occupy groups 3–12 (Sc to Zn, etc.): e.g. Fe, Cu, Mn, Cr, Ni, Zn.", "过渡元素位于第 3–12 族"], ["Properties: hard, strong, high melting points and densities, good conductors, form coloured compounds, variable oxidation numbers (Fe²⁺/Fe³⁺), act as catalysts, form complex ions.", "性质：硬、熔点高、密度大、导电、有色化合物、可变价、催化剂、络离子"], ["Coloured ions: \\(\\ce{Cu^2+}\\) blue; \\(\\ce{Fe^2+}\\) green; \\(\\ce{Fe^3+}\\) brown/yellow; \\(\\ce{MnO4-}\\) purple; \\(\\ce{Cr2O7^2-}\\) orange; \\(\\ce{Ni^2+}\\) green.", "离子颜色"], ["Catalysts: Fe in the Haber process; \\(\\ce{V2O5}\\) in the Contact process; Ni in hydrogenation of oils; Pt in the Ostwald process and catalytic converters; \\(\\ce{MnO2}\\) in decomposition of \\(\\ce{H2O2}\\).", "催化剂：Fe、V₂O₅、Ni、Pt、MnO₂"], ["Compared with group 1: transition metals are harder, denser, less reactive and have higher melting points.", "与第 1 族对比"]], "", "Tip: the three key words — coloured compounds, catalysts, variable oxidation numbers."], ["4.7 Properties of Transition Elements (F + H)", "4.7 过渡元素的性质", [["F1 Hard, strong, dense, with high melting and boiling points (except mercury). H: strong metallic bonds.", "F1 硬而强、密度大、熔沸点高（汞除外）"], ["F2 Good conductors of heat and electricity.", "F2 良好导热导电"], ["F3 Form coloured compounds and ions. H: Cu²⁺ blue, Fe²⁺ pale green, Fe³⁺ brown/yellow, MnO₄⁻ purple.", "F3 形成有色化合物：Cu²⁺ 蓝、Fe²⁺ 浅绿、Fe³⁺ 棕黄、MnO₄⁻ 紫"], ["F4 Show variable oxidation numbers. H: iron forms Fe²⁺ and Fe³⁺; copper forms Cu⁺ and Cu²⁺.", "F4 可变化合价：Fe²⁺、Fe³⁺；Cu⁺、Cu²⁺"], ["F5 Form complex ions and act as catalysts.", "F5 形成配离子；用作催化剂"]], "", "Tip: 'coloured compounds, variable oxidation numbers, catalysts' = the three special properties."], ["4.7 Transition Elements as Catalysts and Comparison with Group 1", "4.7 过渡元素作催化剂与和第1族的比较", [["Iron: Haber process (ammonia). Vanadium(V) oxide: Contact process (sulphuric acid). Nickel: hydrogenation of alkenes (margarine). Platinum: catalytic converter.", "铁：哈伯法；V₂O₅：接触法；镍：氢化制人造奶油；铂：催化转化器"], ["Transition elements compared with Group 1: harder, denser, higher melting point, less reactive, form coloured compounds, have more than one oxidation number and are catalysts.", "与第1族比较：更硬、密度大、熔点高、较不活泼，有色、多种化合价、催化剂"], ["Group 1 metals are soft, low density, low melting point, very reactive, form white compounds and have only the +1 oxidation number.", "第1族：软、低密度、低熔点、很活泼；白色化合物；只有+1价"]], "", "Tip: use a comparison table with at least three pairs."], ["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Group 1 and Group 17", "示例题：试卷2 A部分（第1族与第17族）", [["(a) [2] State two observations when sodium reacts with water. Scheme: moves rapidly on the water; melts into a ball; fizzes; dissolves (any 2 × 1m).", "(a)钠与水反应的两项观察"], ["(b) [2] Write the equation for potassium and water. Scheme: \\(\\ce{2K + 2H2O -> 2KOH + H2}\\) (formulae 1m; balanced 1m).", "(b)钾与水的方程式：化学式1分，配平1分"], ["(c) [3] Explain why potassium is more reactive than sodium. Scheme: potassium atom is bigger (1m); valence electron is further from the nucleus (1m); attraction is weaker so it donates the electron more easily (1m).", "(c)钾比钠活泼：原子大、价电子远、引力弱易失电子"], ["(d) [2] Which halogen is the most reactive, chlorine, bromine or iodine? Explain. Scheme: chlorine (1m); smallest atom, strongest attraction for an electron so it gains electrons most easily (1m).", "(d)氯最活泼：原子最小，对电子引力最强"]], "", "Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style."], ["Sample Paper 2 Section B: Periodic Table Essay", "示例题：试卷2 B部分（周期表）", [["(a) [6] Describe the reaction of chlorine, bromine and iodine with iron wool and compare their reactivity. Scheme: iron(III) halide formed (1m); chlorine glows brightly (1m); bromine less brightly (1m); iodine dim (1m); reactivity decreases down the group (1m); equation with chlorine (1m).", "(a)卤素与铁丝：6点"], ["(b) [6] Explain the trend across Period 3 in atomic size. Scheme: decreases from Na to Cl (1m); proton number increases (1m); number of shells is the same (1m); attraction becomes stronger (1m); electrons pulled closer (1m); example (1m).", "(b)第3周期原子半径"], ["(c) [8] Compare sodium and iron in three physical and two chemical properties. Scheme: hardness; melting point; density; reactivity with water; compounds (any 8 comparison points; each with both elements).", "(c)比较钠与铁：8个比较点"]], "", "Tip: self-made practice question; marks are an example; follow your teacher's scheme."], ["Common Mistakes and Exam Tips", "常见错误与考试提示", [["Saying 'group 17 elements gain electrons easily' without explaining the trend using atomic size.", "没用原子大小解释趋势"], ["Stating that reactivity increases down both group 1 and group 17.", "第 1 族向下增强，第 17 族向下减弱"], ["Wrong flame colour: potassium is lilac, sodium is yellow, lithium is crimson.", "焰色：钾紫、钠黄、锂红"], ["Confusing period (shells) and group (valence electrons).", "混淆周期和族"], ["Forgetting that noble gases are monatomic.", "稀有气体是单原子分子"]], "", "Tip: for trend explanations: size → distance to nucleus → attraction → ease of losing/gaining an electron."], ["Uji Diri", "自测", [["S: Why are noble gases unreactive? J: They have stable duplet or octet electron arrangements.", "问：稀有气体为何不活泼？答：已有稳定的二/八电子排布"], ["S: Why is potassium more reactive than sodium? J: Its atom is larger, so the valence electron is further from the nucleus and is donated more easily.", "问：钾为何比钠活泼？答：半径大，价电子更远，易失去"], ["S: What is observed when chlorine water is added to potassium bromide? J: The colourless solution turns brown/orange because bromine is formed.", "问：氯水加入溴化钾？答：溶液变棕橙色（生成溴）"], ["S: Name two properties of transition elements. J: Form coloured compounds; act as catalysts.", "问：过渡元素的两个性质？答：有色化合物；催化剂"], ["S: In which group and period is the element with electron arrangement 2.8.5? J: Group 15, period 3.", "问：2.8.5 在哪个族哪个周期？答：第 15 族第 3 周期"]], "", ""]], "kim|T4-5": [["Why Do Atoms Form Chemical Bonds?", "原子为何形成化学键？", [["Atoms of noble gases are stable because they have a duplet (2) or octet (8) of valence electrons. Other atoms achieve this by gaining, losing or sharing electrons.", "其他原子通过得失或共用电子，达到稳定结构"], ["Ionic bond: transfer of electrons between a metal and a non-metal, forming ions. Covalent bond: sharing of electrons between non-metal atoms.", "离子键：金属与非金属转移电子；共价键：非金属共用电子"], ["Chemical bonds hold atoms in compounds: ionic, covalent, dative (coordinate), hydrogen bond (intermolecular), metallic.", "键的类型"], ["Compounds have properties different from their elements: sodium (reactive metal) + chlorine (poisonous gas) → sodium chloride (table salt).", "化合物性质与元素不同"], ["Draw electron arrangement diagrams to show how bonds form and show only the valence electrons for covalent molecules.", "画电子排布图时只画价电子"]], "", "Tip: the first step of every bonding explanation is to write the electron arrangement."], ["5.1 Reaching a Stable Electron Arrangement: Worked Examples", "5.1 达到稳定电子排布：例题", [["Atoms of Group 18 already have a stable duplet or octet, so they do not form compounds easily; other atoms bond to reach a stable arrangement.", "第18族已稳定；其他原子通过成键达到稳定"], ["Metals donate electrons: Na (2.8.1) → Na⁺ (2.8); Mg (2.8.2) → Mg²⁺ (2.8).", "金属失电子：Na→Na⁺；Mg→Mg²⁺"], ["Non-metals accept electrons: Cl (2.8.7) → Cl⁻ (2.8.8); O (2.6) → O²⁻ (2.8).", "非金属得电子：Cl→Cl⁻；O→O²⁻"], ["Non-metals share electrons: H (1) shares 1; O (2.6) shares 2; N (2.5) shares 3; C (2.4) shares 4.", "非金属共用电子：H共用1、O共用2、N共用3、C共用4"], ["Rule: metal + non-metal → ionic bond (transfer); non-metal + non-metal → covalent bond (sharing).", "规律：金属＋非金属→离子键；非金属＋非金属→共价键"]], "", "Tip: write the electron arrangement before and after bonding."], ["Ionic Bond", "离子键", [["A metal atom donates electrons to form a positive ion (cation); a non-metal atom accepts electrons to form a negative ion (anion). The strong electrostatic attraction between the oppositely charged ions is the ionic bond.", "金属失电子成阳离子，非金属得电子成阴离子；静电引力即离子键"], ["Sodium chloride: Na 2.8.1 → \\(\\ce{Na+}\\) 2.8 (loses 1 e⁻); Cl 2.8.7 → \\(\\ce{Cl-}\\) 2.8.8 (gains 1 e⁻).", "NaCl 的形成"], ["Magnesium oxide: Mg 2.8.2 loses 2 e⁻ → \\(\\ce{Mg^2+}\\); O 2.6 gains 2 e⁻ → \\(\\ce{O^2-}\\).", "MgO 的形成"], ["Calcium chloride: one Ca (2.8.8.2) gives one electron each to two Cl atoms → \\(\\ce{CaCl2}\\).", "CaCl₂"], ["Ions are arranged in a regular giant ionic lattice; ionic compounds are solids.", "巨型离子晶格"]], "", "Tip: show the transfer of electrons with arrows and include charges on the ions in the diagram."], ["5.2 Formation of Ionic Compounds: Step by Step", "5.2 离子化合物的形成：步骤", [["Step 1: write the electron arrangement of each atom. Step 2: show the metal donating and the non-metal accepting electrons. Step 3: write the ions with charges and their new arrangements. Step 4: electrostatic attraction between the opposite ions = ionic bond.", "步骤：写电子排布→电子转移→写离子与新排布→静电引力＝离子键"], ["NaCl: Na (2.8.1) donates 1 electron → Na⁺ (2.8); Cl (2.8.7) accepts 1 electron → Cl⁻ (2.8.8).", "NaCl：Na⁺ 2.8；Cl⁻ 2.8.8"], ["\\(\\ce{MgCl2}\\): Mg (2.8.2) donates 2 electrons, one to each of two Cl atoms → Mg²⁺ and 2Cl⁻.", "MgCl₂：Mg 给两个Cl各1个电子"], ["\\(\\ce{MgO}\\): Mg (2.8.2) donates 2 electrons → Mg²⁺ (2.8); O (2.6) accepts 2 → O²⁻ (2.8). \\(\\ce{Na2O}\\): two Na atoms give 1 electron each to one O atom.", "MgO：Mg²⁺ 与 O²⁻；Na₂O：两个Na各给1个电子"]], "", "Tip: the answer needs the transfer, the ions and the electrostatic attraction (3 marks)."], ["5.2 Properties of Ionic Compounds (F + H)", "5.2 离子化合物的性质", [["F1 High melting and boiling points. H: strong electrostatic forces between the oppositely charged ions need a lot of heat energy to overcome.", "F1 熔沸点高；离子间静电引力强"], ["F2 Conduct electricity in the molten or aqueous state but not as solids. H: the ions move freely when molten or dissolved; in a solid the ions are held in fixed positions.", "F2 熔融或水溶液导电，固体不导电；离子能自由移动"], ["F3 Soluble in water, insoluble in organic solvents. H: water molecules can separate the ions.", "F3 溶于水，不溶于有机溶剂"], ["F4 Hard but brittle. H: the ions form a rigid lattice; a blow shifts the layers so like charges repel and the crystal breaks.", "F4 硬而脆；受力后同电荷互斥而断裂"]], "", "Tip: always give the reason (H) after each property."], ["Covalent Bond", "共价键", [["Non-metal atoms share pairs of electrons to achieve a stable duplet or octet. Single bond (1 pair), double bond (2 pairs), triple bond (3 pairs).", "共用电子对：单键、双键、三键"], ["Examples: \\(\\ce{H2}\\) (single), \\(\\ce{Cl2}\\), \\(\\ce{HCl}\\), \\(\\ce{H2O}\\), \\(\\ce{NH3}\\), \\(\\ce{CH4}\\), \\(\\ce{O2}\\) (double), \\(\\ce{CO2}\\) (two double), \\(\\ce{N2}\\) (triple).", "例子"], ["Simple molecular structure: molecules held by weak intermolecular forces (van der Waals) — low melting/boiling point.", "简单分子结构：分子间作用力弱，熔沸点低"], ["Draw the diagrams: each shared pair shown as overlapping shells; for \\(\\ce{CO2}\\): O=C=O with lone pairs on oxygen.", "画重叠电子壳层图"], ["Number of covalent bonds: H 1, O 2, N 3, C 4, halogens 1.", "共价数：H1、O2、N3、C4"]], "", "Tip: always check each atom has 8 electrons (2 for hydrogen) around it."], ["5.3 Formation of Covalent Molecules", "5.3 共价分子的形成", [["\\(\\ce{H2O}\\): O (2.6) shares 2 electrons with two H atoms → two single bonds; O has 2 lone pairs.", "H₂O：氧与两个氢共用；氧有2对孤对电子"], ["\\(\\ce{NH3}\\): N (2.5) shares 3 electrons with three H atoms; N keeps 1 lone pair. \\(\\ce{CH4}\\): C (2.4) shares 4 electrons with four H atoms.", "NH₃：氮共用3个电子；CH₄：碳共用4个"], ["\\(\\ce{CO2}\\): C forms two double bonds, O=C=O; each O has 2 lone pairs.", "CO₂：两个双键"], ["\\(\\ce{O2}\\): double bond; \\(\\ce{N2}\\): triple bond; \\(\\ce{HCl}\\) and \\(\\ce{Cl2}\\): single bond.", "O₂ 双键；N₂ 三键；HCl、Cl₂ 单键"]], "", "Tip: after drawing, count 8 electrons (2 for H) around each atom."], ["5.3 Properties of Covalent Compounds (F + H)", "5.3 共价化合物的性质", [["F1 Low melting and boiling points. H: the forces between molecules are weak, so little heat energy is needed to overcome them (the covalent bonds do not break).", "F1 熔沸点低；分子间作用力弱，共价键不断裂"], ["F2 Do not conduct electricity in any state. H: they consist of neutral molecules, with no freely moving ions or electrons.", "F2 任何状态都不导电；由中性分子组成"], ["F3 Usually insoluble in water but soluble in organic solvents such as propanone.", "F3 通常不溶于水，溶于有机溶剂"], ["Exceptions: HCl and \\(\\ce{NH3}\\) dissolve in water and form ions, so the solutions conduct electricity; glucose dissolves but does not conduct.", "例外：HCl、NH₃ 溶于水形成离子，溶液导电"]], "", "Tip: the covalent bond is strong; the force BETWEEN molecules is weak."], ["Hydrogen Bond", "氢键", [["Hydrogen bond: a strong intermolecular attraction between a hydrogen atom bonded to a very electronegative atom (N, O or F) and the lone pair on the N, O or F of another molecule.", "氢键：H–N/O/F 与另一分子的 N/O/F 孤对电子之间的较强吸引力"], ["Examples: water, ammonia, hydrogen fluoride, alcohols.", "水、氨、氟化氢、醇"], ["Effects: unusually high boiling points of water (100 °C) compared with \\(\\ce{H2S}\\); ice is less dense than liquid water (open lattice held by hydrogen bonds) so it floats; ammonia is very soluble in water.", "影响：水沸点高；冰比水轻；氨易溶于水"], ["Hydrogen bonds are weaker than covalent bonds but stronger than van der Waals forces.", "强弱：共价键 > 氢键 > 范德华力"], ["Hydrogen bonds hold the two strands of DNA together.", "氢键使 DNA 双链相连"]], "", "Tip: draw the hydrogen bond as a dotted line between H and the lone pair of the neighbouring molecule."], ["5.4 Hydrogen Bonds: Effects on Water (F + H)", "5.4 氢键对水的影响", [["F1 A hydrogen bond is a force of attraction between a hydrogen atom bonded to N, O or F and a lone pair on another N, O or F atom of a neighbouring molecule.", "F1 氢键：与N、O、F相连的氢和邻近分子的N、O、F孤对电子之间的吸引力"], ["F2 Water has a high boiling point (100 °C) compared with \\(\\ce{H2S}\\). H: extra heat energy is needed to break the hydrogen bonds.", "F2 水沸点高；需要额外热量破坏氢键"], ["F3 Ice is less dense than water. H: in ice the molecules are held in an open lattice by hydrogen bonds, so ice floats.", "F3 冰比水轻；冰中分子以氢键形成松散晶格"], ["F4 Other examples: \\(\\ce{NH3}\\) and HF also form hydrogen bonds, and ammonia is very soluble in water.", "F4 其他例子：NH₃、HF；氨极易溶于水"]], "", "Tip: hydrogen bond = intermolecular force, not a bond inside the molecule."], ["Dative (Coordinate) Bond and Metallic Bond", "配位键与金属键", [["Dative bond: a covalent bond in which both shared electrons come from one atom (the donor, which has a lone pair) to an atom with an empty orbital.", "配位键：共用电子对由同一原子提供"], ["Examples: ammonium ion \\(\\ce{NH4+}\\) (\\(\\ce{NH3}\\) donates its lone pair to \\(\\ce{H+}\\)); oxonium ion \\(\\ce{H3O+}\\) (\\(\\ce{H2O}\\) donates to \\(\\ce{H+}\\)).", "例：NH₄⁺、H₃O⁺"], ["Metallic bond: the electrostatic attraction between the positive metal ions and the 'sea' of delocalised valence electrons.", "金属键：金属阳离子与离域电子海之间的引力"], ["Properties of metals: conduct electricity (free electrons carry charge), malleable and ductile (layers of ions slide), high melting points (strong metallic bonds), shiny.", "金属性质：导电、可延展、熔点高"], ["Strength increases with the number of valence electrons and smaller ionic size (Mg stronger than Na).", "价电子越多、离子越小，金属键越强"]], "", "Tip: use the words 'sea of delocalised electrons' and 'layers of atoms can slide over each other'."], ["5.5 Dative Bond: Formation of NH₄⁺ and H₃O⁺", "5.5 配位键：NH₄⁺ 与 H₃O⁺ 的形成", [["A dative (coordinate) bond is a covalent bond in which both shared electrons come from one atom.", "配位键：共用的两个电子都来自同一个原子"], ["\\(\\ce{NH3 + H+ -> NH4+}\\): the lone pair on N is donated to H⁺, which has no electrons.", "NH₃ 的孤对电子给了没有电子的 H⁺"], ["\\(\\ce{H2O + H+ -> H3O+}\\): a lone pair on O is donated to H⁺.", "H₂O 的孤对电子给了 H⁺"], ["Once formed, the dative bond is identical to the other bonds in the ion; it is drawn as an arrow from the donor atom.", "形成后与其他键无区别；用箭头指向接受者"]], "", "Tip: the donor has a lone pair; the acceptor has an empty shell."], ["5.6 Metallic Bond and Properties of Metals (F + H)", "5.6 金属键与金属的性质", [["F1 A metallic bond is the electrostatic attraction between positive metal ions and a 'sea' of delocalised valence electrons.", "F1 金属键：金属正离子与自由电子之间的静电引力"], ["F2 Good conductors of electricity and heat. H: the delocalised electrons move freely.", "F2 导电导热好；自由电子移动"], ["F3 Malleable and ductile. H: the layers of ions slide over one another while the electrons keep the ions bonded.", "F3 延展性好；离子层可滑动，电子保持结合"], ["F4 High melting point, dense and shiny. H: the metallic bond is strong.", "F4 熔点高、密度大、有光泽；金属键强"], ["Alloys are harder because atoms of different sizes stop the layers from sliding.", "合金更硬：不同大小的原子阻止层滑动"]], "", "Tip: malleable answer needs 'layers slide' and 'electrons still hold them'."], ["Ionic and Covalent Compounds: Properties", "离子与共价化合物的性质", [["Melting/boiling point: ionic — high (strong electrostatic forces need much energy); covalent (simple molecules) — low (weak intermolecular forces).", "熔沸点：离子高；共价低"], ["Electrical conductivity: ionic — conduct when molten or aqueous (free-moving ions), not as solids; covalent — do not conduct (no ions or free electrons), except graphite/acids in water.", "导电：离子化合物熔融/水溶液导电；共价不导电"], ["Solubility: ionic — dissolve in water, not in organic solvents; covalent — usually dissolve in organic solvents (e.g. naphthalene in methylbenzene), not water.", "溶解：离子易溶水；共价易溶有机溶剂"], ["Volatility: covalent compounds are more volatile. Physical state at room temperature: ionic solids; covalent gases, liquids or solids.", "挥发性：共价较高"], ["Giant covalent structures (diamond, graphite, silicon dioxide) are exceptions: very high melting points.", "例外：巨型共价（金刚石、石墨）熔点高"]], "", "Tip: explain by the type of particles and the forces that must be overcome."], ["5.7 Experiment: Electrical Conductivity of Ionic and Covalent Compounds", "5.7 实验：离子与共价化合物的导电性", [["Apparatus: carbon electrodes, battery, bulb or ammeter, crucible, Bunsen burner (fume cupboard for lead(II) bromide).", "仪器：碳电极、电池、灯泡或安培计、坩埚、本生灯（溴化铅在通风橱）"], ["Ionic: solid lead(II) bromide — bulb does not light; molten lead(II) bromide — bulb lights; sodium chloride solution — bulb lights.", "离子化合物：固体溴化铅不亮；熔融亮；NaCl溶液亮"], ["Covalent: naphthalene (solid and molten), ethanol, tetrachloromethane — bulb does not light.", "共价：萘（固/熔）、乙醇、四氯化碳均不亮"], ["Conclusion: ionic compounds conduct electricity in the molten or aqueous state because of mobile ions; covalent compounds do not because they have no ions.", "结论：离子化合物熔融/水溶液因有可移动离子导电；共价没有离子不导电"]], "", "Tip: state the state (solid, molten, aqueous) with every observation."], ["5.7 Experiment: Melting Point and Solubility", "5.7 实验：熔点与溶解性", [["Melting point: sodium chloride melts at about 801 °C; naphthalene melts at about 80 °C — ionic compounds have much higher melting points.", "熔点：NaCl约801 °C；萘约80 °C"], ["Solubility test: add a spatula of each solid to water and to an organic solvent such as propanone, shake and observe.", "溶解性：加入水与有机溶剂，摇匀观察"], ["Ionic (NaCl): dissolves in water, does not dissolve in propanone. Covalent (naphthalene): does not dissolve in water, dissolves in propanone.", "NaCl溶于水不溶于丙酮；萘溶于丙酮不溶于水"], ["Use separate clean test tubes; the organic solvent is flammable, so keep it away from flame.", "用干净试管；有机溶剂易燃，远离火源"]], "", "Tip: variables: manipulated = type of compound; responding = solubility; fixed = amount and solvent volume."], ["Experiment Questions: Conductivity and Melting", "实验题：导电性与熔点", [["Experiment: test the conductivity of naphthalene, lead(II) bromide and sodium chloride in different states with a bulb and carbon electrodes.", "实验：用灯泡和碳电极测导电性"], ["Solid ionic compound: no conduction — ions are in fixed positions. Molten/aqueous: bulb lights — ions move freely.", "固体不导电；熔融/水溶液导电"], ["Naphthalene (covalent): does not conduct in solid or molten state — consists of neutral molecules.", "萘：不导电，只有中性分子"], ["Heating naphthalene melts at about 80 °C easily, but sodium chloride needs 801 °C: why? Weak intermolecular forces vs strong ionic bonds.", "萘约 80 °C 熔化；NaCl 801 °C：分子间力 vs 离子键"], ["Precaution: use a water bath for naphthalene (flammable).", "注意：萘易燃，用水浴"]], "", "Tip: 'because there are no freely moving ions' is the standard answer for solid ionic compounds."], ["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Chemical Bonds", "示例题：试卷2 A部分（化学键）", [["Element X has electron arrangement 2.8.1 and element Y has 2.8.7.", "X为2.8.1；Y为2.8.7"], ["(a) [1] State the group of X. Scheme: Group 1. (b) [2] Write the formula of the compound formed and the type of bond. Scheme: XY (1m); ionic bond (1m).", "(a)第1族；(b)XY；离子键"], ["(c) [3] Explain how the compound is formed. Scheme: atom X donates 1 electron to form X⁺ (2.8) (1m); atom Y accepts 1 electron to form Y⁻ (2.8.8) (1m); electrostatic attraction between the ions (1m).", "(c)形成：给电子、得电子、静电引力"], ["(d) [2] State two properties of the compound. Scheme: high melting point; conducts electricity in the molten or aqueous state; soluble in water (any 2 × 1m).", "(d)两项性质"]], "", "Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style."], ["Sample Paper 2 Section B: Ionic and Covalent Compounds (Essay)", "示例题：试卷2 B部分（离子与共价化合物）", [["(a) [10] Compare ionic and covalent compounds in formation of the bond, melting point, electrical conductivity and solubility. Scheme: ionic — electron transfer (1m), high melting point (1m), conducts when molten/aqueous (1m), soluble in water (1m); covalent — electron sharing (1m), low melting point (1m), does not conduct (1m), soluble in organic solvents (1m); reasons for the differences (2m).", "(a)比较：离子与共价各4点＋理由2分"], ["(b) [10] Describe an experiment to show that an ionic compound conducts electricity only when molten or in solution. Scheme: aim; apparatus (carbon electrodes, bulb, battery); materials (lead(II) bromide); procedure (test the solid, then melt it and test again; precautions in the fume cupboard); observations (solid: bulb off; molten: bulb on); conclusion with the reason (mobile ions) (any 10 points).", "(b)描述实验：目的、仪器、步骤、观察、结论"]], "", "Tip: self-made practice question; marks are an example, ask your teacher for the real breakdown."], ["Common Mistakes", "常见错误", [["Mistake: saying 'covalent bonds break when a molecular compound melts' — only the intermolecular forces are overcome.", "错误：共价化合物熔化时断的是分子间力，不是共价键"], ["Mistake: forgetting the charge when drawing ions or showing electrons from only one atom in a dative bond.", "错误：忘了离子电荷"]], "", ""], ["Uji Diri", "自测", [["S: Draw/describe the bonding in magnesium chloride. J: Mg (2.8.2) donates 2 electrons, one each to two Cl atoms (2.8.7) → \\(\\ce{Mg^2+}\\) and 2 \\(\\ce{Cl-}\\); formula \\(\\ce{MgCl2}\\).", "问：描述 MgCl₂ 成键。答：Mg 失 2 电子，分别给两个 Cl"], ["S: Why does ice float on water? J: Hydrogen bonds hold the molecules in an open lattice, making ice less dense.", "问：冰为何浮在水上？答：氢键形成疏松晶格，密度小"], ["S: Why do metals conduct electricity? J: Delocalised electrons move freely and carry charge.", "问：金属为何导电？答：离域电子自由移动"]], "", ""]], "kim|T4-6": [["The Role of Water in Acidity and Alkalinity", "水在酸碱性中的作用", [["An acid is a chemical substance that ionises in water to produce hydrogen ions \\(\\ce{H+}\\) (hydroxonium ions \\(\\ce{H3O+}\\)). An alkali is a base that dissolves in water and ionises to produce hydroxide ions \\(\\ce{OH-}\\).", "酸：在水中电离出 H⁺；碱（碱液）：在水中电离出 OH⁻"], ["Examples: \\(\\ce{HCl -> H+ + Cl-}\\); \\(\\ce{NaOH -> Na+ + OH-}\\); ammonia: \\(\\ce{NH3 + H2O <=> NH4+ + OH-}\\).", "电离方程式"], ["Water is needed: dry hydrogen chloride gas or glacial ethanoic acid does not change dry blue litmus paper; in methylbenzene the acid does not ionise, so it shows no acidic properties. Add water → ions form → acidic properties appear.", "需要水：在无水或有机溶剂中酸不电离，无酸性"], ["Acidic properties are due to \\(\\ce{H+}\\); alkaline properties are due to \\(\\ce{OH-}\\). Acids: sour taste, turn blue litmus red, pH < 7. Alkalis: bitter, soapy, turn red litmus blue, pH > 7.", "酸性来自 H⁺，碱性来自 OH⁻"], ["Basicity: HCl, \\(\\ce{HNO3}\\) are monoprotic; \\(\\ce{H2SO4}\\) is diprotic (\\(\\ce{H2SO4 -> 2H+ + SO4^2-}\\)); \\(\\ce{H3PO4}\\) triprotic.", "酸的元数：一元、二元、三元"]], "", "Tip: 'in the presence of water the acid ionises to produce hydrogen ions'."], ["6.1 Experiment: The Role of Water in Showing Acidity and Alkalinity", "6.1 实验：水在显示酸碱性中的作用", [["Hydrogen chloride dissolved in water: turns blue litmus paper red, reacts with magnesium and zinc (bubbles), reacts with calcium carbonate.", "氯化氢溶于水：蓝石蕊变红，与镁、锌反应，与碳酸钙反应"], ["Hydrogen chloride dissolved in methylbenzene (an organic solvent) or dry hydrogen chloride gas: no change to dry blue litmus paper and no reaction with metals or carbonates.", "氯化氢溶于甲苯或干燥氯化氢气体：干蓝石蕊不变，不与金属、碳酸盐反应"], ["Ammonia dissolved in water turns red litmus paper blue; ammonia dissolved in propanone does not.", "氨溶于水使红石蕊变蓝；溶于丙酮则不变"], ["Conclusion: water is needed for acidic and alkaline properties because water allows the substance to ionise: HCl gives H⁺ ions, ammonia gives OH⁻ ions. In organic solvents the substance remains as molecules with no ions.", "结论：水使物质电离：HCl 产生 H⁺；氨产生 OH⁻；有机溶剂中只有分子，没有离子"]], "", "Tip: 'ionises in water to produce H⁺' is the key phrase."], ["6.1 Acids, Alkalis, Basicity and Ionisation Equations", "6.1 酸、碱、碱度与电离方程式", [["Acid: a substance that ionises in water to produce hydrogen ions (H⁺, present as hydroxonium ions H₃O⁺). Alkali: a substance that ionises in water to produce hydroxide ions (OH⁻).", "酸：在水中电离产生 H⁺；碱：在水中电离产生 OH⁻"], ["Basicity = number of H⁺ ions one molecule of the acid produces: monoprotic HCl, HNO₃, CH₃COOH (1); diprotic H₂SO₄ (2); triprotic H₃PO₄ (3).", "碱度（元数）：一元 HCl、HNO₃、CH₃COOH；二元 H₂SO₄；三元 H₃PO₄"], ["\\(\\ce{HCl -> H+ + Cl-}\\); \\(\\ce{H2SO4 -> 2H+ + SO4^2-}\\); \\(\\ce{NaOH -> Na+ + OH-}\\); \\(\\ce{CH3COOH <=> H+ + CH3COO-}\\) (weak acid, reversible).", "电离方程式：强酸用 →；弱酸用 ⇌"], ["Alkalis: NaOH, KOH, Ca(OH)₂ and ammonia solution. Bases that dissolve in water are alkalis.", "碱：NaOH、KOH、Ca(OH)₂、氨水；可溶于水的碱称碱液"]], "", "Tip: write the ionisation equation when the question asks you to explain."], ["The pH Scale", "pH 值", [["pH is a measure of the concentration of hydrogen ions: \\(\\text{pH}=-\\log_{10}[\\ce{H+}]\\). pH 0–6 acidic; 7 neutral; 8–14 alkaline.", "pH = −log[H⁺]"], ["Lower pH → higher \\(\\ce{H+}\\) concentration. A change of one pH unit changes [H⁺] by a factor of 10.", "pH 差 1，[H⁺] 差 10 倍"], ["Measure: universal indicator (colour chart), pH paper, pH meter (digital, most accurate).", "测量：万能指示剂、pH 试纸、pH 计"], ["Examples: 0.1 mol dm⁻³ HCl: [H⁺] = 0.1 → pH 1; 0.01 mol dm⁻³ HCl → pH 2; 0.1 mol dm⁻³ NaOH: pOH = 1 → pH 13.", "算例：0.1 mol/dm³ HCl pH=1；0.1 mol/dm³ NaOH pH=13"], ["Universal indicator colours: red (pH 1–3), orange (4), yellow (5), green (7), blue (9–11), purple (12–14).", "万能指示剂颜色"]], "", "Tip: for strong monoprotic acids pH = −log(concentration). For \\(\\ce{H2SO4}\\), [H⁺] = 2 × concentration."], ["6.2 Worked Examples: pH and Hydrogen Ion Concentration", "6.2 例题：pH 与氢离子浓度", [["pH = −log₁₀[H⁺]; the lower the pH, the higher the concentration of H⁺ ions.", "pH = −log[H⁺]；pH越低，H⁺浓度越高"], ["0.1 mol dm⁻³ HCl: [H⁺] = 0.1 → pH = 1. 0.01 mol dm⁻³ HCl: pH = 2.", "0.1 mol/dm³ HCl：pH 1；0.01：pH 2"], ["0.05 mol dm⁻³ H₂SO₄ (diprotic): [H⁺] = 2 × 0.05 = 0.10 mol dm⁻³ → pH = 1.", "0.05 mol/dm³ H₂SO₄：[H⁺]=0.10，pH 1"], ["Given pH 3: [H⁺] = 1 × 10⁻³ mol dm⁻³. A change of 1 pH unit changes [H⁺] by 10 times: pH 2 has 100 times the H⁺ of pH 4.", "pH 3：[H⁺]=1×10⁻³；差1个单位＝10倍"], ["pH < 7 acidic; pH = 7 neutral; pH > 7 alkaline; 0.1 mol dm⁻³ NaOH has a pH of about 13.", "pH＜7酸性；＝7中性；＞7碱性；0.1 mol/dm³ NaOH 约 pH 13"]], "", "Tip: for diprotic acids double the molarity to get [H⁺]."], ["6.2 Measuring pH: Indicators and pH Meter", "6.2 测量 pH：指示剂与 pH 计", [["Universal indicator (approx.): red (pH 1–3), orange/yellow (4–6), green (7), blue (8–11), purple (12–14).", "通用指示剂（约）：红、橙黄、绿、蓝、紫"], ["Litmus: red in acid, blue in alkali. Methyl orange: red in acid, yellow in alkali. Phenolphthalein: colourless in acid, pink in alkali.", "石蕊：酸红碱蓝；甲基橙：酸红碱黄；酚酞：酸无色碱粉红"], ["A pH meter gives an accurate digital reading; rinse the electrode with distilled water between measurements.", "pH计读数准确；每次测量间用蒸馏水冲洗电极"], ["Universal indicator gives an approximate pH; litmus only shows whether the solution is acidic or alkaline.", "通用指示剂给出近似pH；石蕊只能判断酸碱"]], "", "Tip: say which indicator and the colour for acid and alkali."], ["Strength of Acids and Alkalis", "酸和碱的强度", [["Strong acid: ionises completely in water (HCl, \\(\\ce{HNO3}\\), \\(\\ce{H2SO4}\\)) — high concentration of \\(\\ce{H+}\\), low pH. Weak acid: partially ionises (ethanoic acid \\(\\ce{CH3COOH}\\), \\(\\ce{H2CO3}\\)) — equilibrium.", "强酸完全电离；弱酸部分电离"], ["Strong alkali: ionises completely (NaOH, KOH); weak alkali: partially (\\(\\ce{NH3}\\) in water).", "强碱 NaOH、KOH；弱碱 NH₃"], ["Same concentration comparison: strong acid has lower pH, higher conductivity, reacts faster with magnesium/carbonate than a weak acid.", "同浓度：强酸 pH 更低、导电更强、反应更快"], ["Strength (degree of ionisation) is NOT the same as concentration (amount of solute per dm³). A dilute strong acid can have a higher pH than a concentrated weak acid.", "强度 ≠ 浓度"], ["Experiment: compare 0.1 mol dm⁻³ HCl and 0.1 mol dm⁻³ ethanoic acid: pH 1 vs about 3; reaction with Mg is vigorous vs slow.", "实验：同浓度 HCl 与乙酸比较"]], "", "Tip: write 'ionises completely' / 'ionises partially' — do not say 'dissociates a lot'."], ["6.3 Experiment: Comparing Strong and Weak Acids and Alkalis", "6.3 实验：比较强酸、弱酸与强碱、弱碱", [["Use the same concentration (0.1 mol dm⁻³) and the same volume: HCl (strong acid) and ethanoic acid (weak acid); NaOH (strong alkali) and ammonia solution (weak alkali).", "同浓度同体积：HCl 与乙酸；NaOH 与氨水"], ["pH: HCl about 1; ethanoic acid about 3; NaOH about 13; ammonia solution about 11.", "pH：HCl约1；乙酸约3；NaOH约13；氨水约11"], ["Electrical conductivity: the bulb is brighter for HCl and NaOH. Reaction with magnesium: HCl bubbles vigorously; ethanoic acid slowly.", "导电性：HCl、NaOH 灯更亮；与镁反应：HCl 剧烈，乙酸缓慢"], ["Conclusion: HCl and NaOH are strong (higher concentration of ions); ethanoic acid and ammonia are weak.", "结论：HCl、NaOH 是强；乙酸、氨是弱"]], "", "Tip: same concentration, same volume = fair test."], ["6.3 Explaining Strength: Complete and Partial Ionisation (F + H)", "6.3 解释强弱：完全与部分电离", [["F1 A strong acid ionises completely in water. H: it produces a high concentration of H⁺ ions, so the pH is low (HCl, HNO₃, H₂SO₄).", "F1 强酸完全电离；H⁺浓度高，pH低"], ["F2 A weak acid ionises partially in water. H: only a few molecules form ions (reversible), so the concentration of H⁺ ions is lower and the pH is higher (CH₃COOH, H₂CO₃).", "F2 弱酸部分电离；H⁺浓度低，pH较高"], ["F3 A strong alkali ionises completely, producing a high concentration of OH⁻ ions (NaOH, KOH); a weak alkali ionises partially (ammonia solution).", "F3 强碱完全电离；弱碱部分电离"], ["F4 Strength is the degree of ionisation; concentration is the amount of solute per dm³ — a concentrated weak acid is not the same as a strong acid.", "F4 强度＝电离程度；浓度＝每 dm³ 溶质量，两者不同"]], "", "Tip: never say strong = concentrated."], ["Chemical Properties of Acids and Alkalis", "酸和碱的化学性质", [["Acid + metal (above hydrogen) → salt + hydrogen: \\(\\ce{Mg + 2HCl -> MgCl2 + H2}\\). Test: lighted splint — 'pop' sound.", "酸 + 金属 → 盐 + H₂；点燃木条发出爆鸣"], ["Acid + base/metal oxide → salt + water: \\(\\ce{CuO + H2SO4 -> CuSO4 + H2O}\\). Acid + alkali → salt + water.", "酸 + 碱 → 盐 + 水"], ["Acid + metal carbonate → salt + water + carbon dioxide: \\(\\ce{CaCO3 + 2HCl -> CaCl2 + H2O + CO2}\\). Test: limewater turns cloudy.", "酸 + 碳酸盐 → 盐 + 水 + CO₂；石灰水变浑浊"], ["Alkali + acid → salt + water; alkali + ammonium salt → salt + water + ammonia (warm; pungent gas turns damp red litmus blue): \\(\\ce{NaOH + NH4Cl -> NaCl + H2O + NH3}\\).", "碱 + 铵盐 → 氨气"], ["Alkali + metal ions → insoluble metal hydroxide precipitate: \\(\\ce{Cu^2+ + 2OH- -> Cu(OH)2}\\) (blue).", "碱 + 金属离子 → 氢氧化物沉淀"]], "", "Tip: write the test and the observation for each gas."], ["6.4 Experiments: Reactions of Acids and Alkalis (Observations)", "6.4 实验：酸和碱的反应（观察）", [["Acid + magnesium: bubbles, magnesium dissolves, gas gives a 'pop' with a lighted splint (hydrogen). Copper and silver do not react because they are below hydrogen.", "酸＋镁：冒泡，镁溶解，爆鸣声（氢）；铜、银不反应"], ["Acid + copper(II) oxide (warm): black solid dissolves, blue solution. Acid + calcium carbonate: bubbles, limewater turns cloudy (CO₂).", "酸＋氧化铜：黑色溶解，蓝色溶液；酸＋碳酸钙：冒泡，石灰水变浑浊"], ["Alkali + ammonium chloride (warm): pungent gas, damp red litmus turns blue (ammonia).", "碱＋氯化铵（加热）：刺激性气体，湿红石蕊变蓝"], ["Alkali + copper(II) sulphate: blue precipitate of copper(II) hydroxide: \\(\\ce{Cu^2+ + 2OH- -> Cu(OH)2}\\).", "碱＋硫酸铜：蓝色沉淀"]], "", "Tip: write observation, then name the product."], ["Concentration of Aqueous Solutions", "水溶液的浓度", [["Concentration is the quantity of solute dissolved in 1 dm³ of solution: g dm⁻³ or mol dm⁻³ (molarity M).", "浓度：每 dm³ 溶液中的溶质量"], ["\\(M=\\dfrac{n}{V}\\) (V in dm³); \\(n=MV/1000\\) if V in cm³; mol dm⁻³ = g dm⁻³ ÷ molar mass.", "M = n/V；mol/dm³ = (g/dm³)/M"], ["Dilution: \\(M_1V_1=M_2V_2\\) (moles of solute remain constant).", "稀释：M₁V₁ = M₂V₂"], ["Q1: 4.0 g NaOH in 500 cm³: n = 4.0/40 = 0.10 mol; M = 0.10/0.5 = 0.20 mol dm⁻³ (8.0 g dm⁻³).", "题1：0.20 mol/dm³"], ["Q2: Dilute 50 cm³ of 2.0 mol dm⁻³ HCl to 250 cm³: M₂ = 2.0 × 50/250 = 0.40 mol dm⁻³.", "题2：0.40 mol/dm³"]], "", "Tip: always convert cm³ to dm³ by dividing by 1000."], ["6.5 More Worked Examples: Concentration and Dilution", "6.5 更多例题：浓度与稀释", [["5.3 g of sodium carbonate (M = 106) in 250 cm³: n = 5.3 ÷ 106 = 0.050 mol; M = 0.050 ÷ 0.250 = 0.20 mol dm⁻³.", "5.3 g Na₂CO₃ 在 250 cm³：0.20 mol/dm³"], ["Volume of 0.50 mol dm⁻³ H₂SO₄ containing 0.025 mol: V = 0.025 ÷ 0.50 = 0.050 dm³ = 50 cm³.", "含0.025 mol 的0.50 mol/dm³ H₂SO₄：50 cm³"], ["20 g dm⁻³ NaOH ÷ 40 = 0.50 mol dm⁻³.", "20 g/dm³ NaOH → 0.50 mol/dm³"], ["Dilute 25 cm³ of 1.0 mol dm⁻³ HCl to 0.10 mol dm⁻³: V₂ = 1.0 × 25 ÷ 0.10 = 250 cm³; add 225 cm³ of water.", "25 cm³ 1.0 稀释到0.10：总体积250 cm³，加水225 cm³"]], "", "Tip: show M₁V₁ = M₂V₂ and the unit."], ["Standard Solutions", "标准溶液", [["A standard solution is a solution whose concentration is accurately known.", "标准溶液：浓度准确已知"], ["Method 1 (from solid): calculate the mass; weigh in a beaker; dissolve in distilled water; transfer into a volumetric flask with a funnel; rinse the beaker and funnel into the flask; add water until near the mark, then dropwise until the meniscus is at the mark; stopper and invert to mix.", "由固体配制：称量、溶解、转移、洗涤、定容、摇匀"], ["Q: Prepare 250 cm³ of 0.10 mol dm⁻³ NaOH: n = 0.10 × 0.25 = 0.025 mol; m = 0.025 × 40 = 1.0 g.", "题：配 250 cm³ 0.10 mol/dm³ NaOH：需 1.0 g"], ["Method 2 (dilution): pipette a calculated volume of the stock solution into a volumetric flask and add distilled water to the mark.", "稀释法：移液管取浓溶液，定容"], ["Why rinse the beaker? To transfer all the solute so the concentration is accurate. Why shake? To get a uniform solution.", "冲洗烧杯确保溶质全部转移；摇匀使浓度均匀"]], "", "Tip: the meniscus must be at the calibration mark at eye level."], ["6.6 Preparing a Standard Solution: Steps (F + H)", "6.6 配制标准溶液：步骤", [["F1 Calculate the mass: 250 cm³ of 1.0 mol dm⁻³ NaOH needs 1.0 × 0.250 × 40 = 10.0 g. H: use the formula n = MV and m = n × M.", "F1 计算质量：10.0 g"], ["F2 Weigh the solid accurately in a beaker, add about 50–100 cm³ of distilled water and stir until it dissolves.", "F2 称量固体，烧杯溶解（约50–100 cm³ 水）"], ["F3 Pour into a 250 cm³ volumetric flask through a funnel; rinse the beaker, rod and funnel and add the rinsings. H: so no solute is lost.", "F3 倒入容量瓶；冲洗烧杯、玻棒、漏斗并并入；避免溶质损失"], ["F4 Add distilled water until near the mark, then drop by drop until the bottom of the meniscus touches the mark at eye level.", "F4 加水到刻度附近，滴管逐滴加到弯月面最低处平齐"], ["F5 Stopper and invert several times. H: the solution becomes uniform.", "F5 塞紧倒转摇匀"]], "", "Tip: rinsing the apparatus is a common mark."], ["6.6 Preparing a Dilute Solution by Dilution", "6.6 稀释法配制溶液", [["Prepare 250 cm³ of 0.10 mol dm⁻³ HCl from 1.0 mol dm⁻³ HCl: V₁ = 0.10 × 250 ÷ 1.0 = 25.0 cm³.", "由 1.0 mol/dm³ 配 250 cm³ 0.10 mol/dm³：V₁=25.0 cm³"], ["Use a pipette to transfer 25.0 cm³ of the stock solution into a 250 cm³ volumetric flask; add distilled water to the mark; stopper and mix.", "移液管取25.0 cm³ 注入容量瓶，加水至刻度并摇匀"], ["For concentrated acids, add the acid slowly to water (never water to acid) and wear goggles.", "浓酸：把酸慢慢加入水中，不可把水加入酸；戴护目镜"], ["Check: moles of solute stay the same: 1.0 × 25.0 = 0.10 × 250.", "检验：溶质摩尔不变"]], "", "Tip: 'add acid to water' safety rule."], ["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Acids, pH and Standard Solutions", "示例题：试卷2 A部分（酸、pH、标准溶液）", [["Acid P is 0.1 mol dm⁻³ hydrochloric acid (pH 1). Acid Q is 0.1 mol dm⁻³ ethanoic acid (pH 3).", "酸P：0.1 mol/dm³ 盐酸（pH 1）；酸Q：0.1 mol/dm³ 乙酸（pH 3）"], ["(a) [1] What does pH show? Scheme: concentration of hydrogen ions. (b) [3] Why do P and Q have different pH? Scheme: P ionises completely (1m); Q ionises partially (1m); P has a higher concentration of H⁺ ions (1m).", "(a)pH表示H⁺浓度；(b)P完全电离、Q部分电离、P的H⁺浓度更高"], ["(c) [1] Write the ionisation equation of Q. Scheme: \\(\\ce{CH3COOH <=> H+ + CH3COO-}\\). (d) [2] Calculate the mass of NaOH to prepare 250 cm³ of 0.20 mol dm⁻³ solution (M = 40). Scheme: n = 0.20 × 0.250 = 0.050 mol (1m); m = 0.050 × 40 = 2.0 g (1m).", "(c)乙酸电离方程式；(d)2.0 g"]], "", "Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style."], ["Neutralisation and Titration", "中和反应与滴定", [["Neutralisation: acid + alkali → salt + water. Ionic equation: \\(\\ce{H+ + OH- -> H2O}\\).", "中和：H⁺ + OH⁻ → H₂O"], ["Titration: pipette 25.0 cm³ of alkali into a conical flask; add 2–3 drops of phenolphthalein (pink in alkali, colourless in acid); add acid from a burette with swirling until the end point (permanent colour change); record the volume; repeat until two concordant readings (±0.10 cm³).", "滴定：移液管取碱，加指示剂，从滴定管加酸至终点；重复至读数相近"], ["Calculation: \\(\\dfrac{M_aV_a}{M_bV_b}=\\dfrac{a}{b}\\) where a and b are mole coefficients of acid and base in the balanced equation.", "公式：MaVa/MbVb = a/b"], ["Q1: 25.0 cm³ of 0.10 mol dm⁻³ NaOH is neutralised by 20.0 cm³ HCl. \\(M_a\\times20=0.10\\times25\\) → \\(M_a=0.125\\) mol dm⁻³.", "题1：Ma = 0.125 mol/dm³"], ["Q2: \\(\\ce{H2SO4 + 2NaOH -> Na2SO4 + 2H2O}\\): 20.0 cm³ of 0.10 M \\(\\ce{H2SO4}\\) needs V cm³ of 0.20 M NaOH: \\(\\dfrac{0.10\\times20}{0.20\\times V}=\\dfrac12\\) → V = 20.0 cm³.", "题2：V = 20.0 cm³"]], "", "Tip: use methyl orange (red in acid, yellow in alkali) for strong acid–weak alkali titrations."], ["6.7 Neutralisation: Ionic Equation and Applications (F + H)", "6.7 中和反应：离子方程式与应用", [["F1 Acid + alkali → salt + water. H: the ionic equation is \\(\\ce{H+ + OH- -> H2O}\\) and heat is released (exothermic).", "F1 酸＋碱→盐＋水；离子方程式 H⁺＋OH⁻→H₂O，放热"], ["F2 Antacids (magnesium hydroxide, aluminium hydroxide) relieve gastric pain. H: they neutralise the excess stomach acid.", "F2 抗酸剂中和胃酸"], ["F3 Toothpaste is slightly alkaline. H: it neutralises acids produced by bacteria and protects the teeth.", "F3 牙膏微碱性，中和细菌产生的酸"], ["F4 Quicklime or slaked lime is added to acidic soil. H: neutralises the acid so crops can grow.", "F4 酸性土壤加石灰"], ["F5 Treating acidic industrial waste with an alkali before release. H: prevents pollution of rivers.", "F5 工业废酸排放前先用碱中和"]], "", "Tip: give the application AND what is neutralised."], ["6.7 Titration: Procedure and Precautions (F + H)", "6.7 滴定：步骤与注意事项", [["F1 Rinse the pipette with the alkali and the burette with the acid. H: removes water that would dilute the solution.", "F1 移液管用碱冲洗，滴定管用酸冲洗；避免稀释"], ["F2 Pipette 25.0 cm³ of alkali into a clean conical flask; add 2–3 drops of phenolphthalein (do not rinse the flask with alkali).", "F2 取25.0 cm³ 碱，加2–3滴酚酞；锥形瓶不用碱冲洗"], ["F3 Fill the burette with acid, remove the air bubble from the tip and record the initial reading at eye level.", "F3 装酸，排气泡，记初读数（视线平齐）"], ["F4 Add the acid while swirling the flask; drop by drop near the end point until the pink colour just disappears; record the final reading.", "F4 边摇边加酸，近终点逐滴，粉红刚消失为终点"], ["F5 Repeat until two readings differ by 0.10 cm³ or less; use a white tile and calculate the average titre.", "F5 重复至读数相差≤0.10 cm³；用白瓷砖；取平均"]], "", "Tip: say why for each precaution."], ["6.7 Worked Titration Calculations", "6.7 例题：滴定计算", [["25.0 cm³ of 0.100 mol dm⁻³ NaOH needs 20.0 cm³ of HCl. n(NaOH) = 0.100 × 25.0 ÷ 1000 = 0.00250 mol; ratio 1 : 1; n(HCl) = 0.00250 mol; M = 0.00250 ÷ (20.0 ÷ 1000) = 0.125 mol dm⁻³.", "25.0 cm³ 0.100 NaOH 用20.0 cm³ HCl：0.125 mol/dm³"], ["\\(\\ce{H2SO4 + 2NaOH -> Na2SO4 + 2H2O}\\): 25.0 cm³ of 0.200 mol dm⁻³ NaOH needs 20.0 cm³ H₂SO₄. n(NaOH) = 0.00500 mol; n(H₂SO₄) = 0.00250 mol; M = 0.125 mol dm⁻³.", "H₂SO₄ 与 NaOH 为 1:2：M = 0.125"], ["Titre readings 20.10, 20.00, 20.05 cm³ (all within 0.10): average = 20.05 cm³.", "滴定读数平均值 20.05 cm³"], ["Method: balanced equation → moles of the known solution → mole ratio → unknown moles → concentration.", "方法：方程式→已知摩尔→摩尔比→未知摩尔→浓度"]], "", "Tip: the mole ratio comes from the balanced equation."], ["Salts, Crystals and Their Uses", "盐、晶体及用途", [["A salt is an ionic compound in which the hydrogen ion of an acid is replaced by a metal ion or ammonium ion. Crystals: solids with regular geometrical shape, flat surfaces, sharp edges.", "盐：酸的 H⁺ 被金属离子或铵离子取代"], ["Solubility rules: all sodium, potassium, ammonium salts are soluble; all nitrates are soluble; chlorides soluble except \\(\\ce{AgCl}\\), \\(\\ce{PbCl2}\\); sulphates soluble except \\(\\ce{BaSO4}\\), \\(\\ce{PbSO4}\\), \\(\\ce{CaSO4}\\) (slightly); carbonates insoluble except Na, K, NH₄ salts.", "溶解性规则"], ["Hydrated crystals contain water of crystallisation: \\(\\ce{CuSO4.5H2O}\\) (blue) → heat → \\(\\ce{CuSO4}\\) (white).", "结晶水：蓝色硫酸铜 → 白色无水硫酸铜"], ["Uses of salts: NaCl — food seasoning and preservation; \\(\\ce{KNO3}\\) and \\(\\ce{(NH4)2SO4}\\) — fertilisers; \\(\\ce{CaCO3}\\) — cement, antacid; \\(\\ce{CuSO4}\\) — fungicide; \\(\\ce{MgSO4}\\) — Epsom salt; \\(\\ce{NaHCO3}\\) — baking soda.", "盐的用途"], ["Ammonium salts used as fertilisers supply nitrogen (urea, ammonium nitrate, ammonium sulphate).", "铵盐肥料提供氮"]], "", "Tip: memorise the three insoluble chlorides/sulphates (Ag, Pb, Ba) for the precipitation questions."], ["6.8 Solubility of Salts in Water", "6.8 盐在水中的溶解性", [["All nitrates are soluble. All sodium, potassium and ammonium salts are soluble.", "所有硝酸盐可溶；钠、钾、铵盐可溶"], ["Chlorides are soluble except lead(II) chloride and silver chloride.", "氯化物可溶，氯化铅、氯化银除外"], ["Sulphates are soluble except lead(II) sulphate and barium sulphate (calcium sulphate is slightly soluble).", "硫酸盐可溶，硫酸铅、硫酸钡除外（硫酸钙微溶）"], ["Carbonates are insoluble except sodium, potassium and ammonium carbonates.", "碳酸盐不溶，钠、钾、铵除外"]], "", "Tip: memorise this table; it decides which method to use."], ["6.8 Water of Crystallisation: Worked Example", "6.8 例题：结晶水", [["Hydrated crystals contain water of crystallisation, e.g. \\(\\ce{CuSO4.5H2O}\\) (blue). Heating gives white anhydrous copper(II) sulphate; adding water turns it back to blue (test for water).", "含结晶水的晶体：CuSO₄·5H₂O 蓝色；加热变白；加水又变蓝"], ["2.50 g of hydrated copper(II) sulphate gives 1.60 g of anhydrous salt: mass of water = 0.90 g.", "2.50 g 水合硫酸铜加热得1.60 g 无水盐：水0.90 g"], ["n(H₂O) = 0.90 ÷ 18 = 0.050 mol; n(CuSO₄) = 1.60 ÷ 160 = 0.010 mol; ratio 1 : 5.", "H₂O 0.050 mol；CuSO₄ 0.010 mol；1:5"], ["Formula: \\(\\ce{CuSO4.5H2O}\\); heat until constant mass to be sure all water is removed.", "化学式 CuSO₄·5H₂O；加热至质量不变"]], "", "Tip: subtract to find the mass of water first."], ["Preparation of Salts", "盐的制备", [["Soluble salts of Na, K, NH₄: titration (acid + alkali, no excess), then crystallise: heat to saturation, cool, filter, wash with a little cold distilled water, dry with filter paper.", "钠钾铵盐：滴定法 → 蒸发结晶"], ["Other soluble salts: add excess solid (metal, metal oxide or metal carbonate) to a warm acid until no more dissolves; filter off the excess; heat the filtrate until saturated; cool; filter; wash; dry. E.g. \\(\\ce{CuO + H2SO4 -> CuSO4 + H2O}\\); \\(\\ce{ZnCO3 + 2HCl -> ZnCl2 + H2O + CO2}\\).", "其他可溶盐：过量固体 + 酸 → 过滤 → 结晶"], ["Insoluble salts: double decomposition (precipitation) — mix two soluble salt solutions, filter the precipitate, wash with distilled water, dry. E.g. \\(\\ce{Pb(NO3)2 + 2KI -> PbI2 + 2KNO3}\\) (yellow \\(\\ce{PbI2}\\)); \\(\\ce{BaCl2 + Na2SO4 -> BaSO4 + 2NaCl}\\).", "难溶盐：复分解沉淀 → 过滤、洗涤、干燥"], ["Choose the method: first decide if the salt is soluble, then whether the cation is Na⁺/K⁺/NH₄⁺.", "选方法：先判断可溶性，再判断阳离子"], ["Why excess solid? To make sure all the acid has reacted; the excess is removed by filtration.", "过量固体：确保酸完全反应，过滤除去"]], "", "Tip: always give the reactants for the chosen method: e.g. 'copper(II) oxide and sulphuric acid for copper(II) sulphate'."], ["6.9 Choosing the Method to Prepare a Salt", "6.9 选择制备盐的方法", [["Soluble salt of sodium, potassium or ammonium: acid + alkali by titration, then crystallise.", "可溶性钠、钾、铵盐：酸＋碱滴定，再结晶"], ["Other soluble salts: acid + metal / insoluble base (oxide or hydroxide) / carbonate; add the solid in excess, filter, crystallise.", "其他可溶盐：酸＋金属／不溶碱／碳酸盐；固体过量，过滤，结晶"], ["Insoluble salt: precipitation — mix two soluble salts, filter, wash and dry.", "不溶盐：沉淀法—混合两种可溶盐，过滤、洗涤、干燥"], ["Do not use sodium, potassium or calcium metal with acid — too dangerous; use lead carbonate not lead metal for lead salts.", "不用钠、钾、钙金属与酸反应（太危险）"]], "", "Tip: decide by solubility first."], ["6.9 Preparing Copper(II) Sulphate Crystals (F + H)", "6.9 制备硫酸铜晶体", [["F1 Add excess copper(II) oxide to warm dilute sulphuric acid, stirring: \\(\\ce{CuO + H2SO4 -> CuSO4 + H2O}\\). H: excess ensures all the acid is used up.", "F1 过量氧化铜加入温热稀硫酸；确保酸完全反应"], ["F2 Filter. H: removes the unreacted copper(II) oxide.", "F2 过滤，除去多余氧化铜"], ["F3 Heat the filtrate to evaporate about one-third of the water until saturated (a drop on a glass rod forms crystals on cooling).", "F3 加热蒸发约三分之一至饱和（玻棒检验）"], ["F4 Cool slowly, then filter the crystals. H: slow cooling gives larger crystals.", "F4 缓慢冷却后过滤；冷却慢晶体大"], ["F5 Wash with a little cold distilled water and dry between filter papers. H: removes impurities without dissolving many crystals.", "F5 少量冷蒸馏水洗涤，滤纸间吸干"]], "", "Tip: every step: action + reason."], ["6.9 Preparing Sodium Chloride by Titration and Insoluble Salts by Precipitation (F + H)", "6.9 滴定法制氯化钠与沉淀法制不溶盐", [["Titration method: run 1 with indicator to find the volumes needed; run 2 mixes the same volumes WITHOUT indicator; evaporate and crystallise. H: indicator would contaminate the crystals.", "滴定法：第一次用指示剂定体积；第二次同体积不加指示剂"], ["Precipitation: lead(II) nitrate + potassium iodide → yellow precipitate: \\(\\ce{Pb(NO3)2 + 2KI -> PbI2 + 2KNO3}\\); ionic equation \\(\\ce{Pb^2+ + 2I- -> PbI2}\\).", "沉淀法：碘化铅黄色沉淀"], ["Barium sulphate: \\(\\ce{Ba^2+ + SO4^2- -> BaSO4}\\) (white).", "硫酸钡：白色沉淀"], ["Filter the precipitate, wash with distilled water and dry between filter papers.", "过滤，蒸馏水洗涤，滤纸吸干"]], "", "Tip: ionic equation needs only the ions that form the precipitate."], ["Effect of Heat on Salts", "盐受热分解", [["Carbonates (most): \\(\\ce{MCO3 -> MO + CO2}\\). \\(\\ce{CuCO3}\\): green → black \\(\\ce{CuO}\\); \\(\\ce{ZnCO3}\\): white → \\(\\ce{ZnO}\\) yellow when hot, white when cold; \\(\\ce{PbCO3}\\): → \\(\\ce{PbO}\\) brown hot, yellow cold. \\(\\ce{Na2CO3}\\) and \\(\\ce{K2CO3}\\) do not decompose with a Bunsen flame.", "碳酸盐受热 → 氧化物 + CO₂；Na、K 碳酸盐不分解"], ["Nitrates: \\(\\ce{2KNO3 -> 2KNO2 + O2}\\) (K, Na); \\(\\ce{2Zn(NO3)2 -> 2ZnO + 4NO2 + O2}\\); \\(\\ce{2Cu(NO3)2 -> 2CuO + 4NO2 + O2}\\); \\(\\ce{2Pb(NO3)2 -> 2PbO + 4NO2 + O2}\\) (brown \\(\\ce{NO2}\\) gas).", "硝酸盐：K、Na → 亚硝酸盐 + O₂；其余 → 氧化物 + NO₂ + O₂"], ["Gas tests: \\(\\ce{CO2}\\) turns limewater milky; \\(\\ce{O2}\\) relights a glowing splint; \\(\\ce{NO2}\\) is brown and turns damp blue litmus red.", "气体检验"], ["Sulphates and chlorides are generally stable to heat; ammonium salts decompose: \\(\\ce{NH4Cl -> NH3 + HCl}\\).", "硫酸盐、氯化物较稳定；铵盐分解"], ["The more electropositive the metal (K, Na), the more stable the carbonate/nitrate.", "金属越活泼，盐越稳定"]], "", "Tip: remember the colours — CuO black; ZnO yellow (hot)/white (cold); PbO brown (hot)/yellow (cold)."], ["6.10 Thermal Decomposition of Carbonates", "6.10 碳酸盐的热分解", [["Most metal carbonates decompose on heating: metal carbonate → metal oxide + carbon dioxide. Test the gas with limewater (cloudy).", "多数金属碳酸盐加热：→ 氧化物＋CO₂；石灰水变浑浊"], ["\\(\\ce{CuCO3 -> CuO + CO2}\\): green solid → black solid. \\(\\ce{ZnCO3 -> ZnO + CO2}\\): white; zinc oxide is yellow when hot, white when cold.", "CuCO₃：绿→黑；ZnCO₃：氧化锌热黄冷白"], ["\\(\\ce{PbCO3 -> PbO + CO2}\\): lead(II) oxide is brown when hot, yellow when cold. \\(\\ce{CaCO3 -> CaO + CO2}\\) needs strong heating.", "PbCO₃：氧化铅热棕冷黄；CaCO₃ 需强热"], ["Sodium and potassium carbonates do not decompose with a Bunsen burner flame.", "碳酸钠、钾不易分解"]], "", "Tip: colour of the residue is the clue to the metal."], ["6.10 Thermal Decomposition of Nitrates and Ammonium Salts", "6.10 硝酸盐与铵盐的热分解", [["Sodium and potassium nitrates: nitrate → nitrite + oxygen: \\(\\ce{2KNO3 -> 2KNO2 + O2}\\).", "钠、钾硝酸盐 → 亚硝酸盐＋O₂"], ["Other nitrates: nitrate → metal oxide + nitrogen dioxide (brown gas) + oxygen: \\(\\ce{2Cu(NO3)2 -> 2CuO + 4NO2 + O2}\\); similarly Zn and Pb.", "其他硝酸盐 → 氧化物＋NO₂（棕色）＋O₂"], ["Silver nitrate: \\(\\ce{2AgNO3 -> 2Ag + 2NO2 + O2}\\). Test oxygen: relights a glowing splint; nitrogen dioxide: brown, turns damp blue litmus red.", "硝酸银 → 银＋NO₂＋O₂；氧使带火星木条复燃"], ["Ammonium chloride: \\(\\ce{NH4Cl -> NH3 + HCl}\\) (ammonia turns damp red litmus blue).", "氯化铵 → NH₃＋HCl"]], "", "Tip: a brown gas means a nitrate (not Na or K)."], ["Qualitative Analysis: Gas and Anion Tests", "定性分析：气体与阴离子检验", [["\\(\\ce{H2}\\): pop with a lighted splint. \\(\\ce{O2}\\): relights a glowing splint. \\(\\ce{CO2}\\): limewater turns cloudy. \\(\\ce{NH3}\\): pungent, turns damp red litmus blue. \\(\\ce{Cl2}\\): bleaches damp blue litmus. \\(\\ce{NO2}\\): brown gas.", "气体检验"], ["Carbonate \\(\\ce{CO3^2-}\\): add dilute acid → effervescence, gas turns limewater cloudy.", "碳酸根：加酸产气，使石灰水浑浊"], ["Chloride \\(\\ce{Cl-}\\): add dilute nitric acid then silver nitrate → white precipitate (soluble in ammonia).", "氯离子：HNO₃ + AgNO₃ → 白色沉淀"], ["Sulphate \\(\\ce{SO4^2-}\\): add dilute hydrochloric acid then barium chloride → white \\(\\ce{BaSO4}\\) precipitate.", "硫酸根：HCl + BaCl₂ → 白色沉淀"], ["Nitrate \\(\\ce{NO3-}\\): brown ring test — add iron(II) sulphate solution, then slowly add concentrated sulphuric acid down the side of the tube; a brown ring forms at the junction.", "硝酸根：棕色环试验"]], "", "Tip: acidify first to remove carbonate which would interfere in chloride/sulphate tests."], ["6.11 Anion Tests Step by Step (F + H)", "6.11 阴离子检验步骤", [["F1 Carbonate: add dilute acid; effervescence; gas turns limewater cloudy.", "F1 碳酸根：加稀酸冒泡，石灰水浑浊"], ["F2 Chloride: add dilute nitric acid, then silver nitrate; white precipitate. H: the acid removes carbonate ions that would also form a precipitate.", "F2 氯离子：先加稀硝酸再加硝酸银；白色沉淀；酸排除碳酸根干扰"], ["F3 Sulphate: add dilute nitric acid, then barium chloride or barium nitrate; white precipitate (barium sulphate).", "F3 硫酸根：加稀硝酸，再加氯化钡；白色沉淀"], ["F4 Nitrate: add iron(II) sulphate solution, then add concentrated sulphuric acid slowly down the side of the tube; a brown ring forms at the junction.", "F4 硝酸根：加硫酸亚铁，再沿管壁缓缓加浓硫酸；界面棕色环"]], "", "Tip: acidify first, then add the reagent."], ["Qualitative Analysis: Cation Tests (NaOH and Ammonia)", "定性分析：阳离子检验（NaOH 与氨水）", [["\\(\\ce{Cu^2+}\\): blue precipitate; insoluble in excess NaOH; dissolves in excess ammonia → deep/dark blue solution.", "Cu²⁺：蓝色沉淀；过量氨水溶解成深蓝色溶液"], ["\\(\\ce{Fe^2+}\\): green precipitate (insoluble in excess both). \\(\\ce{Fe^3+}\\): brown precipitate (insoluble in excess both).", "Fe²⁺ 绿色沉淀；Fe³⁺ 棕色沉淀"], ["\\(\\ce{Zn^2+}\\): white precipitate; soluble in excess NaOH and excess ammonia (colourless solutions).", "Zn²⁺：白色沉淀；过量 NaOH、氨水均溶解"], ["\\(\\ce{Al^3+}\\) and \\(\\ce{Pb^2+}\\): white precipitate; soluble in excess NaOH; insoluble in excess ammonia (Pb²⁺ also gives a white precipitate with dilute HCl/KI → yellow \\(\\ce{PbI2}\\)).", "Al³⁺、Pb²⁺：白色沉淀；过量 NaOH 溶解，氨水不溶"], ["\\(\\ce{Mg^2+}\\) and \\(\\ce{Ca^2+}\\): white precipitate; insoluble in excess NaOH; \\(\\ce{Mg^2+}\\) insoluble in ammonia; \\(\\ce{Ca^2+}\\) gives little/no precipitate with ammonia. \\(\\ce{NH4+}\\): warm with NaOH → ammonia gas.", "Mg²⁺、Ca²⁺：白色沉淀，过量 NaOH 不溶；NH₄⁺：加热放出氨"]], "", "Tip: build a table of 'precipitate colour / in excess NaOH / in excess NH₃' and memorise it."], ["Confirming Fe²⁺, Fe³⁺ and Worked Analysis", "Fe²⁺、Fe³⁺ 的确认与综合分析", [["\\(\\ce{Fe^2+}\\): potassium hexacyanoferrate(III) → dark blue precipitate. \\(\\ce{Fe^3+}\\): potassium hexacyanoferrate(II) → dark blue precipitate; or potassium thiocyanate → blood-red solution.", "Fe²⁺：铁氰化钾 → 深蓝；Fe³⁺：KSCN → 血红色"], ["Q: Green solid X is heated: black solid Y and a gas that turns limewater cloudy. Y dissolves in dilute sulphuric acid giving blue solution Z. X = \\(\\ce{CuCO3}\\), Y = \\(\\ce{CuO}\\), Z = \\(\\ce{CuSO4}\\).", "题：绿色 X → 黑色 Y + CO₂；Y 溶于硫酸得蓝色溶液：X=CuCO₃，Y=CuO"], ["Q: White precipitate with NaOH, dissolves in excess; also dissolves in excess ammonia; filtrate with BaCl₂ gives white precipitate. The salt is zinc sulphate.", "题：NaOH 白色沉淀溶于过量、氨水溶解；加 BaCl₂ 白色沉淀 → 硫酸锌"], ["Write the answer as: test → observation → inference.", "答题格式：试验 → 现象 → 推断"], ["Always identify the cation and the anion separately and write the formula.", "阳离子、阴离子分开确定，并写出化学式"]], "", "Tip: 'Add dilute nitric acid first' for the chloride test and 'dilute hydrochloric acid first' for the sulphate test."], ["6.11 Worked Analysis: Identifying Unknown Salts", "6.11 例题：鉴定未知盐", [["Salt P: green solid. On heating, black solid + gas that turns limewater cloudy → copper(II) carbonate. With dilute HCl: effervescence, blue solution; with NaOH: blue precipitate insoluble in excess; with ammonia: blue precipitate dissolves to a deep blue solution → Cu²⁺.", "盐P：绿色→黑色＋CO₂；Cu²⁺ 蓝色沉淀，氨水过量溶成深蓝色"], ["Salt Q: white solid soluble in water. With nitric acid and silver nitrate: white precipitate → Cl⁻. With NaOH and with ammonia: white precipitate dissolving in excess of both → Zn²⁺. Q is zinc chloride.", "盐Q：Cl⁻；Zn²⁺（过量NaOH与氨水均溶解）→ 氯化锌"], ["Write each test, the observation and the ion identified; name the salt at the end.", "写出每个检验、现象、鉴定的离子，最后写出盐"], ["Do not forget the control: use distilled water as a comparison if needed.", "必要时用蒸馏水作对照"]], "", "Tip: present answers in a table: test | observation | inference."], ["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Titration", "示例题：试卷2 A部分（滴定）", [["25.0 cm³ of 0.100 mol dm⁻³ sodium hydroxide is neutralised by 20.0 cm³ of hydrochloric acid using phenolphthalein.", "25.0 cm³ 0.100 mol/dm³ NaOH 被20.0 cm³ 盐酸中和（酚酞）"], ["(a) [1] Name the apparatus to measure 25.0 cm³. Scheme: pipette. (b) [1] State the colour change at the end point. Scheme: pink to colourless.", "(a)移液管；(b)粉红变无色"], ["(c) [1] Write the equation. Scheme: \\(\\ce{NaOH + HCl -> NaCl + H2O}\\). (d) [3] Calculate the concentration of the acid. Scheme: n(NaOH) = 0.00250 mol (1m); n(HCl) = 0.00250 mol (1m); M = 0.00250 ÷ 0.0200 = 0.125 mol dm⁻³ with unit (1m).", "(c)方程式；(d)0.125 mol/dm³"]], "", "Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style."], ["Sample Paper 2 Section B: Preparation of Salts and Analysis (Essay)", "示例题：试卷2 B部分（制盐与鉴定）", [["(a) [10] Describe the preparation of dry copper(II) sulphate crystals from copper(II) oxide and dilute sulphuric acid. Scheme: warm the acid (1m); add excess CuO with stirring (1m); equation (1m); filter (1m); evaporate to saturation (1m); cool to crystallise (1m); filter crystals (1m); wash with cold distilled water (1m); dry between filter papers (1m); reasons given for excess and filtering (1m).", "(a)描述制备硫酸铜晶体：任意10点"], ["(b) [10] A white solid dissolves in water. Plan tests to show it contains zinc ions and chloride ions. Scheme: NaOH — white precipitate that dissolves in excess (2m); ammonia — white precipitate that dissolves in excess (2m); nitric acid + silver nitrate — white precipitate (2m); observations (2m); conclusion (2m).", "(b)证明含 Zn²⁺ 与 Cl⁻"]], "", "Tip: self-made practice question; marks are an example, ask your teacher for the real breakdown."], ["Common Mistakes", "常见错误", [["Mistake: confusing strength and concentration; mixing 'basic' and 'alkaline'.", "错误：混淆强度与浓度；混用 basic 与 alkaline"], ["Mistake: using a measuring cylinder instead of a pipette for titration; forgetting to rinse the burette with the acid first.", "错误：滴定用量筒；滴定管未润洗"]], "", ""], ["Uji Diri", "自测", [["S: pH of 0.01 mol dm⁻³ HCl? J: 2.", "问：0.01 mol/dm³ HCl 的 pH？答：2"], ["S: Name the reaction between lead(II) nitrate and potassium iodide. J: Double decomposition (precipitation) forming yellow lead(II) iodide.", "问：硝酸铅与碘化钾反应？答：复分解沉淀，生成黄色 PbI₂"], ["S: Volume of 0.10 mol dm⁻³ HCl needed to neutralise 25.0 cm³ of 0.20 mol dm⁻³ NaOH? J: V = 0.20 × 25.0/0.10 = 50.0 cm³.", "问：中和 25.0 cm³ 0.20 M NaOH 需 0.10 M HCl？答：50.0 cm³"]], "", ""]], "kim|T4-7": [["Rate of Reaction", "反应速率", [["Rate of reaction = change in quantity of reactant or product per unit time.", "反应速率 = 单位时间内反应物/产物量的变化"], ["Average rate = \\(\\dfrac{\\text{quantity of product formed (or reactant used)}}{\\text{time taken}}\\). Units: g s⁻¹, cm³ s⁻¹, mol dm⁻³ s⁻¹.", "平均速率 = 变化量/时间"], ["Instantaneous (rate at a given time) = gradient of the tangent to the curve at that time.", "瞬时速率 = 该点切线斜率"], ["Graph: the steeper the curve, the faster the reaction; the curve becomes flat when the reaction stops (one reactant used up).", "曲线越陡反应越快；平台期表示反应结束"], ["Fast reactions: precipitation, explosion, neutralisation. Slow: rusting, fermentation, photosynthesis.", "快反应与慢反应"]], "", "Tip: in a graph question, state the gradient formula (Δy/Δx) and the units."], ["Measuring the Rate", "测量反应速率", [["Gas production: collect the gas in a gas syringe or burette over water; record volume at regular time intervals. E.g. \\(\\ce{CaCO3 + 2HCl -> CaCl2 + H2O + CO2}\\).", "测气体体积：气体注射器/排水集气"], ["Mass loss: place the flask on a balance; the decrease in mass (gas escapes) is recorded every 30 s (use cotton wool in the mouth).", "测质量减少：天平上记录"], ["Precipitate formed (disappearing cross): sodium thiosulphate + acid → sulphur; time for the 'X' under the flask to disappear. \\(\\ce{Na2S2O3 + 2HCl -> 2NaCl + S + SO2 + H2O}\\). Rate ∝ 1/time.", "硫代硫酸钠：十字消失的时间，速率 ∝ 1/t"], ["Q: 48 cm³ of H₂ collected in 60 s: average rate = 0.80 cm³ s⁻¹.", "题：48 cm³ 氢气用 60 s：0.80 cm³/s"], ["Q: The graph of volume vs time is flat after 120 s at 90 cm³: the reaction ended; the average rate overall = 90/120 = 0.75 cm³ s⁻¹.", "题：平台后反应结束"]], "", "Tip: choose the measuring method that matches the product — gas, precipitate or mass."], ["7.1 Reading a Rate Graph (F + H)", "7.1 读懂反应速率图", [["F1 The curve is steepest at the start. H: the concentration of reactants is highest, so the rate is highest.", "F1 开始最陡：反应物浓度最高，速率最高"], ["F2 The gradient decreases with time. H: the reactants are used up, so their concentration falls and the rate decreases.", "F2 斜率逐渐减小：反应物被消耗"], ["F3 The graph becomes horizontal. H: the reaction has stopped because the limiting reactant is used up.", "F3 曲线变平：限量反应物用完，反应停止"], ["F4 Average rate = total change in quantity ÷ total time. Instantaneous rate = gradient of the tangent at that time.", "F4 平均速率＝总变化量÷总时间；瞬时速率＝切线斜率"]], "", "Tip: draw the tangent and a large right-angled triangle."], ["7.1 Worked Example: Rate from a Data Table", "7.1 例题：由数据表求速率", [["Volume of CO₂ (cm³) at 0, 30, 60, 90, 120 s: 0, 21, 36, 45, 45.", "CO₂体积：0、21、36、45、45 cm³"], ["Average rate 0–30 s = 21 ÷ 30 = 0.70 cm³ s⁻¹; 30–60 s = 15 ÷ 30 = 0.50; 60–90 s = 9 ÷ 30 = 0.30; 90–120 s = 0.", "各段平均速率：0.70、0.50、0.30、0"], ["Overall average rate (0–90 s) = 45 ÷ 90 = 0.50 cm³ s⁻¹; the rate decreases because the acid is being used up.", "0–90 s 平均速率 0.50 cm³/s；酸被消耗，速率下降"], ["Mass loss: 0.40 g in 100 s → 0.40 ÷ 100 = 0.0040 g s⁻¹.", "质量损失：0.0040 g/s"]], "", "Tip: write the unit of rate (cm³ s⁻¹, g s⁻¹ or mol dm⁻³ s⁻¹)."], ["Factors Affecting the Rate", "影响反应速率的因素", [["Concentration: higher concentration → faster reaction. Temperature: higher → faster (roughly doubles for every 10 °C rise). Total surface area: smaller particles (powder) → faster. Catalyst: increases the rate without being used up. Pressure (gases): higher → faster.", "浓度、温度、总表面积、催化剂、压强（气体）"], ["Experiment (concentration): \\(\\ce{Na2S2O3}\\) with different concentrations and the same volume of acid at the same temperature; time for the cross to disappear; graph of concentration against 1/time.", "实验：不同浓度的 Na₂S₂O₃"], ["Experiment (surface area): marble chips (large) vs powdered calcium carbonate with the same mass and acid; collect \\(\\ce{CO2}\\).", "实验：大理石块 vs 粉末"], ["Experiment (catalyst): decomposition of hydrogen peroxide \\(\\ce{2H2O2 -> 2H2O + O2}\\) with \\(\\ce{MnO2}\\); the mass of \\(\\ce{MnO2}\\) is unchanged afterwards.", "催化剂：MnO₂ 催化 H₂O₂ 分解；反应前后质量不变"], ["Catalysts are specific: Fe for ammonia (Haber), \\(\\ce{V2O5}\\) for \\(\\ce{SO3}\\) (Contact), Pt/Rh for \\(\\ce{NO}\\), Ni for hydrogenation, enzymes in living things.", "催化剂有专一性"]], "", "Tip: for fair tests state which variables are kept constant."], ["7.2 Experiment: Size of Reactant (F + H)", "7.2 实验：反应物大小", [["F1 Compare calcium carbonate chips and powder (same mass) with the same volume and concentration of hydrochloric acid at the same temperature.", "F1 同质量碳酸钙块与粉末，同体积同浓度盐酸、同温度"], ["F2 Collect the gas in a gas syringe or burette and record the volume every 30 s. H: shows how fast the gas is produced.", "F2 每30 s 记录气体体积"], ["F3 Observation: powder gives faster bubbling and a steeper curve; the final volume is the same. H: same mass means the same amount of product.", "F3 观察：粉末更快、曲线更陡，最终体积相同"], ["F4 Explanation: smaller particles give a larger total surface area exposed to the acid, so the frequency of collisions and of effective collisions increases and the rate increases.", "F4 解释：总表面积大，碰撞与有效碰撞频率增加"]], "", "Tip: manipulated = size; responding = volume or time; fixed = mass, acid, temperature."], ["7.2 Experiment: Concentration (F + H)", "7.2 实验：浓度", [["F1 Mix sodium thiosulphate of different concentrations (diluted with water to the same total volume) with the same acid; time how long the 'X' under the flask takes to disappear.", "F1 不同浓度硫代硫酸钠（总体积相同）与同样的酸混合；记录十字消失时间"], ["F2 Observation: the higher the concentration, the shorter the time; rate ∝ 1/time.", "F2 观察：浓度越高，时间越短"], ["F3 Explanation: more particles per unit volume, so more frequent collisions, more frequent effective collisions and a higher rate.", "F3 解释：单位体积粒子多，碰撞与有效碰撞更频繁"], ["F4 Fixed variables: total volume, concentration and volume of acid, temperature. Do the reaction in a fume cupboard because sulphur dioxide is formed.", "F4 固定变量；SO₂ 有毒，须在通风橱进行"]], "", "Tip: graph of concentration against 1/time shows a straight line."], ["7.2 Experiment: Temperature (F + H)", "7.2 实验：温度", [["F1 Warm the sodium thiosulphate solution to 30, 35, 40, 45 and 50 °C before adding the acid; record the time for the 'X' to disappear.", "F1 先将硫代硫酸钠加热到30–50 °C，再加酸"], ["F2 Observation: the higher the temperature, the shorter the time; for about every 10 °C rise the rate is about doubled.", "F2 观察：温度越高，时间越短；约每升10 °C 速率加倍"], ["F3 Explanation: particles gain kinetic energy, move faster and collide more often; more particles have energy equal to or greater than the activation energy, so the frequency of effective collisions rises.", "F3 解释：动能增加，碰撞更频繁，更多粒子达到活化能"], ["F4 Precaution: use the same volumes and the same flask each time; fume cupboard for sulphur dioxide.", "F4 注意：体积相同；通风橱"]], "", "Tip: 'energy ≥ activation energy' is the key phrase for temperature."], ["7.2 Experiment: Catalyst (F + H)", "7.2 实验：催化剂", [["F1 Decomposition of hydrogen peroxide: \\(\\ce{2H2O2 -> 2H2O + O2}\\). Add manganese(IV) oxide and compare with no catalyst. H: bubbles of oxygen form much faster.", "F1 过氧化氢分解；加二氧化锰快得多"], ["F2 Zinc + sulphuric acid: adding a few drops of copper(II) sulphate speeds up the production of hydrogen (copper acts as a catalyst).", "F2 锌与硫酸；加硫酸铜加快"], ["F3 Explanation: a catalyst provides an alternative pathway with a lower activation energy, so more particles can react and the frequency of effective collisions increases.", "F3 解释：提供较低活化能的另一途径"], ["F4 Properties of catalysts: not used up (mass unchanged), only a small amount is needed, specific for a reaction, the final amount of product is the same.", "F4 催化剂性质：不消耗、少量、专一、产量不变"]], "", "Tip: the catalyst does not change the amount of product."], ["Collision Theory", "碰撞理论", [["Reactions occur when particles collide with sufficient energy (≥ activation energy Eₐ) and in the correct orientation — an effective collision.", "有效碰撞：能量 ≥ 活化能，且取向正确"], ["Rate of reaction ∝ frequency of effective collisions.", "反应速率 ∝ 有效碰撞频率"], ["Activation energy: the minimum energy that colliding particles must have for a reaction to occur.", "活化能：反应所需最低能量"], ["Energy profile diagram: reactants → peak (Eₐ) → products; \\(\\Delta H\\) = difference in energy between products and reactants. With a catalyst the peak (Eₐ) is lower.", "能量曲线：催化剂降低 Ea"], ["Not all collisions are effective: only those with energy ≥ Eₐ and the correct orientation.", "并非所有碰撞都有效"]], "", "Tip: use the phrase 'frequency of effective collisions' in every explanation."], ["Explaining the Factors with Collision Theory", "用碰撞理论解释各因素", [["Concentration ↑: more particles per unit volume → the frequency of collisions ↑ → frequency of effective collisions ↑ → rate ↑.", "浓度↑：单位体积粒子数↑ → 碰撞频率↑ → 有效碰撞频率↑"], ["Temperature ↑: particles gain kinetic energy and move faster → more collisions and more particles with energy ≥ Eₐ → frequency of effective collisions ↑.", "温度↑：动能↑ → 能量 ≥ Ea 的粒子更多"], ["Total surface area ↑ (smaller pieces): more particles of the solid are exposed to the other reactant → collision frequency ↑ → effective collisions ↑.", "表面积↑：暴露粒子更多"], ["Catalyst: provides an alternative pathway with a lower activation energy → more colliding particles have energy ≥ Eₐ → effective collisions ↑.", "催化剂：降低 Ea 的替代路径"], ["Gas pressure ↑: the same number of gas particles in a smaller volume → effectively concentration ↑.", "压强↑ ≈ 浓度↑"]], "", "Tip: for temperature always add 'more particles have energy ≥ activation energy'."], ["7.4 Answer Template: Explaining a Factor with Collision Theory (F + H)", "7.4 答题模板：用碰撞理论解释", [["Step 1: state the change in the particles (e.g. larger surface area, more particles per unit volume, higher kinetic energy, lower activation energy).", "步骤1：指出粒子上的变化"], ["Step 2: the frequency of collisions between the reacting particles increases (for a catalyst, skip to step 3).", "步骤2：碰撞频率增加（催化剂此步省略）"], ["Step 3: the frequency of effective collisions increases. H: effective collisions have energy ≥ activation energy and correct orientation.", "步骤3：有效碰撞频率增加；有效碰撞＝能量≥活化能且方向正确"], ["Step 4: so the rate of reaction increases.", "步骤4：故反应速率增大"], ["Energy profile: with a catalyst the peak is lower, so the activation energy is lower; the energy of the reactants and products is unchanged.", "能量图：催化剂使活化能降低，反应物产物能量不变"]], "", "Tip: use the exact words 'frequency of effective collisions'."], ["Worked Examples: Rate", "例题：速率", [["Q1: Calculate the average rate in the first 40 s if 30 cm³ of gas is released. 30/40 = 0.75 cm³ s⁻¹.", "题1：前 40 s：0.75 cm³/s"], ["Q2: From a tangent drawn at t = 20 s that passes through (0, 5) and (40, 45): gradient = 40/40 = 1.0 cm³ s⁻¹ — the instantaneous rate at 20 s.", "题2：切线斜率 = 1.0 cm³/s"], ["Q3: When the temperature rises by 10 °C the time falls from 80 s to 40 s: the rate doubles.", "题3：10 °C 使时间减半，速率加倍"], ["Q4: Sketch how the curve changes when a catalyst is added: steeper initially but reaching the same final volume.", "题4：加催化剂：起始更陡，最终体积不变"], ["Q5: Same acid but double the mass of magnesium: the final volume doubles if the acid is in excess. (If acid is the limiting reagent, the final volume is the same.)", "题5：限量试剂决定最终体积"]], "", "Tip: the final volume of a gas depends on the limiting reactant, not on the rate."], ["Applications in Daily Life and Industry", "日常与工业应用", [["Food storage: refrigeration slows down the rate of food spoilage (lower temperature); cooking in small pieces (larger total surface area) cooks faster; pressure cooker (higher temperature) cooks faster.", "食物：冷藏减慢变质；切小块；高压锅"], ["Industry: Haber process (Fe catalyst, 450 °C, 200 atm) for ammonia; Contact process (\\(\\ce{V2O5}\\)) for sulphuric acid; Ostwald process (Pt) for nitric acid; hydrogenation (Ni) for margarine.", "工业：哈伯、接触法、奥斯特瓦尔德法、氢化"], ["Safety: fine flour/coal dust in the air can explode (very large surface area); fire-fighters cut off oxygen to reduce the rate.", "安全：粉尘爆炸"], ["Medicine: drugs in powder or solution form act faster; enzymes (biological catalysts) work at body temperature.", "药物与酶"], ["Reactions in life: respiration, photosynthesis, rusting, tarnishing, fermentation.", "生活中的反应"]], "", "Tip: link the application to the factor, e.g. 'powder → larger total surface area'."], ["7.3 Applications of the Factors (F + H)", "7.3 影响速率因素的应用", [["F1 Food kept in a refrigerator. H: lower temperature slows the reactions of bacteria that spoil food.", "F1 冰箱保存食物；低温减慢变质"], ["F2 Pressure cooker cooks faster. H: higher pressure raises the boiling point, so the temperature inside is higher.", "F2 压力锅；温度更高"], ["F3 Catalytic converter in cars (platinum, rhodium). H: converts carbon monoxide and nitrogen oxides to carbon dioxide and nitrogen.", "F3 汽车催化转化器"], ["F4 Haber process uses an iron catalyst; enzymes in detergent act as catalysts.", "F4 哈伯法用铁；洗衣粉酶"], ["F5 Flour dust explosion in factories. H: very large surface area burns extremely fast, so prevent dust accumulation.", "F5 面粉粉尘爆炸；表面积极大"]], "", "Tip: link each application to one factor."], ["Sample Paper 2 Section A: Rate of Reaction", "示例题：试卷2 A部分（反应速率）", [["Experiment I: excess calcium carbonate chips with 50 cm³ of 0.5 mol dm⁻³ hydrochloric acid. Experiment II: the same mass of calcium carbonate powder with the same acid.", "实验I：碳酸钙块；实验II：同质量粉末，同样酸"], ["(a) [1] Which experiment has the higher rate? Scheme: II. (b) [3] Explain. Scheme: smaller particle size, larger total surface area (1m); frequency of collisions increases (1m); frequency of effective collisions increases (1m).", "(a)II；(b)表面积→碰撞→有效碰撞"], ["(c) [2] 40 cm³ of gas is collected in 80 s in experiment II. Calculate the average rate. Scheme: 40 ÷ 80 (1m); 0.50 cm³ s⁻¹ (1m).", "(c)平均速率 0.50 cm³/s"], ["(d) [1] Why is the total volume of gas the same in both experiments? Scheme: the same mass of calcium carbonate (the same number of moles).", "(d)总体积相同：碳酸钙质量相同"]], "", "Tip: self-made practice question in SPM style."], ["Sample Paper 2 Section B: Plan an Experiment on Temperature (Essay)", "示例题：试卷2 B部分（设计温度实验）", [["(a) [10] Plan an experiment to investigate the effect of temperature on the rate of reaction between sodium thiosulphate and sulphuric acid. Scheme: aim (1m); problem statement (1m); hypothesis (1m); variables (3m); materials and apparatus (1m); procedure (2m); tabulation of data (1m).", "(a)设计实验：目的、问题陈述、假设、变量、仪器、步骤、表格"], ["(b) [10] Explain the result using collision theory. Scheme: higher temperature, particles gain kinetic energy (2m); move faster (1m); frequency of collisions increases (2m); more particles have energy ≥ activation energy (2m); frequency of effective collisions increases (2m); rate increases and time decreases (1m).", "(b)用碰撞理论解释结果"]], "", "Tip: self-made practice question; marks are an example, ask your teacher for the real breakdown."], ["Common Mistakes", "常见错误", [["Mistake: 'The particles collide more' only — you must say 'frequency of effective collisions'.", "错误：只写“碰撞更多”"], ["Mistake: saying a catalyst gives the particles more energy.", "错误：催化剂不会给粒子加能量，它降低 Ea"]], "", ""], ["Uji Diri", "自测", [["S: Why does a powder react faster than a lump? J: Larger total surface area → more particles exposed → higher frequency of effective collisions.", "问：粉末为何更快？答：总表面积大，有效碰撞频率高"], ["S: State the effect of a catalyst on the activation energy. J: It lowers the activation energy.", "问：催化剂对活化能的影响？答：降低"], ["S: Gas volume of 36 cm³ collected in 90 s. Average rate? J: 36/90 = 0.4 cm³ s⁻¹.", "问：36 cm³ 用 90 s，平均速率？答：0.4 cm³/s"]], "", ""]], "kim|T4-8": [["Alloys and Their Importance", "合金及其重要性", [["An alloy is a mixture of two or more elements with a specific composition, one of which is a metal.", "合金：由两种或以上元素组成的混合物，其中至少一种是金属"], ["Why pure metals are soft/malleable: atoms of the same size are arranged in orderly layers that slide easily over one another when force is applied.", "纯金属软：原子大小相同，层状排列，容易滑动"], ["In an alloy, atoms of a different size disrupt the orderly arrangement; the layers cannot slide easily → harder and stronger.", "合金：异种原子扰乱排列，层不易滑动 → 更硬更强"], ["Aims of making alloys: increase hardness and strength, prevent corrosion, improve appearance, lower the melting point.", "制合金的目的"], ["Experiment: drop a steel ball from the same height onto a pure metal block and its alloy block; the dent diameter is smaller on the alloy → harder.", "实验：钢珠撞击凹痕，合金凹痕小"]], "", "Tip: draw atoms of two sizes to illustrate the explanation for alloys."], ["Examples of Alloys", "合金例子与用途", [["Bronze: copper + tin; harder than copper, resists corrosion; statues, medals, bells.", "青铜：铜+锡；雕像、奖牌、钟"], ["Brass: copper + zinc; harder than copper, golden; musical instruments, door knobs, taps.", "黄铜：铜+锌；乐器、门把"], ["Steel: iron + carbon; stronger and harder than iron; construction, vehicles, bridges, tools. Stainless steel: iron + chromium + nickel + carbon; does not rust; cutlery, surgical equipment, sinks.", "钢：铁+碳；不锈钢：铁+铬+镍+碳"], ["Duralumin: aluminium + copper + magnesium + manganese; light and strong; aircraft bodies, bicycles.", "硬铝：铝+铜+镁+锰；飞机"], ["Pewter: tin + antimony + copper; souvenirs. Solder: tin + lead; low melting point, joins electrical components. Cupronickel: copper + nickel; coins.", "锡镴；焊锡；白铜"]], "", "Tip: remember each alloy's components and one use."], ["Glass: Composition and Types", "玻璃：成分与类型", [["Glass is an amorphous (non-crystalline), transparent, hard but brittle substance, mainly of silica (\\(\\ce{SiO2}\\), silicon dioxide).", "玻璃：非晶体、透明、硬而脆；主要成分 SiO₂"], ["Fused glass: almost pure \\(\\ce{SiO2}\\); very high melting point; heat resistant, transparent to UV; lenses, prisms, optical instruments, laboratory ware.", "石英（熔融）玻璃：几乎纯 SiO₂"], ["Soda-lime glass: \\(\\ce{SiO2}\\) + sodium carbonate + calcium oxide; cheap, easy to shape, softens at low temperature; bottles, windows, light bulbs.", "钠钙玻璃：瓶、窗"], ["Borosilicate glass: \\(\\ce{SiO2}\\) + boron(III) oxide; resists heat and sudden temperature change, chemically inert; laboratory glassware, cooking ware (Pyrex), medical equipment.", "硼硅玻璃：耐热；实验室仪器"], ["Lead crystal glass: \\(\\ce{SiO2}\\) + lead(II) oxide; high refractive index, shiny, dense; decorative items, glassware, lenses.", "铅玻璃：折射率高，装饰品"]], "", "Tip: link the composition to the property: boron(III) oxide → heat resistant."], ["Ceramics", "陶瓷", [["Ceramics are inorganic non-metallic materials made from clay (aluminosilicates, kaolin) and other minerals, shaped and fired at high temperatures.", "陶瓷：黏土等无机非金属材料，高温烧制"], ["Properties: hard, brittle, high melting point, chemically inert, good electrical and heat insulator, strong under compression, can withstand high temperature.", "性质：硬脆、熔点高、化学惰性、绝缘、抗压"], ["Traditional ceramics: pottery, bricks, tiles, porcelain, cement, kitchenware.", "传统陶瓷：陶器、砖、瓷砖、瓷器"], ["Engineering ceramics: aluminium oxide (cutting tools), silicon carbide (abrasive, car brakes), silicon nitride (engine parts), spark plug insulators, space shuttle heat shields, bio-ceramics for bones and teeth.", "工程陶瓷：氧化铝、碳化硅、氮化硅"], ["Disadvantage: brittle — breaks on impact; modern ceramics are made tougher with additives.", "缺点：脆"]], "", "Tip: the typical answer is 'high melting point and inert' for heat and chemical resistance."], ["Composite Materials", "复合材料", [["A composite material is formed by combining two or more different substances (with different physical and chemical properties) to produce a new material with improved properties.", "复合材料：两种或以上不同物质结合，得到性能更好的新材料"], ["Reinforced concrete: concrete (cement + sand + gravel) + steel bars; strong under compression and tension; buildings, bridges, dams.", "钢筋混凝土：抗压 + 抗拉"], ["Fibre glass: glass fibres + plastic (polyester resin); light, strong, does not corrode; boats, helmets, car bodies, roofing.", "玻璃纤维：船、头盔"], ["Fibre optic: glass core + cladding (lower refractive index); total internal reflection transmits light signals; telecommunications, medical endoscope.", "光纤：玻璃芯 + 包层"], ["Superconductors: ceramic composites that conduct with zero resistance at very low temperature (magnets of MRI scanners, maglev trains). Photochromic glass: glass + silver chloride/bromide; darkens in sunlight; sunglasses.", "超导体；光致变色玻璃"]], "", "Tip: for each composite, name the components and the property gained."], ["Comparison Table: Alloys, Glass, Ceramics, Composites", "对比：合金、玻璃、陶瓷、复合材料", [["Alloys: metals mixed with other elements; conduct electricity; harder, corrosion-resistant; strong ductile materials.", "合金：导电、较硬、耐腐蚀"], ["Glass: silica based, transparent, amorphous, brittle, non-conductor; reusable and recyclable.", "玻璃：透明、脆、不导电"], ["Ceramics: clay based, hard, brittle, high melting point, inert, insulator.", "陶瓷：熔点高、惰性"], ["Composites: combine the best properties of the components (strong + light, strong + flexible).", "复合材料：兼具优点"], ["Choose the right material: oven dish → borosilicate glass/ceramic; aircraft body → duralumin or fibre-reinforced composite; bridge → steel/reinforced concrete.", "选材：烤盘、飞机、桥梁"]], "", "Tip: justify the choice with a property, not just a name."], ["Common Mistakes", "常见错误", [["Mistake: saying an alloy is a compound; it is a mixture.", "错误：合金是混合物，不是化合物"], ["Mistake: 'glass is a crystal' — it is amorphous.", "错误：玻璃是非晶体"]], "", ""], ["Uji Diri", "自测", [["S: Why is brass harder than copper? J: Zinc atoms (different size) disrupt the orderly layers of copper atoms so they cannot slide easily.", "问：黄铜为何比铜硬？答：锌原子扰乱铜层，层不易滑动"], ["S: Which glass is used for laboratory apparatus and why? J: Borosilicate glass — resists high temperature and sudden changes.", "问：实验仪器用哪种玻璃？答：硼硅玻璃，耐热"], ["S: Name the composite used for bridges. J: Reinforced concrete.", "问：桥梁用的复合材料？答：钢筋混凝土"]], "", ""]], "kim|T5-1": [["Oxidation and Reduction", "氧化与还原", [["In terms of oxygen: oxidation = gain of oxygen; reduction = loss of oxygen. In terms of hydrogen: oxidation = loss of hydrogen; reduction = gain of hydrogen.", "按氧：得氧为氧化，失氧为还原；按氢相反"], ["In terms of electrons (OIL RIG): Oxidation Is Loss of electrons; Reduction Is Gain of electrons.", "按电子：失电子为氧化，得电子为还原"], ["In terms of oxidation number: oxidation = increase in oxidation number; reduction = decrease.", "按氧化数：升高为氧化，降低为还原"], ["Redox reaction: oxidation and reduction occur at the same time. Oxidising agent: accepts electrons (itself reduced). Reducing agent: donates electrons (itself oxidised).", "氧化还原反应同时发生；氧化剂得电子被还原，还原剂失电子被氧化"], ["Example: \\(\\ce{Mg + CuO -> MgO + Cu}\\): Mg is oxidised (reducing agent); \\(\\ce{CuO}\\) is reduced (oxidising agent).", "例：Mg 是还原剂，CuO 是氧化剂"]], "", "Tip: always state the change in oxidation number or electrons when explaining oxidation/reduction."], ["Oxidation Numbers", "氧化数", [["Rules: free element = 0; simple ion = its charge; oxygen usually −2 (peroxide −1); hydrogen usually +1 (metal hydrides −1); total in a neutral compound = 0; total in an ion = charge of the ion.", "规则：单质 0；简单离子 = 电荷；O 通常 −2；H 通常 +1；化合物总和 0"], ["Examples: S in \\(\\ce{SO4^2-}\\): x + 4(−2) = −2 → +6; Mn in \\(\\ce{MnO4-}\\): x − 8 = −1 → +7; Cr in \\(\\ce{Cr2O7^2-}\\): 2x − 14 = −2 → +6; N in \\(\\ce{NO3-}\\): +5.", "算例：SO₄²⁻ 中 S +6；MnO₄⁻ 中 Mn +7；Cr₂O₇²⁻ 中 Cr +6"], ["IUPAC names use roman numerals: iron(II) oxide \\(\\ce{FeO}\\), iron(III) oxide \\(\\ce{Fe2O3}\\), copper(I) oxide \\(\\ce{Cu2O}\\).", "命名用罗马数字"], ["Q: \\(\\ce{2FeCl2 + Cl2 -> 2FeCl3}\\): Fe +2 → +3 (oxidised, Fe²⁺ reducing agent); Cl 0 → −1 (reduced, Cl₂ oxidising agent).", "题：Fe²⁺ → Fe³⁺ 被氧化"], ["Disproportionation: the same element is oxidised and reduced at the same time (\\(\\ce{Cl2 + 2NaOH -> NaCl + NaOCl + H2O}\\): Cl 0 → −1 and +1).", "歧化反应"]], "", "Tip: write the oxidation number above each element in the equation."], ["Redox Tests and Displacement Reactions", "氧化还原的检验与置换反应", [["Fe²⁺ → Fe³⁺ (oxidation): add bromine water → green solution turns yellow-brown; acidified \\(\\ce{KMnO4}\\) → purple turns colourless; test the product with KSCN → blood-red.", "Fe²⁺ → Fe³⁺：溴水、酸化高锰酸钾"], ["Fe³⁺ → Fe²⁺ (reduction): add zinc powder → brown/yellow turns green; test with potassium hexacyanoferrate(III) → dark blue precipitate.", "Fe³⁺ → Fe²⁺：加锌粉"], ["Acidified \\(\\ce{K2Cr2O7}\\) is an oxidising agent: orange → green (\\(\\ce{Cr^3+}\\)). Acidified \\(\\ce{KMnO4}\\): purple → colourless (\\(\\ce{Mn^2+}\\)). \\(\\ce{KI}\\) as reducing agent: \\(\\ce{2I- -> I2 + 2e-}\\) → brown, blue-black with starch.", "重铬酸钾橙→绿；高锰酸钾紫→无色；KI → I₂"], ["Displacement of metals: \\(\\ce{Mg + CuSO4 -> MgSO4 + Cu}\\) (blue solution fades, brown solid). A more reactive metal displaces a less reactive metal from its salt solution.", "金属置换：活泼金属置换不活泼金属"], ["Displacement of halogens: \\(\\ce{Cl2 + 2KBr -> 2KCl + Br2}\\): chlorine (stronger oxidising agent) oxidises bromide.", "卤素置换"]], "", "Tip: when asked for observations write the colour before and after."], ["Standard Electrode Potential", "标准电极电势", [["Standard hydrogen electrode (SHE): platinum electrode in 1.0 mol dm⁻³ \\(\\ce{H+}\\), hydrogen gas at 1 atm, 298 K; \\(E^\\circ=0.00\\) V.", "标准氢电极：1.0 M H⁺、H₂ 1 atm、298 K；E° = 0"], ["Standard electrode potential \\(E^\\circ\\): potential difference of a half-cell (ion 1.0 mol dm⁻³, 298 K) measured against the SHE for the reduction half-reaction.", "标准电极电势：半电池相对 SHE 的还原电势"], ["Selected \\(E^\\circ\\) (V): \\(\\ce{Mg^2+/Mg}\\) −2.38; \\(\\ce{Al^3+/Al}\\) −1.66; \\(\\ce{Zn^2+/Zn}\\) −0.76; \\(\\ce{Fe^2+/Fe}\\) −0.44; \\(\\ce{Pb^2+/Pb}\\) −0.13; \\(\\ce{H+/H2}\\) 0.00; \\(\\ce{Cu^2+/Cu}\\) +0.34; \\(\\ce{Ag+/Ag}\\) +0.80; \\(\\ce{Br2/Br-}\\) +1.07; \\(\\ce{Cl2/Cl-}\\) +1.36; \\(\\ce{MnO4-/Mn^2+}\\) +1.51.", "常见 E° 值"], ["The more positive \\(E^\\circ\\), the stronger the oxidising agent (more easily reduced); the more negative, the stronger the reducing agent (more easily oxidised).", "E° 越正：氧化剂越强；越负：还原剂越强"], ["A reaction is spontaneous if \\(E^\\circ_{cell}>0\\): \\(E^\\circ_{cell}=E^\\circ_{\\text{cathode}}-E^\\circ_{\\text{anode}}\\) (E° of the reduction half-cell minus that of the oxidation half-cell).", "\\(E°_{cell}\\) = E°(阴极) − E°(阳极)"]], "", "Tip: the data table is given in the exam; practise reading it."], ["Chemical Cells (Voltaic Cells)", "化学电池（原电池）", [["A chemical cell converts chemical energy to electrical energy through a spontaneous redox reaction. Negative terminal (anode): oxidation; positive terminal (cathode): reduction.", "化学电池：化学能 → 电能；负极（阳极）氧化，正极（阴极）还原"], ["Daniell cell: \\(\\ce{Zn(s)|Zn^2+(aq)||Cu^2+(aq)|Cu(s)}\\). Anode: \\(\\ce{Zn -> Zn^2+ + 2e-}\\); cathode: \\(\\ce{Cu^2+ + 2e- -> Cu}\\). \\(E^\\circ_{cell}=+0.34-(-0.76)=1.10\\) V.", "丹尼尔电池：E°cell = 1.10 V"], ["Electrons flow through the external circuit from the negative terminal (anode) to the positive terminal (cathode). Observations: zinc plate thins, copper plate thickens, blue solution fades.", "外电路电子由负极流向正极；Zn 变薄、Cu 变厚、蓝色变浅"], ["Salt bridge (or porous pot): completes the circuit, allows ions to move, keeps the solutions electrically neutral and prevents mixing of the electrolytes.", "盐桥：完成回路，保持电中性"], ["Q: Mg/Cu cell: \\(E^\\circ_{cell}=0.34-(-2.38)=2.72\\) V; the further apart the metals in the electrochemical series, the higher the voltage.", "题：Mg/Cu 电池 2.72 V；金属相距越远，电压越大"]], "", "Tip: in the cell notation the anode is written on the left."], ["Electrolysis: Principles and Selective Discharge", "电解：原理与选择性放电", [["Electrolysis: decomposition of an electrolyte by electric current. Anode (+): oxidation (anions are discharged). Cathode (−): reduction (cations are discharged).", "电解：电流分解电解质；阳极氧化，阴极还原"], ["Factors deciding the ion discharged: (1) position in the electrochemical series (E° — the ion lower in the series discharges first at the cathode: Ag⁺ > Cu²⁺ > H⁺ > Na⁺); (2) concentration of the ion (e.g. concentrated Cl⁻ discharged in preference to OH⁻); (3) type of electrode (inert carbon/platinum vs active copper).", "决定放电的因素：E°、浓度、电极类型"], ["Molten \\(\\ce{PbBr2}\\): cathode \\(\\ce{Pb^2+ + 2e- -> Pb}\\); anode \\(\\ce{2Br- -> Br2 + 2e-}\\).", "熔融 PbBr₂"], ["Aqueous \\(\\ce{CuSO4}\\), carbon electrodes: cathode \\(\\ce{Cu^2+ + 2e- -> Cu}\\) (brown deposit); anode \\(\\ce{4OH- -> 2H2O + O2 + 4e-}\\); the blue colour fades.", "CuSO₄（碳电极）：阴极 Cu，阳极 O₂；蓝色变浅"], ["Aqueous \\(\\ce{CuSO4}\\), copper electrodes: anode \\(\\ce{Cu -> Cu^2+ + 2e-}\\) (dissolves); cathode \\(\\ce{Cu^2+ + 2e- -> Cu}\\); blue colour unchanged — used for purification and electroplating.", "铜电极：阳极溶解，蓝色不变"]], "", "Tip: list all ions present (including \\(\\ce{H+}\\) and \\(\\ce{OH-}\\) from water) before choosing."], ["Electrolysis of Aqueous Solutions: More Examples", "水溶液电解：更多例子", [["Concentrated NaCl (carbon electrodes): cathode \\(\\ce{2H+ + 2e- -> H2}\\); anode \\(\\ce{2Cl- -> Cl2 + 2e-}\\) (high concentration of Cl⁻); the remaining solution is NaOH.", "浓 NaCl：阴极 H₂，阳极 Cl₂，余下 NaOH"], ["Dilute NaCl: anode \\(\\ce{4OH- -> 2H2O + O2 + 4e-}\\) (low [Cl⁻]).", "稀 NaCl：阳极放 O₂"], ["Dilute sulphuric acid: \\(\\ce{H2}\\) at the cathode, \\(\\ce{O2}\\) at the anode in the ratio 2 : 1 by volume (electrolysis of water).", "稀硫酸：H₂ : O₂ = 2 : 1"], ["Electroplating: object to be plated = cathode; plating metal = anode; electrolyte = solution of the plating metal's salt (e.g. silver plating: anode Ag, electrolyte \\(\\ce{AgNO3}\\)). Purpose: prevent corrosion, improve appearance.", "电镀：镀件为阴极，镀层金属为阳极"], ["Purification of copper: impure copper = anode; pure copper = cathode; electrolyte \\(\\ce{CuSO4}\\); impurities fall as anode mud.", "精炼铜：粗铜为阳极"]], "", "Tip: differentiate the polarity: electrolytic cell anode is +, chemical cell anode is −."], ["Comparison: Electrolytic and Chemical Cells", "对比：电解池与化学电池", [["Energy change: electrolytic — electrical → chemical; chemical cell — chemical → electrical.", "能量转化相反"], ["Anode: electrolytic — positive, oxidation; chemical cell — negative, oxidation. Cathode: electrolytic — negative, reduction; chemical cell — positive, reduction.", "电极极性不同，但阳极始终氧化"], ["Reaction: electrolytic — non-spontaneous, driven by an external power supply; chemical cell — spontaneous.", "电解非自发；原电池自发"], ["Electrolytes: electrolytic — one solution; chemical cell — usually two half-cells joined with a salt bridge.", "电解质：一个溶液 vs 两个半电池"], ["Current flow in the external circuit: electrons always flow from the anode to the cathode.", "外电路中电子总是由阳极流向阴极"]], "", "Tip: remember 'AN OX' and 'RED CAT': Anode = Oxidation; Reduction at Cathode."], ["Extraction of Metals", "金属的提取", [["Method depends on the position in the reactivity series: K, Na, Ca, Mg, Al — electrolysis of the molten ore; Zn, Fe, Sn, Pb — heating with carbon (reduction); Cu, Ag, Au — heating alone or found native.", "方法依金属活泼性：电解 / 碳还原 / 加热"], ["Iron (blast furnace): \\(\\ce{C + O2 -> CO2}\\); \\(\\ce{CO2 + C -> 2CO}\\); \\(\\ce{Fe2O3 + 3CO -> 2Fe + 3CO2}\\); limestone: \\(\\ce{CaCO3 -> CaO + CO2}\\), \\(\\ce{CaO + SiO2 -> CaSiO3}\\) (slag removes impurities).", "高炉炼铁及造渣"], ["Aluminium: electrolysis of molten aluminium oxide dissolved in molten cryolite (lowers melting point from 2000 °C to about 900 °C); cathode: \\(\\ce{Al^3+ + 3e- -> Al}\\); anode: \\(\\ce{2O^2- -> O2 + 4e-}\\); graphite anodes burn away and must be replaced.", "铝：熔融 Al₂O₃ 加冰晶石电解"], ["Tin and zinc: reduction of the oxides with carbon. Copper: roasting ore then reduction.", "锡锌：碳还原"], ["Environmental effect: carbon dioxide emissions, mining waste, energy use; recycle metals to save ores and energy.", "环境影响；回收金属"]], "", "Tip: say why molten, not solid — ions can move only when molten."], ["Rusting and Its Prevention", "生锈及防锈", [["Rusting is the redox corrosion of iron: needs water and oxygen. Anode (dent, less oxygen): \\(\\ce{Fe -> Fe^2+ + 2e-}\\); cathode (edges, more oxygen): \\(\\ce{O2 + 2H2O + 4e- -> 4OH-}\\); \\(\\ce{Fe^2+}\\) → \\(\\ce{Fe^3+}\\) → \\(\\ce{Fe2O3.xH2O}\\) (rust).", "生锈：Fe 失电子，O₂ 得电子；Fe₂O₃·xH₂O"], ["Faster in salt water or acid rain (more free ions as electrolyte), in contact with a less electropositive metal (Cu, Sn).", "盐水、酸雨加快生锈；与不活泼金属接触"], ["Prevention: paint, oil/grease (barrier); galvanising (zinc coating, sacrificial); electroplating with tin/chromium; alloying (stainless steel); sacrificial protection with Mg or Zn blocks on ship hulls and pipelines (more electropositive metal corrodes instead of iron).", "防锈：涂层、镀锌、镀锡/铬、不锈钢、牺牲阳极"], ["Tin plating protects only while the layer is intact; if scratched, iron (more electropositive than tin) rusts faster.", "镀锡：破损后铁更易锈"], ["Zinc protects even if scratched because zinc is more electropositive than iron (it is oxidised in preference).", "镀锌：划破后仍保护铁"]], "", "Tip: in rusting explanation name the three things: anode (iron), cathode (oxygen) and electrolyte (water)."], ["Common Mistakes", "常见错误", [["Mistake: mixing up anode/cathode in chemical cells and electrolytic cells.", "错误：混淆两种电池的电极"], ["Mistake: forgetting to include the half equations' electrons or wrong charge.", "错误：半反应漏写电子"]], "", ""], ["Uji Diri", "自测", [["S: Oxidation number of Cr in \\(\\ce{K2Cr2O7}\\)? J: +6.", "问：K₂Cr₂O₇ 中 Cr 的氧化数？答：+6"], ["S: Calculate \\(E^\\circ_{cell}\\) for Zn/Ag cell. J: 0.80 − (−0.76) = 1.56 V.", "问：Zn/Ag 电池 E°？答：1.56 V"], ["S: Why is cryolite added in extraction of aluminium? J: To lower the melting point of aluminium oxide, saving energy.", "问：为何加冰晶石？答：降低熔点，节能"]], "", ""]], "kim|T5-2": [["Types of Carbon Compounds", "碳化合物的类型", [["Organic compounds contain carbon (usually with hydrogen), often covalent with low melting/boiling points, insoluble in water but soluble in organic solvents, do not conduct electricity, and burn.", "有机物：含碳；共价；熔沸点低；难溶水；不导电；可燃"], ["Hydrocarbons: compounds containing only carbon and hydrogen. Saturated: only C–C single bonds (alkanes). Unsaturated: at least one C=C double bond (alkenes) or C≡C triple bond (alkynes).", "烃：饱和（烷烃）；不饱和（烯烃）"], ["Sources: crude oil, natural gas, coal. Fractional distillation separates crude oil by boiling point: petroleum gas (LPG), petrol, naphtha, kerosene, diesel, lubricating oil, bitumen.", "来源：原油分馏"], ["Inorganic carbon compounds: \\(\\ce{CO2}\\), \\(\\ce{CO}\\), carbonates, carbides.", "无机碳化物：CO₂、CO、碳酸盐"], ["Cracking converts large hydrocarbon molecules to smaller, more useful ones (alkanes + alkenes) using a catalyst (alumina/silica) at high temperature.", "裂化：大分子 → 小分子"]], "", "Tip: remember that all alkenes are unsaturated and burn with a sooty flame."], ["Homologous Series", "同系列", [["A homologous series is a family of organic compounds with the same functional group and general formula, in which successive members differ by \\(\\ce{CH2}\\), and with similar chemical properties and gradually changing physical properties.", "同系列：相同官能团和通式，相邻成员差 CH₂"], ["Alkane \\(\\ce{C_nH_{2n+2}}\\) (single bond, –ane); alkene \\(\\ce{C_nH_{2n}}\\) (C=C, –ene); alcohol \\(\\ce{C_nH_{2n+1}OH}\\) (–OH, –ol); carboxylic acid \\(\\ce{C_nH_{2n+1}COOH}\\) (–COOH, –oic acid); ester \\(\\ce{RCOOR'}\\) (–COO–, –oate).", "通式和官能团"], ["Names by number of carbons: 1 meth–, 2 eth–, 3 prop–, 4 but–, 5 pent–, 6 hex–, 7 hept–, 8 oct–.", "碳数命名：甲乙丙丁戊己庚辛"], ["Physical properties trend: as the molecular size increases, boiling/melting points increase (stronger van der Waals forces); density increases; solubility in water decreases (alcohols); volatility decreases.", "物理性质趋势"], ["Chemical properties are the same within a series because they have the same functional group.", "同系列化学性质相似"]], "", "Tip: write the formula with the general formula e.g. C₃H₈ is an alkane (2×3+2 = 8)."], ["Alkanes and Alkenes: Reactions", "烷烃与烯烃的反应", [["Alkane combustion: complete \\(\\ce{CH4 + 2O2 -> CO2 + 2H2O}\\); incomplete → soot (C) and CO. Substitution with halogens under UV light: \\(\\ce{CH4 + Cl2 -> CH3Cl + HCl}\\).", "烷烃：燃烧；紫外光下卤代"], ["Alkene: burns with a yellow sooty flame (higher % carbon). Addition reactions: with hydrogen (Ni, 180 °C) \\(\\ce{C2H4 + H2 -> C2H6}\\); with bromine \\(\\ce{C2H4 + Br2 -> C2H4Br2}\\) (brown bromine water decolourised); with steam (\\(\\ce{H3PO4}\\), 300 °C, 60 atm) → ethanol; with hydrogen halides → haloalkane.", "烯烃：加成反应：H₂、Br₂、水"], ["Oxidation by acidified \\(\\ce{KMnO4}\\): purple → colourless (alkene) — alkanes do not react.", "酸化 KMnO₄ 褪色（烯烃）"], ["Test to distinguish alkane from alkene: shake with bromine water or acidified potassium manganate(VII): alkene decolourises it.", "区分烷烃与烯烃：溴水或 KMnO₄"], ["Polymerisation: ethene → poly(ethene) (addition polymerisation); hydrogenation converts vegetable oil to margarine.", "聚合；氢化制人造奶油"]], "", "Tip: unsaturated hydrocarbons undergo addition reactions; saturated undergo substitution."], ["Alcohols", "醇", [["Functional group –OH. Ethanol \\(\\ce{C2H5OH}\\). Preparation: (1) fermentation of glucose with yeast, 30–35 °C, no oxygen: \\(\\ce{C6H12O6 -> 2C2H5OH + 2CO2}\\); (2) hydration of ethene with steam (\\(\\ce{H3PO4}\\), 300 °C, 60 atm).", "官能团 –OH；制备：发酵；乙烯水合"], ["Combustion: \\(\\ce{C2H5OH + 3O2 -> 2CO2 + 3H2O}\\) (clean blue flame; used as fuel).", "燃烧"], ["Oxidation: ethanol → ethanoic acid using acidified \\(\\ce{K2Cr2O7}\\) (orange → green) or acidified \\(\\ce{KMnO4}\\) (purple → colourless).", "氧化：乙醇 → 乙酸"], ["Dehydration: heated with concentrated \\(\\ce{H2SO4}\\) or passed over hot porcelain chips/\\(\\ce{Al2O3}\\) → ethene + water.", "脱水：生成乙烯"], ["Uses: solvent, fuel, disinfectant, alcoholic drinks, perfume. Methanol is poisonous.", "用途；甲醇有毒"]], "", "Tip: show the fermentation conditions (yeast, 30–35 °C, absence of air)."], ["Carboxylic Acids and Esters", "羧酸与酯", [["Functional group –COOH. Ethanoic acid \\(\\ce{CH3COOH}\\): a weak acid (partially ionises), pH about 3 for 0.1 mol dm⁻³.", "羧酸：–COOH；乙酸是弱酸"], ["Reactions: with reactive metals → salt + \\(\\ce{H2}\\); with bases → salt + water; with carbonates → salt + water + \\(\\ce{CO2}\\) (e.g. \\(\\ce{CH3COOH}\\) + Mg → magnesium ethanoate + \\(\\ce{H2}\\)).", "与金属、碱、碳酸盐反应"], ["Esterification: carboxylic acid + alcohol ⇌ ester + water, with concentrated sulphuric acid as a catalyst, heated under reflux: \\(\\ce{CH3COOH + C2H5OH <=> CH3COOC2H5 + H2O}\\) (ethyl ethanoate).", "酯化反应：浓 H₂SO₄ 催化，回流"], ["Esters: sweet fruity smell; insoluble in water; uses: flavouring, perfumes, solvents. Naming: alcohol part first (ethyl) + acid part (ethanoate).", "酯：果香；命名先醇后酸"], ["Reflux: prevents loss of volatile reactants and products by condensing the vapour and returning it to the flask.", "回流：防止挥发物损失"]], "", "Tip: name the ester by writing the alcohol-derived part first."], ["Interconversion of Carbon Compounds", "碳化合物的互相转化", [["Alkane → alkene: cracking (heat + catalyst) or dehydrogenation. Alkene → alkane: hydrogenation (Ni, 180 °C).", "烷烃 ⇄ 烯烃：裂化 / 氢化"], ["Alkene → alcohol: hydration (steam, \\(\\ce{H3PO4}\\), 300 °C, 60 atm). Alcohol → alkene: dehydration (conc. \\(\\ce{H2SO4}\\) or \\(\\ce{Al2O3}\\)).", "烯烃 ⇄ 醇：水合 / 脱水"], ["Alcohol → carboxylic acid: oxidation (acidified \\(\\ce{KMnO4}\\)/\\(\\ce{K2Cr2O7}\\)).", "醇 → 酸：氧化"], ["Alcohol + carboxylic acid → ester: esterification (conc. \\(\\ce{H2SO4}\\), heat).", "醇 + 酸 → 酯"], ["Flow chart: alkane ⇄ alkene ⇄ alcohol → carboxylic acid → ester. Always give reagents and conditions.", "流程图：写出试剂与条件"]], "", "Tip: learn the flowchart as a single page and write conditions on every arrow."], ["Isomers and IUPAC Naming", "同分异构体与命名", [["Isomers: compounds with the same molecular formula but different structural formulae. \\(\\ce{C4H10}\\): butane and 2-methylpropane. \\(\\ce{C5H12}\\): pentane, 2-methylbutane, 2,2-dimethylpropane.", "同分异构体：分子式相同，结构不同"], ["IUPAC naming rules: (1) select the longest continuous carbon chain; (2) number the chain so that branches or functional groups have the lowest numbers; (3) name branches (methyl, ethyl) in alphabetical order with locants; (4) use di-, tri- for repeated branches.", "命名规则：最长主链、最小编号、支链字母顺序"], ["Alkenes: but-1-ene \\(\\ce{CH2=CH-CH2CH3}\\), but-2-ene \\(\\ce{CH3CH=CHCH3}\\); the double bond gets the lowest number.", "烯烃：双键编号最小"], ["Alcohols: propan-1-ol \\(\\ce{CH3CH2CH2OH}\\), propan-2-ol \\(\\ce{CH3CH(OH)CH3}\\). Haloalkanes: 2-chlorobutane.", "醇：丙-1-醇、丙-2-醇"], ["Isomers have the same chemical properties (same functional group) but different physical properties (boiling points: branched chain is lower).", "异构体：化学性质相似，物理性质不同；支链越多沸点越低"]], "", "Tip: for C₅H₁₂ you must draw all three isomers."], ["Worked Examples: Structure and Naming", "例题：结构与命名", [["Q1: Draw and name all alkenes with formula \\(\\ce{C4H8}\\) (three open-chain): but-1-ene, but-2-ene, 2-methylpropene.", "题1：C₄H₈ 三种链状异构体"], ["Q2: Name \\(\\ce{CH3CH(CH3)CH2CH3}\\): longest chain 4 carbons, methyl on carbon 2 → 2-methylbutane.", "题2：2-甲基丁烷"], ["Q3: Write an equation for complete combustion of propane: \\(\\ce{C3H8 + 5O2 -> 3CO2 + 4H2O}\\).", "题3：丙烷燃烧"], ["Q4: How to distinguish hexane and hexene? Add bromine water and shake: hexene decolourises the brown colour; hexane does not.", "题4：溴水区分"], ["Q5: Name \\(\\ce{CH3COOCH3}\\): methyl ethanoate (alcohol part methyl; acid part ethanoate).", "题5：乙酸甲酯"]], "", "Tip: write structural formulae with every bond when asked to 'draw'."], ["Common Mistakes", "常见错误", [["Mistake: numbering from the wrong end of the chain; naming a branch as the main chain.", "错误：编号方向错；主链选错"], ["Mistake: writing the ester name in the wrong order (ethanoic ethyl).", "错误：酯名顺序"]], "", ""], ["Uji Diri", "自测", [["S: General formula of the alkene homologous series? J: \\(\\ce{C_nH_{2n}}\\).", "问：烯烃通式？答：CₙH₂ₙ"], ["S: What is observed when ethene is bubbled into bromine water? J: The brown colour is decolourised.", "问：乙烯通入溴水？答：褐色褪去"], ["S: Name the product of ethanol and ethanoic acid with conc. \\(\\ce{H2SO4}\\). J: Ethyl ethanoate (an ester) and water.", "问：乙醇与乙酸（浓 H₂SO₄）？答：乙酸乙酯和水"]], "", ""]], "kim|T5-3": [["Exothermic and Endothermic Reactions", "放热与吸热反应", [["Thermochemistry studies the heat changes that accompany chemical reactions.", "热化学研究化学反应中的热变化"], ["Exothermic reaction: releases heat to the surroundings; the temperature of the surroundings rises; \\(\\Delta H\\) is negative. Examples: combustion, neutralisation, respiration, reaction of metal with acid, dissolving anhydrous \\(\\ce{CuSO4}\\) in water.", "放热反应：向周围释放热量，周围温度上升，ΔH 为负"], ["Endothermic reaction: absorbs heat from the surroundings; the temperature of the surroundings falls; \\(\\Delta H\\) is positive. Examples: photosynthesis, thermal decomposition of \\(\\ce{CaCO3}\\), dissolving \\(\\ce{NH4Cl}\\) in water, reaction of \\(\\ce{Ba(OH)2}\\) with \\(\\ce{NH4Cl}\\).", "吸热反应：吸收热量，周围温度下降，ΔH 为正"], ["Heat change is caused by bond breaking (absorbs energy) and bond forming (releases energy). If energy released on forming bonds is greater than the energy absorbed on breaking bonds, the reaction is exothermic.", "键断裂吸能，键形成放能"], ["Heat of reaction \\(\\Delta H\\): the heat change when the reaction occurs according to the mole ratio in the balanced equation (unit kJ mol⁻¹).", "反应热 ΔH：按方程式计量比反应时的热变化"]], "", "Tip: link the temperature change to the type of reaction — 'temperature rises → exothermic'."], ["Energy Level Diagrams and Activation Energy", "能级图与活化能", [["Exothermic: the products have lower energy than the reactants; \\(\\Delta H=\\) energy of products − energy of reactants < 0.", "放热：生成物能量低于反应物"], ["Endothermic: the products have higher energy than the reactants; \\(\\Delta H>0\\).", "吸热：生成物能量高于反应物"], ["Activation energy \\(E_a\\): the minimum energy that colliding particles must have to react; shown as the 'hill' from the reactants up to the peak of the curve.", "活化能：碰撞粒子发生反应所需最小能量"], ["A catalyst provides an alternative pathway with lower \\(E_a\\); it does not change \\(\\Delta H\\).", "催化剂降低 Ea，不改变 ΔH"], ["Label the diagram: axis 'Energy', reactants, products, \\(E_a\\) arrow, \\(\\Delta H\\) arrow, with the sign and the equation.", "作图要标：能量轴、反应物、生成物、Ea、ΔH"]], "", "Tip: draw ΔH from the energy of the reactants to the energy of the products, with the arrowhead at the products."], ["Heat of Reaction and Calculation Method", "反应热与计算方法", [["Heat released or absorbed: \\(Q=mc\\theta\\) (m = mass of solution in g, c = 4.2 J g⁻¹ °C⁻¹, θ = temperature change). Assume the density of the solution = 1 g cm⁻³.", "Q = mcθ；溶液密度按 1 g/cm³"], ["Number of moles: \\(n=MV/1000\\) (M in mol dm⁻³, V in cm³).", "物质的量 n = MV/1000"], ["\\(\\Delta H=-\\dfrac{Q}{n}\\) for an exothermic reaction (convert J to kJ) and \\(+\\dfrac{Q}{n}\\) for an endothermic one.", "ΔH = ∓Q/n（放热为负）"], ["Use a polystyrene cup with a lid to reduce heat loss; stir; record the highest (or lowest) temperature.", "用保温杯加盖、搅拌，记录最高/最低温度"], ["Simplifying assumptions: no heat is lost to the surroundings; the specific heat capacity of the solution = that of water.", "假设：无热损失；溶液比热容同水"]], "", "Tip: write the three steps clearly: Q → n → ΔH, with units kJ mol⁻¹."], ["Heat of Precipitation", "沉淀热", [["Heat of precipitation: the heat change when 1 mole of a precipitate is formed from its ions in aqueous solution. Example: \\(\\ce{Ag+(aq) + Cl-(aq) -> AgCl(s)}\\), \\(\\Delta H=-65\\) kJ mol⁻¹.", "沉淀热：由水溶液中的离子生成 1 mol 沉淀的热变化"], ["Experiment: mix 25 cm³ of 0.5 mol dm⁻³ \\(\\ce{AgNO3}\\) with 25 cm³ of 0.5 mol dm⁻³ \\(\\ce{NaCl}\\) in a polystyrene cup; record the initial and highest temperature.", "实验：混合两种溶液并测温"], ["Q: Temperature rises by 3.9 °C. \\(Q=50\\times4.2\\times3.9=819\\) J; \\(n=\\dfrac{0.5\\times25}{1000}=0.0125\\) mol.", "题：θ = 3.9 °C：Q = 819 J；n = 0.0125 mol"], ["\\(\\Delta H=-\\dfrac{819}{0.0125}=-65\\,520\\) J mol⁻¹ \\(\\approx-65.5\\) kJ mol⁻¹.", "ΔH ≈ −65.5 kJ/mol"], ["Ionic equation and energy level diagram are often asked together.", "常与离子方程式和能级图一起考"]], "", "Tip: always divide by the number of moles of the PRECIPITATE formed."], ["Heat of Displacement", "置换热", [["Heat of displacement: the heat change when 1 mole of a metal is displaced from its salt solution by a more reactive metal.", "置换热：较活泼金属置换出 1 mol 金属的热变化"], ["Example: \\(\\ce{Zn(s) + Cu^2+(aq) -> Zn^2+(aq) + Cu(s)}\\), \\(\\Delta H=-210\\) kJ mol⁻¹.", "例：Zn + Cu²⁺，ΔH ≈ −210 kJ/mol"], ["Experiment: add excess zinc powder to 50 cm³ of 0.5 mol dm⁻³ \\(\\ce{CuSO4}\\) and stir; zinc is in excess so that all \\(\\ce{Cu^2+}\\) ions react.", "实验：锌粉过量，使 Cu²⁺ 全部反应"], ["Q: Temperature rises by 25 °C: \\(Q=50\\times4.2\\times25=5250\\) J; \\(n(\\ce{Cu^2+})=\\dfrac{0.5\\times50}{1000}=0.025\\) mol; \\(\\Delta H=-\\dfrac{5250}{0.025}=-210\\,000\\) J mol⁻¹ = −210 kJ mol⁻¹.", "题：θ = 25 °C → ΔH = −210 kJ/mol"], ["Observations: blue solution fades; reddish-brown solid deposited; temperature rises.", "现象：蓝色变浅，红棕色固体析出，温度上升"]], "", "Tip: the limiting reagent is the salt solution; use its moles in the calculation."], ["Heat of Neutralisation", "中和热", [["Heat of neutralisation: the heat change when 1 mole of water is formed from the reaction of an acid with an alkali. Strong acid + strong alkali: \\(\\ce{H+ + OH- -> H2O}\\), \\(\\Delta H\\approx-57\\) kJ mol⁻¹.", "中和热：酸碱反应生成 1 mol 水的热变化；强酸强碱约 −57 kJ/mol"], ["Q: 50 cm³ of 1.0 mol dm⁻³ \\(\\ce{HCl}\\) + 50 cm³ of 1.0 mol dm⁻³ \\(\\ce{NaOH}\\); temperature rises 6.8 °C. \\(Q=100\\times4.2\\times6.8=2856\\) J; \\(n(\\ce{H2O})=0.05\\) mol; \\(\\Delta H=-\\dfrac{2856}{0.05}=-57\\,120\\) J mol⁻¹ \\(\\approx-57.1\\) kJ mol⁻¹.", "题：θ = 6.8 °C → ΔH ≈ −57.1 kJ/mol"], ["Weak acid or weak alkali (e.g. ethanoic acid + NaOH): the heat of neutralisation is less exothermic (about −55 kJ mol⁻¹ or lower in magnitude) because part of the heat released is used to ionise the weak acid completely.", "弱酸/弱碱：中和热较小，因为部分热量用于使弱酸完全电离"], ["Examples: \\(\\ce{HCl}\\) / \\(\\ce{HNO3}\\) with \\(\\ce{NaOH}\\) ≈ −57 kJ mol⁻¹; \\(\\ce{CH3COOH}\\) with \\(\\ce{NaOH}\\) smaller.", "例：强酸 ≈ −57；乙酸较小"], ["For \\(\\ce{H2SO4}\\) (diprotic) the moles of water formed = 2 × moles of acid.", "硫酸为二元酸，水的物质的量 = 2 × 酸的物质的量"]], "", "Tip: 'Weak acid ionises only partially; heat is absorbed to ionise it completely, so ΔH is lower.'"], ["Heat of Combustion", "燃烧热", [["Heat of combustion: the heat released when 1 mole of a substance is burnt completely in excess oxygen. Example: \\(\\ce{CH3CH2OH + 3O2 -> 2CO2 + 3H2O}\\), \\(\\Delta H=-1367\\) kJ mol⁻¹.", "燃烧热：1 mol 物质在过量氧气中完全燃烧放出的热量"], ["Alcohols: methanol −726, ethanol −1367, propan-1-ol −2021, butan-1-ol −2676 kJ mol⁻¹ — the heat of combustion increases as the number of carbon atoms (and \\(\\ce{CO2}\\), \\(\\ce{H2O}\\) formed) increases.", "醇的燃烧热随碳原子数增加而增大"], ["Experiment: burn an alcohol in a spirit lamp under a copper can containing 200 cm³ of water; measure the temperature rise and the mass of alcohol burnt.", "实验：酒精灯加热铜罐中的水，测温升与酒精质量"], ["Q: 0.46 g ethanol (\\(M_r=46\\), 0.010 mol) raises 200 g water by 13.3 °C: \\(Q=200\\times4.2\\times13.3=11\\,172\\) J; \\(\\Delta H=-\\dfrac{11.17}{0.010}\\approx-1117\\) kJ mol⁻¹.", "题：测得约 −1117 kJ/mol"], ["The experimental value is lower than the theoretical (−1367) because of heat loss to the surroundings, incomplete combustion and heat absorbed by the can. Improve: use a windshield, a lid, polish the can, stir the water.", "实验值偏小：热损失、不完全燃烧；改进：防风罩等"]], "", "Tip: the common error answer is 'heat loss' — always add one improvement."], ["Fuel Value and Applications of Energy Changes", "燃料值与热变化的应用", [["Fuel value = heat released per gram: \\(\\dfrac{\\Delta H}{M_r}\\) (kJ g⁻¹). Ethanol: \\(\\dfrac{1367}{46}=29.7\\) kJ g⁻¹.", "燃料值 = 每克燃烧放热"], ["A good fuel: high fuel value, burns cleanly, low cost, easy to store/transport, little pollution. Examples: natural gas, petrol, hydrogen, biofuels.", "好燃料：燃料值高、清洁、便宜、易储运"], ["Hot packs use exothermic reactions (e.g. dissolving \\(\\ce{CaCl2}\\) or \\(\\ce{MgSO4}\\) in water); instant cold packs use endothermic reactions (dissolving \\(\\ce{NH4NO3}\\)).", "热敷袋：放热；冷敷袋：吸热"], ["Self-heating food cans and cooking by combustion are everyday uses of exothermic reactions.", "日常应用：自热食品、燃烧加热"], ["Energy sources are limited; use them efficiently and develop renewable ones (solar, biomass, hydro).", "能源有限，应提高效率并发展再生能源"]], "", "Tip: for 'compare two fuels' questions, give the fuel value numbers and a comment on pollution."], ["Common Mistakes", "常见错误", [["Mistake: forgetting the negative sign for exothermic ΔH.", "错误：放热 ΔH 忘记写负号"], ["Mistake: using the mass of solution only from one reactant; the total volume is used in \\(Q=mc\\theta\\).", "错误：m 要用混合后总质量"]], "", ""], ["Uji Diri", "自测", [["S: What is the heat of neutralisation of a strong acid and a strong alkali? J: About −57 kJ mol⁻¹.", "问：强酸强碱的中和热？答：约 −57 kJ/mol"], ["S: Why is the heat of neutralisation of ethanoic acid with NaOH less exothermic? J: Part of the heat is used to ionise the weak acid completely.", "问：乙酸中和热为何较小？答：部分热量用于使乙酸电离"], ["S: What does a catalyst do to the activation energy and ΔH? J: It lowers the activation energy; ΔH is unchanged.", "问：催化剂对 Ea、ΔH 的影响？答：降低 Ea，ΔH 不变"]], "", ""]], "kim|T5-4": [["Polymers: Monomer and Polymerisation", "聚合物：单体与聚合反应", [["A polymer is a long-chain molecule made of many repeating units called monomers joined by covalent bonds; polymerisation is the process of joining the monomers.", "聚合物：许多单体重复连接而成的长链分子"], ["Natural polymers: starch and cellulose (monomer glucose), proteins (monomer amino acids), natural rubber (monomer isoprene), DNA, fats/oils are not polymers.", "天然聚合物：淀粉、纤维素、蛋白质、天然橡胶"], ["Synthetic polymers: polyethene, polypropene, polyvinyl chloride (PVC), polystyrene, nylon, polyester, perspex (poly(methyl methacrylate)), bakelite.", "合成聚合物：聚乙烯、聚丙烯、PVC、聚苯乙烯、尼龙等"], ["Properties: strong, light, not corroded, electrical insulators, easily moulded, cheap — but most are non-biodegradable.", "性质：强、轻、耐腐蚀、绝缘、易塑形；但多不可降解"], ["Addition polymerisation: unsaturated monomers (with C=C) join with no other product; condensation polymerisation: monomers join with the loss of small molecules such as water.", "加聚反应与缩聚反应"]], "", "Tip: Define a polymer with the words 'many repeating units (monomers)'."], ["Addition Polymers: Equations and Uses", "加聚物：方程式与用途", [["Ethene → poly(ethene): \\(n\\,\\ce{CH2=CH2 -> [-CH2-CH2-]_n}\\). Uses: plastic bags, bottles, toys, wire insulation.", "乙烯 → 聚乙烯：塑料袋、瓶子、玩具"], ["Propene → poly(propene): used in ropes, food containers, car parts, carpets.", "丙烯 → 聚丙烯：绳、食品盒、汽车零件"], ["Chloroethene (vinyl chloride) → PVC: pipes, floor tiles, electric cable insulation, raincoats.", "氯乙烯 → PVC：水管、地砖、电缆"], ["Styrene → polystyrene: foam packaging, disposable cups, insulation.", "苯乙烯 → 聚苯乙烯：泡沫包装、杯子"], ["How to draw: the double bond opens and the two carbon atoms become part of the main chain; side groups stay attached; show the repeating unit in square brackets with subscript n.", "画法：双键打开成主链，侧基保留，用方括号和 n 表示"]], "", "Tip: name the monomer from the polymer by finding the repeating unit and adding the double bond back."], ["Condensation Polymers (Nylon and Polyester)", "缩聚物：尼龙与聚酯", [["Nylon: formed from a diamine and a dicarboxylic acid; each link forms an amide bond and releases water.", "尼龙：二元胺 + 二元酸，形成酰胺键并释放水"], ["Polyester (e.g. PET): formed from a diol and a dicarboxylic acid; each link forms an ester bond and releases water. Uses: bottles, clothing fibres.", "聚酯（PET）：二元醇 + 二元酸；酯键；用于瓶子、衣料"], ["Both are used as fibres in clothes, ropes, fishing lines, parachutes, carpets.", "用途：衣物纤维、绳、降落伞"], ["Natural condensation polymers: proteins (amide/peptide bond) and carbohydrates.", "天然缩聚物：蛋白质、多糖"]], "", "Tip: SPM questions on this are usually descriptive; remember 'small molecule (water) is released'."], ["Natural Rubber: Latex, Isoprene and Coagulation", "天然橡胶：胶乳、异戊二烯与凝固", [["Natural rubber is a natural polymer of isoprene (2-methylbuta-1,3-diene), \\(\\ce{CH2=C(CH3)-CH=CH2}\\); latex from rubber trees is a colloid of rubber particles in water.", "天然橡胶是异戊二烯的聚合物；胶乳是橡胶粒子在水中的胶体"], ["The rubber particles are surrounded by a layer of protein with negative charges, so the particles repel each other and the latex does not coagulate.", "橡胶粒子外包带负电的蛋白质膜，相互排斥"], ["Coagulation: adding an acid (methanoic acid or ethanoic acid) — the \\(\\ce{H+}\\) ions neutralise the negative charges on the protein membrane; the rubber particles collide, merge and coagulate.", "凝固：加酸，H⁺ 中和负电荷，粒子聚结凝固"], ["Preventing coagulation: add ammonia solution (alkali); the \\(\\ce{OH-}\\) ions neutralise the \\(\\ce{H+}\\) produced by bacteria, so the latex stays liquid.", "防止凝固：加氨水（碱），中和细菌产生的 H⁺"], ["Natural rubber properties: elastic, soft and sticky; weak when heated; easily oxidised; decomposes with time.", "性质：有弹性、软、黏；受热易软化、易氧化"]], "", "Tip: acid → coagulates; alkali (ammonia) → prevents coagulation. Explain with the \\(\\ce{H+}\\) / \\(\\ce{OH-}\\) ions."], ["Vulcanisation of Rubber", "橡胶硫化", [["Vulcanisation: heating natural rubber with sulphur. The sulphur atoms form cross-links (–S–S– bridges) between the rubber polymer chains.", "硫化：橡胶与硫共热，硫原子在聚合物链之间形成交联"], ["Vulcanised rubber is harder, stronger, more elastic, more resistant to heat, abrasion and chemicals and less easily oxidised than natural rubber.", "硫化橡胶更硬、更强、更有弹性、更耐热耐磨"], ["The cross-links prevent the chains from sliding past each other easily, so the rubber returns to its original shape after being stretched.", "交联防止链滑动，拉伸后可恢复原状"], ["Experiment: compare the elasticity of vulcanised and unvulcanised rubber strips by hanging a mass and measuring the extension and recovery.", "实验：比较弹性：挂重物测伸长与恢复"], ["Uses: tyres, shoe soles, conveyor belts, rubber gloves, hoses.", "用途：轮胎、鞋底、传送带"]], "", "Tip: mention 'sulphur atoms' and 'cross-links between polymer chains' to earn both marks."], ["Synthetic Rubber", "合成橡胶", [["Synthetic rubbers are made from petroleum products by addition polymerisation: neoprene (chloroprene), styrene-butadiene rubber (SBR), nitrile rubber.", "合成橡胶：由石油产品加聚而成：氯丁、丁苯、丁腈"], ["Neoprene: resistant to oil, heat and chemicals — used in hoses, gaskets, diving suits.", "氯丁橡胶：耐油、耐热、耐化学品"], ["SBR: abrasion resistant — used in tyres, shoe soles, conveyor belts.", "丁苯橡胶：耐磨：轮胎、鞋底"], ["Nitrile rubber: oil-resistant — used for gloves and fuel hoses.", "丁腈橡胶：耐油：手套、油管"], ["Natural vs synthetic: natural rubber is more elastic and cheaper to tap but weaker to heat and oil; synthetic rubber is more resistant to heat, oil and chemicals and its properties can be designed.", "天然橡胶弹性好；合成橡胶更耐热耐油，性能可设计"]], "", "Tip: when comparing, give one advantage and one limitation for each type."], ["Polymers and the Environment", "聚合物与环境", [["Most synthetic polymers are non-biodegradable: they accumulate in landfills and oceans, harm wildlife and block drains.", "合成聚合物多不可降解：堆积于填埋场和海洋，伤害动物"], ["Burning plastics releases harmful gases: \\(\\ce{CO2}\\), \\(\\ce{CO}\\), \\(\\ce{HCl}\\) (from PVC), dioxins — causing air pollution and acid rain.", "燃烧塑料产生 CO₂、CO、HCl 等有害气体"], ["Solutions: the 3Rs (reduce, reuse, recycle), biodegradable plastics from starch or cellulose, proper waste segregation, bans on single-use plastics.", "解决办法：3R、可降解塑料、分类、禁用一次性塑料"], ["Pyrolysis and recycling can convert plastic waste into fuel or new products.", "热解和回收可再利用塑料"], ["Rubber waste (e.g. tyres) is recycled as road surfacing, playground flooring and crumb rubber.", "废轮胎可回收用于铺路、操场地垫"]], "", "Tip: a good answer pairs a problem with a matching solution."], ["Common Mistakes", "常见错误", [["Mistake: writing the polymer without the square brackets and subscript n.", "错误：聚合物没写方括号和 n"], ["Mistake: saying that acid prevents coagulation (it causes it); ammonia prevents it.", "错误：酸防止凝固（应为凝固）"]], "", ""], ["Uji Diri", "自测", [["S: Name the monomer of natural rubber. J: Isoprene (2-methylbuta-1,3-diene).", "问：天然橡胶的单体？答：异戊二烯"], ["S: What is vulcanisation? J: Heating rubber with sulphur to form cross-links between polymer chains.", "问：硫化？答：橡胶与硫共热形成交联"], ["S: Why is ammonia added to latex? J: To neutralise the acid produced by bacteria and prevent coagulation.", "问：胶乳中为何加氨水？答：中和细菌产生的酸，防止凝固"]], "", ""]], "kim|T5-5": [["Cleaning Agents: Soap and Saponification", "清洁剂：肥皂与皂化反应", [["Soap is a sodium or potassium salt of a long-chain fatty acid, e.g. sodium stearate \\(\\ce{C17H35COONa}\\), sodium palmitate \\(\\ce{C15H31COONa}\\).", "肥皂：长链脂肪酸的钠盐或钾盐"], ["Saponification: oil/fat + concentrated alkali (NaOH or KOH) → soap + glycerol. Triglyceride + 3NaOH → 3 sodium fatty acid salt + glycerol.", "皂化反应：油脂 + 浓碱 → 肥皂 + 甘油"], ["Preparation: boil palm oil with NaOH solution for about 10 minutes; add sodium chloride (salting out) so that the soap becomes insoluble and floats; filter and wash the soap.", "制法：棕榈油 + NaOH 煮沸；加食盐盐析；过滤洗涤"], ["Soap made with NaOH is hard; soap made with KOH is soft.", "NaOH 制硬皂；KOH 制软皂"]], "", "Tip: write the reactants and both products: soap and glycerol."], ["Cleaning Action and Micelles", "去污原理", [["Soap anion has two parts: a hydrophilic head (\\(\\ce{-COO-}\\), dissolves in water) and a hydrophobic tail (hydrocarbon chain, dissolves in oil/grease).", "肥皂阴离子：亲水头 + 疏水尾"], ["Soap reduces the surface tension of water, so the water wets the cloth better.", "降低水的表面张力，使水更易润湿"], ["The hydrophobic tails dissolve in the grease while the hydrophilic heads stay in water; with agitation the grease is lifted off, broken into small droplets and surrounded by soap anions (emulsion/micelles).", "疏水尾溶入油污，亲水头留在水中；搅动后油污分散成小滴"], ["The repulsion between negatively charged droplets keeps them suspended; rinsing washes them away.", "带同种电荷的液滴相互排斥，被冲走"]], "", "Tip: use the key words 'hydrophilic head', 'hydrophobic tail', 'emulsion', 'surface tension'."], ["Soaps vs Detergents; Hard Water", "肥皂与洗涤剂；硬水", [["Hard water contains \\(\\ce{Ca^2+}\\) and \\(\\ce{Mg^2+}\\) ions. Soap reacts with them to form insoluble scum: \\(\\ce{2C17H35COO- + Ca^2+ -> (C17H35COO)2Ca}\\) — soap is wasted and cleans poorly.", "硬水含 Ca²⁺、Mg²⁺：与肥皂生成不溶的浮渣"], ["Detergents (e.g. sodium alkylbenzene sulphonate) do not form scum in hard water because their calcium/magnesium salts are soluble.", "洗涤剂在硬水中不生浮渣"], ["Detergent additives: enzymes (remove protein/fat stains), bleach (removes coloured stains), brighteners, builders (soften water), perfumes, foaming agents.", "洗涤剂添加物：酶、漂白剂、增白剂、软水剂"], ["Environmental effects: phosphate builders cause eutrophication; non-biodegradable detergents persist in water. Choose biodegradable detergents and use correct amounts.", "环境问题：磷酸盐造成富营养化；应选可降解洗涤剂"], ["Soap is biodegradable and made from natural oils/fats; detergents are synthetic from petroleum, can be used in acidic or hard water.", "肥皂可降解；洗涤剂合成、可用于酸性/硬水"]], "", "Tip: for 'Why is detergent better in hard water?' write: no scum, because its salt with Ca²⁺ is soluble."], ["Oils and Fats", "油和脂肪", [["Oils (liquid) and fats (solid) are esters of glycerol and fatty acids (triglycerides); sources: plants (palm, coconut, olive) and animals (butter, lard).", "油脂：甘油三酯"], ["Saturated fatty acids have only C–C single bonds (e.g. palmitic acid \\(\\ce{C15H31COOH}\\), stearic acid \\(\\ce{C17H35COOH}\\)); unsaturated fatty acids have one or more C=C double bonds (oleic acid \\(\\ce{C17H33COOH}\\)).", "饱和脂肪酸：只有单键；不饱和：含 C=C"], ["Animal fats are rich in saturated fats (solid, raise cholesterol); vegetable oils are rich in unsaturated fats (liquid, healthier) — omega-3/6 fatty acids are essential.", "动物脂肪多饱和；植物油多不饱和"], ["Test for unsaturation: shake with bromine water — the brown colour is decolourised for unsaturated oil.", "不饱和测试：溴水褪色"], ["Hydrogenation: unsaturated oil + \\(\\ce{H2}\\) with nickel catalyst at about 180 °C → saturated fat (margarine); increases melting point and shelf life.", "氢化：Ni 催化，约 180 °C，用于制人造奶油"]], "", "Tip: 'Ni catalyst + 180 °C + hydrogen' are standard hydrogenation conditions."], ["Palm Oil and Its Importance", "棕榈油及其重要性", [["Palm oil is extracted from the fruit of the oil palm: sterilise the fruit bunches with steam, strip the fruits, digest/mash, press to obtain crude palm oil, then purify.", "棕榈油提取：蒸煮 → 脱果 → 蒸煮捣碎 → 压榨 → 精炼"], ["Uses: cooking oil, margarine, soap, cosmetics, biodiesel, candles.", "用途：食用油、人造奶油、肥皂、化妆品、生物柴油"], ["Malaysia is one of the world's largest palm-oil producers; it contributes significantly to the economy and rural jobs.", "马来西亚是主要棕榈油生产国"], ["Concerns: deforestation, loss of habitat, saturated fat content; solutions: sustainable palm oil (MSPO certification), replanting rather than clearing forest.", "问题：毁林、饱和脂肪；解决：可持续认证"], ["Palm oil is semi-solid at room temperature and has long shelf life because it contains saturated fatty acids.", "棕榈油含饱和脂肪酸，室温半固态"]], "", "Tip: always give both a benefit and an environmental issue when asked to evaluate palm oil."], ["Food Additives", "食品添加剂", [["Preservatives slow food spoilage: sodium benzoate, sodium nitrite, sulphur dioxide, salt, sugar, vinegar.", "防腐剂：苯甲酸钠、亚硝酸钠、盐、糖、醋"], ["Antioxidants prevent oxidation of food: ascorbic acid (vitamin C), BHT, vitamin E.", "抗氧化剂：维生素 C、BHT"], ["Flavourings: monosodium glutamate (MSG), aspartame (artificial sweetener), vanilla.", "调味剂：味精、阿斯巴甜"], ["Stabilisers and thickeners: gelatine, pectin, starch, xanthan gum; emulsifier: lecithin keeps oil and water mixed.", "稳定剂/增稠剂：明胶、果胶；乳化剂：卵磷脂"], ["Dyes: tartrazine (yellow), sunset yellow, carmoisine — some may cause allergies or hyperactivity; read food labels and choose natural options where possible.", "色素：柠檬黄等；可能引起过敏"]], "", "Tip: for each type of additive, learn one example and its function."], ["Medicines and Cosmetics", "药物与化妆品", [["Traditional medicine uses natural sources (herbs, plants); modern medicine uses chemicals tested through clinical trials.", "传统药物：草药；现代药物：经临床试验的化学药物"], ["Analgesics relieve pain: aspirin, paracetamol, codeine. Antibiotics kill or stop bacteria: penicillin, streptomycin (finish the full course to avoid antibiotic resistance).", "止痛药：阿司匹林、扑热息痛；抗生素：青霉素（需完成疗程）"], ["Psychotherapeutic medicines treat mental conditions: stimulants, antidepressants, antipsychotics; they must be taken only with a doctor's prescription.", "精神类药物：必须遵医嘱"], ["Cosmetics: cleansers, moisturisers, lipsticks, sunscreens and perfumes; ingredients include water, oils, emulsifiers, preservatives, colourants and fragrances.", "化妆品：成分含水、油、乳化剂、防腐剂、色素、香料"], ["Side effects: allergy, skin irritation, harmful metals (e.g. mercury, lead) — buy products approved by the authorities and do a patch test first.", "副作用：过敏、含重金属；选正规产品并先试用"]], "", "Tip: always add 'under doctor's supervision' when discussing medicines."], ["Nanotechnology and Green Technology in Industry", "纳米技术与绿色技术", [["Nanotechnology works with particles of size about 1–100 nm; nanoparticles have a large surface-area-to-volume ratio and properties different from bulk material.", "纳米技术：1–100 nm；表面积/体积大，性质特殊"], ["Applications: nano silver in antibacterial clothing and wound dressings, \\(\\ce{TiO2}\\) and \\(\\ce{ZnO}\\) in sunscreen, nano-coatings (self-cleaning glass), carbon nanotubes in strong light materials, drug delivery, water filtration.", "应用：纳米银抗菌、防晒霜、自洁玻璃、纳米碳管、药物递送"], ["Concerns: effects of nanoparticles on health and environment are not fully known.", "忧虑：对健康和环境的影响尚未完全清楚"], ["Green technology in industrial waste management: reduce, reuse, recycle; neutralise acidic waste with lime; remove \\(\\ce{SO2}\\) with scrubbers; catalytic converters; effluent treatment plants; bioremediation using microorganisms.", "工业废物管理：3R、石灰中和、洗涤塔、催化转化器、废水处理、生物修复"], ["Principles of green chemistry: prevent waste, use safer chemicals, use renewable raw materials and save energy.", "绿色化学：防止废物、使用更安全、可再生原料、节能"]], "", "Tip: link each technology to a problem it solves."], ["Common Mistakes", "常见错误", [["Mistake: saying soap is a detergent; soap is made from natural fats/oils, detergents are synthetic.", "错误：把肥皂说成洗涤剂"], ["Mistake: forgetting the conditions (nickel, 180 °C) in hydrogenation.", "错误：漏写氢化条件"]], "", ""], ["Uji Diri", "自测", [["S: What is formed when oil is boiled with NaOH? J: Soap and glycerol (saponification).", "问：油与 NaOH 煮沸得到？答：肥皂和甘油"], ["S: Why does soap form scum in hard water? J: Ca²⁺ and Mg²⁺ ions react with soap anions to form insoluble salts.", "问：肥皂为何在硬水产生浮渣？答：与 Ca²⁺/Mg²⁺ 生成不溶盐"], ["S: Give two examples of antibiotics and one precaution. J: Penicillin and streptomycin; complete the full course.", "问：抗生素例子和注意？答：青霉素、链霉素；完成疗程"]], "", ""]]};
